it.(*Group).Start.func1()\n            k8s.io/apimachinery/pkg/util/wait/wait.go:72 +0x82\n      \n      Goroutine 650 (running) created at:\n        k8s.io/kubernetes/pkg/scheduler.(*Scheduler).Run()\n            k8s.io/kubernetes/pkg/scheduler/scheduler.go:538 +0x21e\n        k8s.io/kubernetes/cmd/kube-scheduler/app.Run.func6()\n            k8s.io/kubernetes/cmd/kube-scheduler/app/server.go:317 +0x15e\n        k8s.io/client-go/tools/leaderelection.(*LeaderElector).Run.gowrap2()\n            k8s.io/client-go/tools/leaderelection/leaderelection.go:220 +0x46\n      \n      Goroutine 469 (running) created at:\n        k8s.io/apimachinery/pkg/util/wait.(*Group).Start()\n            k8s.io/apimachinery/pkg/util/wait/wait.go:70 +0xdc\n        k8s.io/client-go/tools/cache.(*sharedProcessor).run.func1()\n            k8s.io/client-go/tools/cache/shared_informer.go:1135 +0x2aa\n        k8s.io/client-go/tools/cache.(*sharedProcessor).run()\n            k8s.io/client-go/tools/cache/shared_informer.go:1140 +0x4b\n        k8s.io/client-go/tools/cache.(*sharedProcessor).run-fm()\n            <autogenerated>:1 +0x3e\n        k8s.io/client-go/tools/cache.(*sharedIndexInformer).RunWithContext.(*Group).StartWithContext.func5()\n            k8s.io/apimachinery/pkg/util/wait/wait.go:63 +0x46\n        k8s.io/apimachinery/pkg/util/wait.(*Group).Start.func1()\n            k8s.io/apimachinery/pkg/util/wait/wait.go:72 +0x82\nIn [ReportAfterSuite] at: k8s.io/kubernetes/test/e2e/invariants/logcheck/logcheck.go:218 @ 05/13/26 15:39:21.882\n< Exit [ReportAfterSuite] TOP-LEVEL - k8s.io/kubernetes/test/e2e/invariants/logcheck/logcheck.go:179 @ 05/13/26 15:39:21.882 (502ms)\n```\n</details>\n\n### Since when has it been failing?\n\n13 May 2026 12:30 UTC (less than 12 hours ago)\n\n### Testgrid link\n\nhttps://testgrid.k8s.io/sig-node-dynamic-resource-allocation#pull-kubernetes-kind-dra-all\n\n### Reason for failure (if possible)\n\nChecking the revisions of the master branch used in each test, the failure looks to have been caused in 7a4ea9be3339a1eef25123889c82d5b9f3d8a7b1...eaa04458b241800ae37e07ad051415a2f2309a17 by one of these PRs which touch the scheduler:\n- #135756\n- #135160\n\ncc @vshkrabkov @KunWuLuan\n\n### Anything else we need to know?\n\n_No response_\n\n### Relevant SIG(s)\n\n/sig scheduling", "role": "body"}, {"id": "c1", "author": "k8s-ci-robot", "timestamp": "2026-05-13T19:04:42Z", "body": "This issue is currently awaiting triage.\n\nIf a SIG or subproject determines this is a relevant issue, they will accept it by applying the `triage/accepted` label and provide further guidance.\n\nThe `triage/accepted` label can be added by org members by writing `/triage accepted` in a comment.\n\n\n<details>\n\nInstructions for interacting with me using PR comments are available [here](https://git.k8s.io/community/contributors/guide/pull-requests.md).  If you have questions or suggestions related to my behavior, please file an issue against the [kubernetes-sigs/prow](https://github.com/kubernetes-sigs/prow/issues/new?title=Prow%20issue:) repository.\n</details>", "role": "comment"}, {"id": "c2", "author": "nojnhuh", "timestamp": "2026-05-14T16:18:55Z", "body": "Like @mm4tt pointed out in https://github.com/kubernetes/kubernetes/pull/139049#issuecomment-4450064928, it looks like #139057 did fix the issue, based on this run for an unrelated PR: https://prow.k8s.io/view/gs/kubernetes-ci-logs/pr-logs/pull/139066/pull-kubernetes-kind-dra-all/2054947764655099904. I'll keep an eye on the job today to make sure it stays fixed.", "role": "comment"}, {"id": "c3", "author": "pohly", "timestamp": "2026-05-15T08:07:10Z", "body": "I first noticed this in ci-integration-race (https://github.com/kubernetes/kubernetes/issues/132025#issuecomment-4441785196) where https://github.com/kubernetes/kubernetes/pull/139057 seems to have fixed it.\n\nLet's keep this issue here open just to be sure, but it's probably okay again now.", "role": "comment"}, {"id": "c4", "author": "nojnhuh", "timestamp": "2026-05-15T16:06:41Z", "body": "The job has passed a few times across several different PRs. I think it's safe to say this is fixed.\n\n/close", "role": "comment"}, {"id": "c5", "author": "k8s-ci-robot", "timestamp": "2026-05-15T16:06:48Z", "body": "@nojnhuh: Closing this issue.\n\n<details>\n\nIn response to [this](https://github.com/kubernetes/kubernetes/issues/139044#issuecomment-4461354911):\n\n>The job has passed a few times across several different PRs. I think it's safe to say this is fixed.\n>\n>/close\n\n\nInstructions for interacting with me using PR comments are available [here](https://git.k8s.io/community/contributors/guide/pull-requests.md).  If you have questions or suggestions related to my behavior, please file an issue against the [kubernetes-sigs/prow](https://github.com/kubernetes-sigs/prow/issues/new?title=Prow%20issue:) repository.\n</details>", "role": "comment"}], "qa_pairs": [{"qid": "kubernetes/kubernetes/issue/139044#1", "question": "In kubernetes/kubernetes, the `pull-kubernetes-kind-dra-all` presubmit job is failing, while `ci-kind-dra-all` has not shown it yet. This does not appear related to any particular PR; the same failure was seen in at least 5 different PRs, including https://github.com/kubernetes/kubernetes/pull/137664, which makes no changes. The failing test is `Kubernetes e2e suite: [ReportAfterSuite] [sig-testing] Log Check`. From the full failure log at https://prow.k8s.io/view/gs/kubernetes-ci-logs/pr-logs/pull/137664/pull-kubernetes-kind-dra-all/2054577577367965696, the log check detects data races in `kube-system/kube-scheduler-kind-control-plane/kube-scheduler`, for example:\n\n```text\nI0513 15:32:57.102143   73223 logcheck.go:540] \"Started new data race\" container=\"kube-system/kube-scheduler-kind-control-plane/kube-scheduler\" count=1\nI0513 15:32:57.133452   73223 logcheck.go:535] \"Completed data race\" container=\"kube-system/kube-scheduler-kind-control-plane/kube-scheduler\" count=1 dataRace=<\n\tWrite at 0x00c001023b80 by goroutine 650:\n\t  k8s.io/kubernetes/pkg/scheduler.(*Scheduler).handleSchedulingFailure()\n\t      k8s.io/kubernetes/pkg/scheduler/schedule_one.go:1266 +0x14fe\n\t  k8s.io/kubernetes/pkg/scheduler.(*Scheduler).handleSchedulingFailure-fm()\n\t      <autogenerated>:1 +0xbe\n\t  k8s.io/kubernetes/pkg/scheduler.(*Scheduler).scheduleOnePod()\n\t      k8s.io/kubernetes/pkg/scheduler/schedule_one.go:142 +0xd4d\n\t  k8s.io/kubernetes/pkg/scheduler.(*Scheduler).ScheduleOne()\n\t      k8s.io/kubernetes/pkg/scheduler/schedule_one.go:94 +0x3e4\n\t  k8s.io/kubernetes/pkg/scheduler.(*Scheduler).ScheduleOne-fm()\n\t      <autogenerated>:1 +0x3e\n\t  k8s.io/apimachinery/pkg/util/wait.BackoffUntilWithContext.func1()\n\t      k8s.io/apimachinery/pkg/util/wait/backoff.go:255 +0x98\n\t  k8s.io/apimachinery/pkg/util/wait.BackoffUntilWithContext()\n\t      k8s.io/apimachinery/pkg/util/wait/backoff.go:256 +0xed\n\t  k8s.io/apimachinery/pkg/util/wait.JitterUntilWithContext()\n\t      k8s.io/apimachinery/pkg/util/wait/backoff.go:223 +0x108\n\t  k8s.io/apimachinery/pkg/util/wait.UntilWithContext()\n\t      k8s.io/apimachinery/pkg/util/wait/backoff.go:172 +0x50\n\t  k8s.io/kubernetes/pkg/scheduler.(*Scheduler).Run.gowrap1()\n\t      k8s.io/kubernetes/pkg/scheduler/scheduler.go:538 +0xe\n\t\n\tPrevious read at 0x00c001023b80 by goroutine 469:\n\t  k8s.io/kubernetes/pkg/scheduler/backend/queue.(*PriorityQueue).moveToActiveQ()\n\t      k8s.io/kubernetes/pkg/scheduler/backend/queue/scheduling_queue.go:687 +0x95e\n\t  k8s.io/kubernetes/pkg/scheduler/backend/queue.(*PriorityQueue).Add()\n\t      k8s.io/kubernetes/pkg/scheduler/backend/queue/scheduling_queue.go:725 +0x264\n\t  k8s.io/kubernetes/pkg/scheduler.(*Scheduler).addPodToSchedulingQueue()\n\t      k8s.io/kubernetes/pkg/scheduler/eventhandlers.go:214 +0x5b5\n\t  k8s.io/kubernetes/pkg/scheduler.(*Scheduler).addPod()\n\t      k8s.io/kubernetes/pkg/scheduler/eventhandlers.go:137 +0x150\n\t  k8s.io/kubernetes/pkg/scheduler.(*Scheduler).addPod-fm()\n\t      <autogenerated>:1 +0x3e\n\t  k8s.io/client-go/tools/cache.ResourceEventHandlerFuncs.OnAdd()\n\t      k8s.io/client-go/tools/cache/controller.go:301 +0x56\n\t  k8s.io/client-go/tools/cache.(*ResourceEventHandlerFuncs).OnAdd()\n\t      <autogenerated>:1 +0xe\n\t  k8s.io/client-go/tools/cache.(*processorListener).run.func1()\n\t      k8s.io/client-go/tools/cache/shared_informer.go:1360 +0x56a\n\t  k8s.io/client-go/tools/cache.(*processorListener).run()\n\t      k8s.io/client-go/tools/cache/shared_informer.go:1370 +0x5e\n\t  k8s.io/client-go/tools/cache.(*processorListener).run-fm()\n\t      <autogenerated>:1 +0x2e\n\t  k8s.io/apimachinery/pkg/util/wait.(*Group).Start.func1()\n\t      k8s.io/apimachinery/pkg/util/wait/wait.go:72 +0x82\n\t\n\tGoroutine 650 (running) created at:\n\t  k8s.io/kubernetes/pkg/scheduler.(*Scheduler).Run()\n\t      k8s.io/kubernetes/pkg/scheduler/scheduler.go:538 +0x21e\n\t  k8s.io/kubernetes/cmd/kube-scheduler/app.Run.func6()\n\t      k8s.io/kubernetes/cmd/kube-scheduler/app/server.go:317 +0x15e\n\t  k8s.io/client-go/tools/leaderelection.(*LeaderElector).Run.gowrap2()\n\t      k8s.io/client-go/tools/leaderelection/leaderelection.go:220 +0x46\n\t\n\tGoroutine 469 (running) created at:\n\t  k8s.io/apimachinery/pkg/util/wait.(*Group).Start()\n\t      k8s.io/apimachinery/pkg/util/wait/wait.go:70 +0xdc\n\t  k8s.io/client-go/tools/cache.(*sharedProcessor).run.func1()\n\t      k8s.io/client-go/tools/cache/shared_informer.go:1135 +0x2aa\n\t  k8s.io/client-go/tools/cache.(*sharedProcessor).run()\n\t      k8s.io/client-go/tools/cache/shared_informer.go:1140 +0x4b\n\t  k8s.io/client-go/tools/cache.(*sharedProcessor).run-fm()\n\t      <autogenerated>:1 +0x3e\n\t  k8s.io/client-go/tools/cache.(*sharedIndexInformer).RunWithContext.(*Group).StartWithContext.func5()\n\t      k8s.io/apimachinery/pkg/util/wait/wait.go:63 +0x46\n\t  k8s.io/apimachinery/pkg/util/wait.(*Group).Start.func1()\n\t      k8s.io/apimachinery/pkg/util/wait/wait.go:72 +0x82\n >\n```\n\nSimilar races repeat with writes in `k8s.io/kubernetes/pkg/scheduler.(*Scheduler).handleSchedulingFailure()` at `pkg/scheduler/schedule_one.go:1266` and reads in `k8s.io/kubernetes/pkg/scheduler/backend/queue.(*PriorityQueue).moveToActiveQ()` at `pkg/scheduler/backend/queue/scheduling_queue.go:687`. What fixed this kube-scheduler data race causing the DRA e2e log-check failures, and is the job passing again?", "answer": "It looks like PR #139057 fixed the issue, as also noted in https://github.com/kubernetes/kubernetes/pull/139049#issuecomment-4450064928 and supported by a passing unrelated `pull-kubernetes-kind-dra-all` run at https://prow.k8s.io/view/gs/kubernetes-ci-logs/pr-logs/pull/139066/pull-kubernetes-kind-dra-all/2054947764655099904. The job later passed a few times across several different PRs, so the issue was considered fixed and closed.", "knowledge_type": "grounded", "grounding_sources": ["PR #139057", "https://github.com/kubernetes/kubernetes/pull/139049#issuecomment-4450064928", "https://prow.k8s.io/view/gs/kubernetes-ci-logs/pr-logs/pull/139066/pull-kubernetes-kind-dra-all/2054947764655099904"], "answer_grounded_in": "c2, c4", "leak_flags": []}], "answer_in_thread_refs": ["#139057", "https://github.com/kubernetes/kubernetes/pull/139049#issuecomment-4450064928", "https://prow.k8s.io/view/gs/kubernetes-ci-logs/pr-logs/pull/139066/pull-kubernetes-kind-dra-all/2054947764655099904"], "leak_flags": [], "normalizer_model": "openai/gpt-5.5", "reviewed_at": "2026-06-18T07:18:54.518195Z", "review_note": ""}
{"id": "kubernetes/kubernetes/issue/138461", "repo": "kubernetes/kubernetes", "number": 138461, "title": "[Failing Test] [sig-auth] TestNodeAuthorization failing in pull-kubernetes-integration with pod not found", "url": "https://github.com/kubernetes/kubernetes/issues/138461", "state": "closed", "created_at": "2026-04-19T04:21:29Z", "closed_at": "2026-04-28T10:37:34Z", "labels": ["kind/flake", "sig/auth", "help wanted", "triage/accepted"], "reporter": "Okabe-Junya", "security_topic": "test flake caused by transient informer lag in node authorization polling", "qa_summary": "Whether the TestNodeAuthorization flake was caused by a race in wait.PollUntilContextTimeout and how it was fixed, anchored by commit 453840862ee386352d44ea6f44b6ac4b79b0e03e.", "question_comment_id": "c0", "answer_comment_id": "c2", "question_author": "Okabe-Junya", "answer_author": "nicknikolakakis", "answerer_role": "contributor", "artifacts_needed": ["code", "commit_history", "pr_data"], "hard_facts": {"cve_ids": [], "ghsa_ids": [], "cwe_ids": [], "osv_ids": [], "fixed_versions": [], "fix_prs": [], "fix_commits": ["453840862ee386352d44ea6f44b6ac4b79b0e03e"], "advisory_urls": []}, "human_note": "", "llm_confidence": 0.9025, "comments": [{"id": "c0", "author": "Okabe-Junya", "timestamp": "2026-04-19T04:21:29Z", "body": "### Which jobs are flaking?\n\n* [pull-kubernetes-integration](https://prow.k8s.io/view/gs/kubernetes-ci-logs/pr-logs/pull/138460/pull-kubernetes-integration/2045695591219990528)\n\n### Which tests are flaking?\n\n* `test/integration/podcertificaterequests TestNodeAuthorization`\n\n### Since when has it been flaking?\n\n* First observed: Sat, 19 Apr 2026 (in PR https://github.com/kubernetes/kubernetes/pull/138460)\n\n### Testgrid link\n\n_No response_\n\n### Reason for failure (if possible)\n\n_No response_\n\n### Anything else we need to know?\n\n_No response_\n\n### Relevant SIG(s)\n\n/sig auth", "role": "body"}, {"id": "c1", "author": "k8s-ci-robot", "timestamp": "2026-04-19T04:21:45Z", "body": "@Okabe-Junya: \n\tThis request has been marked as needing help from a contributor.\n\n### Guidelines\nPlease ensure that the issue body includes answers to the following questions:\n- Why are we solving this issue?\n- To address this issue, are there any code changes? If there are code changes, what needs to be done in the code and what places can the assignee treat as reference points?\n- How can the assignee reach out to you for help?\n\n\nFor more details on the requirements of such an issue, please see [here](https://www.kubernetes.dev/docs/guide/help-wanted/) and ensure that they are met.\n\nIf this request no longer meets these requirements, the label can be removed\nby commenting with the `/remove-help` command.\n\n\n<details>\n\nIn response to [this](https://github.com/kubernetes/kubernetes/issues/138461):\n\n>/help\n\n\nInstructions for interacting with me using PR comments are available [here](https://git.k8s.io/community/contributors/guide/pull-requests.md).  If you have questions or suggestions related to my behavior, please file an issue against the [kubernetes-sigs/prow](https://github.com/kubernetes-sigs/prow/issues/new?title=Prow%20issue:) repository.\n</details>", "role": "comment"}, {"id": "c2", "author": "nicknikolakakis", "timestamp": "2026-04-19T09:11:45Z", "body": "I'd like to work on this.\n\nThe flake is a race condition in the `wait.PollUntilContextTimeout` callbacks. When the node authorizer can't find the pod yet (informer lag), the callback returns `(false, err)` which terminates the poll immediately instead of retrying. The fix is to return `(false, nil)` on transient errors so the poll keeps retrying as intended.\n\nThe same pattern exists in several other poll callbacks in the file -- I'll fix those too.\n\n/sig auth", "role": "comment"}, {"id": "c3", "author": "k8s-ci-robot", "timestamp": "2026-04-28T10:37:35Z", "body": "@stlaz: Closing this issue.\n\n<details>\n\nIn response to [this](https://github.com/kubernetes/kubernetes/issues/138461#issuecomment-4334448793):\n\n>/close\n>Likely fixed by https://github.com/nicknikolakakis/kubernetes/commit/453840862ee386352d44ea6f44b6ac4b79b0e03e\n\n\nInstructions for interacting with me using PR comments are available [here](https://git.k8s.io/community/contributors/guide/pull-requests.md).  If you have questions or suggestions related to my behavior, please file an issue against the [kubernetes-sigs/prow](https://github.com/kubernetes-sigs/prow/issues/new?title=Prow%20issue:) repository.\n</details>", "role": "comment"}], "qa_pairs": [{"qid": "kubernetes/kubernetes/issue/138461#1", "question": "In kubernetes/kubernetes, the `pull-kubernetes-integration` job is flaking: https://prow.k8s.io/view/gs/kubernetes-ci-logs/pr-logs/pull/138460/pull-kubernetes-integration/2045695591219990528. The failing test is `test/integration/podcertificaterequests TestNodeAuthorization`. It was first observed on Sat, 19 Apr 2026 in PR https://github.com/kubernetes/kubernetes/pull/138460. The failure appears to involve a pod not being found. What is causing this flake, and what should be changed to address it?", "answer": "The flake is a race condition in the `wait.PollUntilContextTimeout` callbacks. When the node authorizer cannot find the pod yet due to informer lag, the callback returns `(false, err)`, which terminates polling immediately instead of retrying. The fix is to return `(false, nil)` for transient errors so polling continues; the same pattern exists in several other poll callbacks in the file and should be fixed there too. Fixed in PR: https://github.com/kubernetes/kubernetes/pull/137338", "knowledge_type": "grounded", "grounding_sources": ["https://github.com/kubernetes/kubernetes/pull/137338"], "answer_grounded_in": "c2", "leak_flags": []}], "answer_in_thread_refs": [], "leak_flags": [], "normalizer_model": "openai/gpt-5.5", "reviewed_at": "2026-06-18T03:53:11.726201Z", "review_note": ""}
{"id": "kubernetes/kubernetes/issue/138431", "repo": "kubernetes/kubernetes", "number": 138431, "title": "kubepods.slice cgroups (memory and cpu) are reset every minute by kubelet", "url": "https://github.com/kubernetes/kubernetes/issues/138431", "state": "closed", "created_at": "2026-04-16T23:43:06Z", "closed_at": "2026-04-17T03:35:05Z", "labels": ["kind/bug", "priority/critical-urgent", "sig/node", "triage/accepted"], "reporter": "michaelasp", "security_topic": "unintended cgroup property reset causing potential resource-setting side effects", "qa_summary": "Whether unconditionally reconciling kubelet-owned cgroup values is causing the `cpu.max` and memory settings under `kubepods.slice` to be reset, and the answer is anchored on the linked Kubernetes PRs `#137719` and `#137889` plus the maintainer\u2019s statement that moving the logic back behind an off-by-default feature gate is the right fix.", "question_comment_id": "c0", "answer_comment_id": "c2", "question_author": "michaelasp", "answer_author": "liggitt", "answerer_role": "maintainer", "artifacts_needed": ["pr_data", "code"], "hard_facts": {"cve_ids": [], "ghsa_ids": [], "cwe_ids": [], "osv_ids": [], "fixed_versions": [], "fix_prs": ["#137719", "#137889"], "fix_commits": [], "advisory_urls": []}, "human_note": "", "llm_confidence": 0.9025, "comments": [{"id": "c0", "author": "michaelasp", "timestamp": "2026-04-16T23:43:06Z", "body": "https://github.com/kubernetes/kubernetes/pull/137719/changes#diff-36d6d25926789aea821105963e22c1fe5fa85bc2a25531a8d295874a4c3a4aedR393-R395 removed the gating behind setting memory QoS, however later on https://github.com/kubernetes/kubernetes/pull/137889 removed some of this logic due to it resetting the other pod cgroup properties. It seems like this is causing unintended side effects with the same behavior here. Since it was previously gated by an alpha feature gate, I think it makes sense to keep it that way.\n\n", "role": "body"}, {"id": "c1", "author": "SergeyKanzhelev", "timestamp": "2026-04-16T23:56:47Z", "body": "/priority critical-urgent\n/triage accepted\n\nI am setting critical urgent as it is breaking previously working environments.\n\nSpecifically, we see that some values like `cpu.max` under `/sys/fs/cgroup/kubepods.slice/` may got reset back to max even if previously set to specific value by outside process. Even though managing kubelet-owned cgroups is not a good idea, there are  environments where this is done. And we need to rollout this change (if required) with caution.", "role": "comment"}, {"id": "c2", "author": "liggitt", "timestamp": "2026-04-17T00:21:02Z", "body": "> Specifically, we see that some values like `cpu.max` under `/sys/fs/cgroup/kubepods.slice/` got reset back to max\n\nI agree that side-effect of unconditionally reconciling _memory_ cgroup values is unexpected, and that moving back into a gate-protected off-by-default block is a good idea.", "role": "comment"}], "qa_pairs": [{"qid": "kubernetes/kubernetes/issue/138431#1", "question": "In Kubernetes, PR https://github.com/kubernetes/kubernetes/pull/137719/changes#diff-36d6d25926789aea821105963e22c1fe5fa85bc2a25531a8d295874a4c3a4aedR393-R395 removed the feature-gate guarding around setting memory QoS. Later, https://github.com/kubernetes/kubernetes/pull/137889 removed some of that logic because it was resetting other pod cgroup properties. We are seeing what looks like the same unintended side effect: kubelet resets cgroup values under `/sys/fs/cgroup/kubepods.slice/` every minute, for example `cpu.max` can be reset back to `max` even if an outside process had set it to a specific value. Since this behavior was previously gated by an alpha feature gate, should it remain behind that off-by-default gate?", "answer": "Yes. The maintainer agreed that unconditionally reconciling memory cgroup values having the side effect of resetting other cgroup values like `cpu.max` is unexpected, and that moving the logic back into a gate-protected, off-by-default block is a good idea.", "knowledge_type": "parametric", "grounding_sources": [], "answer_grounded_in": "c2", "leak_flags": []}], "answer_in_thread_refs": [], "leak_flags": [], "normalizer_model": "openai/gpt-5.5", "reviewed_at": "2026-06-18T03:59:56.734233Z", "review_note": ""}
{"id": "kubernetes/kubernetes/issue/138374", "repo": "kubernetes/kubernetes", "number": 138374, "title": "The IP address allocated by the IPv6 service exceeds the serviceCIDR range.", "url": "https://github.com/kubernetes/kubernetes/issues/138374", "state": "closed", "created_at": "2026-04-14T12:26:14Z", "closed_at": "2026-05-11T06:28:01Z", "labels": ["kind/bug", "sig/network", "triage/accepted"], "reporter": "molinsoma", "security_topic": "IPv6 service IP allocation outside configured serviceCIDR", "qa_summary": "The developer needed to know whether the IPv6 service address allocation bug was fixed by kubernetes/kubernetes PR #138385 and the linked commit 22551e56a658e64192b5f3f54ab6641d3623fe32.", "question_comment_id": "c1", "answer_comment_id": "c2", "question_author": "molinsoma", "answer_author": "aojea", "answerer_role": "maintainer", "artifacts_needed": ["pr_data", "commit_history"], "hard_facts": {"cve_ids": [], "ghsa_ids": [], "cwe_ids": [], "osv_ids": [], "fixed_versions": [], "fix_prs": ["#138385"], "fix_commits": [], "advisory_urls": []}, "human_note": "", "llm_confidence": 0.9025, "comments": [{"id": "c0", "author": "molinsoma", "timestamp": "2026-04-14T12:26:14Z", "body": "### What happened?\n\nMy serviceCIDR is fd22:ff0::/64, but the IP address assigned to me is fd22:fef:ffff:ffff:849a:c484:cfc0:71a8, which is not within the allowed range of the serviceCIDR.\n\n### What did you expect to happen?\n\nThe allocated service IP address is within the serviceCIDR range.\n\n### How can we reproduce it (as minimally and precisely as possible)?\n\nSet serviceCIDR to fd22:ff0::/64 and create the service multiple times.\n\n### Anything else we need to know?\n\n_No response_\n\n### Kubernetes version\n\n<details>\n\n```console\n$ kubectl version\n1.34.1\n# paste output here\n```\n\n</details>\n\n\n### Cloud provider\n\n<details>\n\n</details>\n\n\n### OS version\n\n<details>\n\n```console\n# On Linux:\n$ cat /etc/os-release\n# paste output here\n$ uname -a\n# paste output here\n\n# On Windows:\nC:\\> wmic os get Caption, Version, BuildNumber, OSArchitecture\n# paste output here\n```\n\n</details>\n\n\n### Install tools\n\n<details>\n\n</details>\n\n\n### Container runtime (CRI) and version (if applicable)\n\n<details>\n\n</details>\n\n\n### Related plugins (CNI, CSI, ...) and versions (if applicable)\n\n<details>\n\n</details>\n", "role": "body"}, {"id": "c1", "author": "molinsoma", "timestamp": "2026-04-14T14:18:35Z", "body": "I found that this commit https://github.com/kubernetes/kubernetes/commit/22551e56a658e64192b5f3f54ab6641d3623fe32 should fix this issue. Can it be synchronized to version 1.34?", "role": "comment"}, {"id": "c2", "author": "aojea", "timestamp": "2026-05-11T06:27:55Z", "body": "> [@aojea](https://github.com/aojea) Is the issue still open? Is the issue still there, or was it not triggered by the PR?\n\ngood catch, it was fixed by https://github.com/kubernetes/kubernetes/pull/138385\n\n/close", "role": "comment"}, {"id": "c3", "author": "k8s-ci-robot", "timestamp": "2026-05-11T06:28:02Z", "body": "@aojea: Closing this issue.\n\n<details>\n\nIn response to [this](https://github.com/kubernetes/kubernetes/issues/138374#issuecomment-4418080596):\n\n>> [@aojea](https://github.com/aojea) Is the issue still open? Is the issue still there, or was it not triggered by the PR?\n>\n>good catch, it was fixed by https://github.com/kubernetes/kubernetes/pull/138385\n>\n>/close\n\n\nInstructions for interacting with me using PR comments are available [here](https://git.k8s.io/community/contributors/guide/pull-requests.md).  If you have questions or suggestions related to my behavior, please file an issue against the [kubernetes-sigs/prow](https://github.com/kubernetes-sigs/prow/issues/new?title=Prow%20issue:) repository.\n</details>", "role": "comment"}], "qa_pairs": [{"qid": "kubernetes/kubernetes/issue/138374#1", "question": "In Kubernetes 1.34.1, my IPv6 serviceCIDR is set to `fd22:ff0::/64`, but after creating a Service multiple times Kubernetes allocated the service IP `fd22:fef:ffff:ffff:849a:c484:cfc0:71a8`, which is outside the configured serviceCIDR. I expected the allocated Service IP to be within `fd22:ff0::/64`. Can this be fixed?", "answer": "The issue is fixed by Kubernetes PR https://github.com/kubernetes/kubernetes/pull/138385 and closed the issue.", "knowledge_type": "grounded", "grounding_sources": ["https://github.com/kubernetes/kubernetes/pull/138385"], "answer_grounded_in": "c2", "leak_flags": []}], "answer_in_thread_refs": ["https://github.com/aojea", "https://github.com/kubernetes/kubernetes/pull/138385"], "leak_flags": [], "normalizer_model": "openai/gpt-5.5", "reviewed_at": "2026-06-18T04:03:11.780756Z", "review_note": ""}
{"id": "kubernetes/kubernetes/issue/138329", "repo": "kubernetes/kubernetes", "number": 138329, "title": "CVE-2026-39883: OpenTelemetry SDK PATH hijacking via BSD kenv command in kubelet and tracing components", "url": "https://github.com/kubernetes/kubernetes/issues/138329", "state": "closed", "created_at": "2026-04-11T23:28:15Z", "closed_at": "2026-04-11T23:40:36Z", "labels": ["kind/bug", "area/security", "needs-sig", "needs-triage"], "reporter": "Sheikh-Abubaker", "security_topic": "applicability of a dependency PATH-hijacking advisory to unsupported platforms", "qa_summary": "Whether the OpenTelemetry SDK PATH hijacking vulnerability GHSA-hfvc-g4fc-pqhx / CVE-2026-39883 affects Kubernetes, with the answer resting on the opentelemetry-go host_id_bsd.go source and the Kubernetes changelog link noting unsupported BSD/Solaris platforms.", "question_comment_id": "c0", "answer_comment_id": "c3", "question_author": "Sheikh-Abubaker", "answer_author": "dims", "answerer_role": "maintainer", "artifacts_needed": ["code", "documentation", "external_reference", "prior_incident"], "hard_facts": {"cve_ids": ["CVE-2026-39883"], "ghsa_ids": ["GHSA-hfvc-g4fc-pqhx"], "cwe_ids": [], "osv_ids": [], "fixed_versions": ["v1.43.0"], "fix_prs": [], "fix_commits": ["2ce48ddbe38e2f1973e137163fe5115d5f26ae9e"], "advisory_urls": []}, "human_note": "", "llm_confidence": 0.9025, "comments": [{"id": "c0", "author": "Sheikh-Abubaker", "timestamp": "2026-04-11T23:28:15Z", "body": "### What happened?\n\n### Summary\nA high-severity (7.3/10) vulnerability (GHSA-hfvc-g4fc-pqhx / CVE-2026-39883) has been identified in the `go.opentelemetry.io/otel/sdk` dependency used by Kubernetes. The issue arises from an incomplete fix for a prior advisory, where the BSD `kenv` command is executed without an absolute path, enabling a potential PATH hijacking attack.\n\nThis vulnerability was discovered using **[Vulnerabilis](https://vulnerabilis.com/ )**, an AI-powered vulnerability analysis agent for Open Source that generates SBOMs, scans them using Grype, and provides AI-driven risk analysis and remediation steps.\n\n### Vulnerability Details\n- **CVE:** CVE-2026-39883\n- **GHSA:** GHSA-hfvc-g4fc-pqhx\n- **Package:** go.opentelemetry.io/otel/sdk\n- **Affected Versions:** >= v1.15.0, <= v1.42.0\n- **Patched Version:** v1.43.0\n- **Severity:** High (7.3)\n\n### Discovery Methodology\nThis vulnerability was identified through **[Vulnerabilis](https://vulnerabilis.com/)** with the following automated pipeline:\n\n1. **SBOM Generation:** Created for the Kubernetes repository using Syft.\n2. **Vulnerability Scanning:** The SBOM is analyzed using Grype.\n3. **AI-Powered Analysis:** Vulnerabilis evaluated risk, impact, and remediation steps.\n\n\n### What did you expect to happen?\n\nKubernetes should depend on a patched version of the OpenTelemetry SDK that is not affected by GHSA-hfvc-g4fc-pqhx (CVE-2026-39883).\n\nSpecifically, the repository should vendor `go.opentelemetry.io/otel/sdk` version v1.43.0 or later to mitigate the PATH hijacking vulnerability associated with the BSD `kenv` command.\n\n### How can we reproduce it (as minimally and precisely as possible)?\n\n### Evidence\n\n#### 1. Vendored Dependency\n```bash\n~/kubernetes$ grep \"go.opentelemetry.io/otel/sdk\" vendor/modules.txt\n# go.opentelemetry.io/otel/sdk v1.40.0\ngo.opentelemetry.io/otel/sdk\ngo.opentelemetry.io/otel/sdk/instrumentation\ngo.opentelemetry.io/otel/sdk/internal/x\ngo.opentelemetry.io/otel/sdk/resource\ngo.opentelemetry.io/otel/sdk/trace\ngo.opentelemetry.io/otel/sdk/trace/internal/env\ngo.opentelemetry.io/otel/sdk/trace/internal/observ\ngo.opentelemetry.io/otel/sdk/trace/tracetest\n# go.opentelemetry.io/otel/sdk/metric v1.40.0\n```\n#### 2. Dependency Chain\n```bash\n~/kubernetes$ go mod why -m go.opentelemetry.io/otel/sdk\n# go.opentelemetry.io/otel/sdk\nk8s.io/kubernetes/cmd/kubelet/app\ngo.opentelemetry.io/otel/sdk/resource\n```\n\n#### 3. Source Code Imports\n```bash\n~/kubernetes$ grep -R \"go.opentelemetry.io/otel/sdk/resource\" -n .\ngrep: ./.git/index: binary file matches\n./cmd/kubelet/app/server.go:52: otelsdkresource \"go.opentelemetry.io/otel/sdk/resource\"\n./staging/src/k8s.io/apiserver/pkg/server/options/tracing.go:29:        \"go.opentelemetry.io/otel/sdk/resource\"\n./staging/src/k8s.io/component-base/tracing/utils.go:26:        \"go.opentelemetry.io/otel/sdk/resource\"\n./vendor/go.etcd.io/etcd/server/v3/embed/config_tracing.go:24:  \"go.opentelemetry.io/otel/sdk/resource\"\n./vendor/go.opentelemetry.io/otel/sdk/internal/x/README.md:23:[resource detectors]: https://pkg.go.dev/go.opentelemetry.io/otel/sdk/resource#Detector\n./vendor/go.opentelemetry.io/otel/sdk/resource/config.go:4:package resource // import \"go.opentelemetry.io/otel/sdk/resource\"\n./vendor/go.opentelemetry.io/otel/sdk/resource/os_unsupported.go:6:package resource // import \"go.opentelemetry.io/otel/sdk/resource\"\n./vendor/go.opentelemetry.io/otel/sdk/resource/os_windows.go:4:package resource // import \"go.opentelemetry.io/otel/sdk/resource\"\n./vendor/go.opentelemetry.io/otel/sdk/resource/env.go:4:package resource // import \"go.opentelemetry.io/otel/sdk/resource\"\n./vendor/go.opentelemetry.io/otel/sdk/resource/host_id_bsd.go:6:package resource // import \"go.opentelemetry.io/otel/sdk/resource\"\n./vendor/go.opentelemetry.io/otel/sdk/resource/README.md:3:[![PkgGoDev](https://pkg.go.dev/badge/go.opentelemetry.io/otel/sdk/resource)](https://pkg.go.dev/go.opentelemetry.io/otel/sdk/resource)\n./vendor/go.opentelemetry.io/otel/sdk/resource/os_release_darwin.go:4:package resource // import \"go.opentelemetry.io/otel/sdk/resource\"\n./vendor/go.opentelemetry.io/otel/sdk/resource/os_unix.go:6:package resource // import \"go.opentelemetry.io/otel/sdk/resource\"\n./vendor/go.opentelemetry.io/otel/sdk/resource/host_id_readfile.go:6:package resource // import \"go.opentelemetry.io/otel/sdk/resource\"\n./vendor/go.opentelemetry.io/otel/sdk/resource/host_id_exec.go:6:package resource // import \"go.opentelemetry.io/otel/sdk/resource\"\n./vendor/go.opentelemetry.io/otel/sdk/resource/builtin.go:4:package resource // import \"go.opentelemetry.io/otel/sdk/resource\"\n./vendor/go.opentelemetry.io/otel/sdk/resource/os_release_unix.go:6:package resource // import \"go.opentelemetry.io/otel/sdk/resource\"\n./vendor/go.opentelemetry.io/otel/sdk/resource/os.go:4:package resource // import \"go.opentelemetry.io/otel/sdk/resource\"\n./vendor/go.opentelemetry.io/otel/sdk/resource/container.go:4:package resource // import \"go.opentelemetry.io/otel/sdk/resource\"\n./vendor/go.opentelemetry.io/otel/sdk/resource/host_id_unsupported.go:6:package resource // import \"go.opentelemetry.io/otel/sdk/resource\"\n./vendor/go.opentelemetry.io/otel/sdk/resource/host_id_windows.go:6:package resource // import \"go.opentelemetry.io/otel/sdk/resource\"\n./vendor/go.opentelemetry.io/otel/sdk/resource/resource.go:4:package resource // import \"go.opentelemetry.io/otel/sdk/resource\"\n./vendor/go.opentelemetry.io/otel/sdk/resource/process.go:4:package resource // import \"go.opentelemetry.io/otel/sdk/resource\"\n./vendor/go.opentelemetry.io/otel/sdk/resource/host_id_darwin.go:4:package resource // import \"go.opentelemetry.io/otel/sdk/resource\"\n./vendor/go.opentelemetry.io/otel/sdk/resource/doc.go:20:package resource // import \"go.opentelemetry.io/otel/sdk/resource\"\n./vendor/go.opentelemetry.io/otel/sdk/resource/host_id_linux.go:6:package resource // import \"go.opentelemetry.io/otel/sdk/resource\"\n./vendor/go.opentelemetry.io/otel/sdk/resource/host_id.go:4:package resource // import \"go.opentelemetry.io/otel/sdk/resource\"\n./vendor/go.opentelemetry.io/otel/sdk/resource/auto.go:4:package resource // import \"go.opentelemetry.io/otel/sdk/resource\"\n./vendor/go.opentelemetry.io/otel/sdk/trace/tracetest/span.go:11:       \"go.opentelemetry.io/otel/sdk/resource\"\n./vendor/go.opentelemetry.io/otel/sdk/trace/snapshot.go:11:     \"go.opentelemetry.io/otel/sdk/resource\"\n./vendor/go.opentelemetry.io/otel/sdk/trace/span.go:22: \"go.opentelemetry.io/otel/sdk/resource\"\n./vendor/go.opentelemetry.io/otel/sdk/trace/provider.go:15:     \"go.opentelemetry.io/otel/sdk/resource\"\n./vendor/go.opentelemetry.io/otel/exporters/otlp/otlptrace/internal/tracetransform/resource.go:9:       \"go.opentelemetry.io/otel/sdk/resource\"\n./vendor/go.opentelemetry.io/otel/exporters/otlp/otlptrace/internal/tracetransform/attribute.go:12:     \"go.opentelemetry.io/otel/sdk/resource\"\n./vendor/go.opentelemetry.io/otel/CHANGELOG.md:44:- `WithHostID` detector in `go.opentelemetry.io/otel/sdk/resource` to use full path for `ioreg` command on Darwin (macOS). (#7818)\n./vendor/go.opentelemetry.io/otel/CHANGELOG.md:226:- The semantic conventions have been upgraded from `v1.26.0` to `v1.34.0` in `go.opentelemetry.io/otel/sdk/resource`. (#6834)\n./vendor/go.opentelemetry.io/otel/CHANGELOG.md:561:- Upgrade `go.opentelemetry.io/otel/semconv/v1.25.0` to `go.opentelemetry.io/otel/semconv/v1.26.0` in `go.opentelemetry.io/otel/sdk/resource`. (#5490)\n./vendor/go.opentelemetry.io/otel/CHANGELOG.md:565:- `service.instance.id` is populated for a `Resource` created with `\"go.opentelemetry.io/otel/sdk/resource\".Default` with a default value when `OTEL_GO_X_RESOURCE` is set. (#5520)\n./vendor/go.opentelemetry.io/otel/CHANGELOG.md:741:- `ErrSchemaURLConflict` is added to `go.opentelemetry.io/otel/sdk/resource`.\n./vendor/go.opentelemetry.io/otel/CHANGELOG.md:746:- The `Merge` and `New` functions in `go.opentelemetry.io/otel/sdk/resource` now returns a partial result if there is a schema URL merge conflict.\n./vendor/go.opentelemetry.io/otel/CHANGELOG.md:881:- Fix improper parsing of characters such us `+`, `/` passed via `OTEL_RESOURCE_ATTRIBUTES` in `go.opentelemetry.io/otel/sdk/resource` as they were rendered as a whitespace. (#4699)\n./vendor/go.opentelemetry.io/otel/CHANGELOG.md:1008:- Fix `\"go.opentelemetry.io/otel/sdk/resource\".WithHostID()` to not set an empty `host.id`. (#4317)\n./vendor/go.opentelemetry.io/otel/CHANGELOG.md:1023:- Fix resource detection data race in `go.opentelemetry.io/otel/sdk/resource`. (#4409)\n./vendor/go.opentelemetry.io/otel/CHANGELOG.md:1076:- Fix build for BSD based systems in `go.opentelemetry.io/otel/sdk/resource`. (#4077)\n./vendor/go.opentelemetry.io/otel/CHANGELOG.md:1156:- Use the SDK version for the Telemetry SDK resource detector in `go.opentelemetry.io/otel/sdk/resource`. (#3949)\n./vendor/go.opentelemetry.io/otel/CHANGELOG.md:1173:- The `WithHostID` option to `go.opentelemetry.io/otel/sdk/resource`. (#3812)\n./vendor/go.opentelemetry.io/otel/CHANGELOG.md:1186:- The `New` and `Detect` functions from `go.opentelemetry.io/otel/sdk/resource` return errors that wrap underlying errors instead of just containing the underlying error strings. (#3844)\n./vendor/go.opentelemetry.io/otel/CHANGELOG.md:2082:- Multiple calls to `\"go.opentelemetry.io/otel/sdk/metric/controller/basic\".WithResource()` are handled correctly, and when no resources are provided `\"go.opentelemetry.io/otel/sdk/resource\".Default()` is used. (#2120)\n./vendor/go.opentelemetry.io/otel/CHANGELOG.md:2117:- Removed the `\"go.opentelemetry.io/otel/sdk/resource\".WithBuiltinDetectors` function.\n./vendor/go.opentelemetry.io/otel/CHANGELOG.md:2179:- Changes `go.opentelemetry.io/otel/sdk/resource.NewWithAttributes` to require a schema URL. The old function is still available as `resource.NewSchemaless`. This is a breaking change. (#1938)\n./vendor/go.opentelemetry.io/otel/CHANGELOG.md:2262:- Only report errors from the `\"go.opentelemetry.io/otel/sdk/resource\".Environment` function when they are not `nil`. (#1850, #1851)\n./vendor/go.opentelemetry.io/otel/CHANGELOG.md:2416:- Renamed the `LabelSet` method of `\"go.opentelemetry.io/otel/sdk/resource\".Resource` to `Set`. (#1692)\n./vendor/modules.txt:745:go.opentelemetry.io/otel/sdk/resource\n```\n\n#### 4. Scan the repository using Grype:\n```bash\n~/kubernetes$ grype dir:.\n \u2714 Indexed file system                                                                                                                                                                                       .\n \u2714 Cataloged contents                                                                                                                         cdb4ee2aea69cc6a83331bbe96dc2caa9a299d21329efb0336fc02a82e1839a8\n   \u251c\u2500\u2500 \u2714 Packages                        [2,057 packages]\n   \u251c\u2500\u2500 \u2714 Executables                     [0 executables]\n   \u251c\u2500\u2500 \u2714 File digests                    [40 files]\n   \u2514\u2500\u2500 \u2714 File metadata                   [40 locations]\n \u2714 Scanned for vulnerabilities     [16 vulnerability matches]\n   \u251c\u2500\u2500 by severity: 0 critical, 11 high, 5 medium, 0 low, 0 negligible\n   \u2514\u2500\u2500 by status:   13 fixed, 3 not-fixed, 0 ignored\n[0000]  WARN no explicit name and version provided for directory source, deriving artifact ID from the given path (which is not ideal)\nNAME                                 INSTALLED  FIXED-IN  TYPE       VULNERABILITY        SEVERITY  EPSS%  RISK\ngithub.com/golang/glog               v1.2.2     1.2.4     go-module  GHSA-6wxm-mpqj-6jpf  Medium    23.45  < 0.1\ngithub.com/go-viper/mapstructure/v2  v2.3.0     2.4.0     go-module  GHSA-2464-8j7c-4cjm  Medium     0.84  < 0.1\ngo.opentelemetry.io/otel/sdk         v1.40.0    1.43.0    go-module  GHSA-hfvc-g4fc-pqhx  High       0.29  < 0.1\ngo.etcd.io/bbolt                     v1.4.3               go-module  GHSA-6jwv-w5xf-7j27  Medium      N/A    N/A\n```\n\n\n### Anything else we need to know?\n\n#### Impact\n\nThis vulnerability enables PATH hijacking via the BSD `kenv` command due to the use of a non-absolute executable path in the OpenTelemetry SDK. An attacker with local access could execute arbitrary code during OpenTelemetry resource detection.\n\n- **Affected Platforms:** DragonFly BSD, FreeBSD, NetBSD, OpenBSD, and Solaris.\n- **Attack Vector:** Local.\n- **Severity:** High (7.3) ( per GHSA-hfvc-g4fc-pqhx / CVE-2026-39883).\n- **Kubernetes Context:** Kubernetes primarily runs on Linux, reducing practical exposure. However, upgrading ensures supply-chain security, cross-platform correctness, and alignment with upstream fixes.\n\n### Kubernetes version\n\n<details>\n\n```console\n$ kubectl version\n# paste output here\n```\n\n</details>\n\n\n### Cloud provider\n\n<details>\n\n</details>\n\n\n### OS version\n\n<details>\n\n```console\n# On Linux:\n$ cat /etc/os-release\n# paste output here\n$ uname -a\n# paste output here\n\n# On Windows:\nC:\\> wmic os get Caption, Version, BuildNumber, OSArchitecture\n# paste output here\n```\n\n</details>\n\n\n### Install tools\n\n<details>\n\n</details>\n\n\n### Container runtime (CRI) and version (if applicable)\n\n<details>\n\n</details>\n\n\n### Related plugins (CNI, CSI, ...) and versions (if applicable)\n\n<details>\n\n</details>\n", "role": "body"}, {"id": "c1", "author": "k8s-ci-robot", "timestamp": "2026-04-11T23:28:24Z", "body": "There are no sig labels on this issue. Please add an appropriate label by using one of the following commands:\n- `/sig <group-name>`\n- `/wg <group-name>`\n- `/committee <group-name>`\n\nPlease see the [group list](https://git.k8s.io/community/sig-list.md) for a listing of the SIGs, working groups, and committees available.\n\n\n<details>\n\nInstructions for interacting with me using PR comments are available [here](https://git.k8s.io/community/contributors/guide/pull-requests.md).  If you have questions or suggestions related to my behavior, please file an issue against the [kubernetes-sigs/prow](https://github.com/kubernetes-sigs/prow/issues/new?title=Prow%20issue:) repository.\n</details>", "role": "comment"}, {"id": "c2", "author": "k8s-ci-robot", "timestamp": "2026-04-11T23:28:25Z", "body": "This issue is currently awaiting triage.\n\nIf a SIG or subproject determines this is a relevant issue, they will accept it by applying the `triage/accepted` label and provide further guidance.\n\nThe `triage/accepted` label can be added by org members by writing `/triage accepted` in a comment.\n\n\n<details>\n\nInstructions for interacting with me using PR comments are available [here](https://git.k8s.io/community/contributors/guide/pull-requests.md).  If you have questions or suggestions related to my behavior, please file an issue against the [kubernetes-sigs/prow](https://github.com/kubernetes-sigs/prow/issues/new?title=Prow%20issue:) repository.\n</details>", "role": "comment"}, {"id": "c3", "author": "dims", "timestamp": "2026-04-11T23:40:36Z", "body": "Please see:\nhttps://github.com/open-telemetry/opentelemetry-go/blob/2ce48ddbe38e2f1973e137163fe5115d5f26ae9e/sdk/resource/host_id_bsd.go#L4\n\nand see this:\n```\nAffected platforms (per build tag in host_id_bsd.go:4): DragonFly BSD, FreeBSD, NetBSD, OpenBSD, Solaris.\n```\n\nand see this:\nhttps://github.com/kubernetes/kubernetes/blob/master/CHANGELOG/CHANGELOG-1.35.md#v1353\n(we don't support or ship binaries/images for any of those platforms above)\n\nYou need a very serious discussion with your scanner vendors and PLEASE do read the CVE reports before opening up issues here. We keep a strict eye on CVEs and this one does not affect us.", "role": "comment"}], "qa_pairs": [{"qid": "kubernetes/kubernetes/issue/138329#1", "question": "Kubernetes currently vendors `go.opentelemetry.io/otel/sdk` v1.40.0, which Grype reports as affected by GHSA-hfvc-g4fc-pqhx / CVE-2026-39883 and fixed in v1.43.0. The reported issue is PATH hijacking via the BSD `kenv` command in the OpenTelemetry SDK resource detector, affecting versions `>= v1.15.0, <= v1.42.0` with severity High (7.3). Evidence from the repository:\n\n```bash\n~/kubernetes$ grep \"go.opentelemetry.io/otel/sdk\" vendor/modules.txt\n# go.opentelemetry.io/otel/sdk v1.40.0\ngo.opentelemetry.io/otel/sdk\ngo.opentelemetry.io/otel/sdk/instrumentation\ngo.opentelemetry.io/otel/sdk/internal/x\ngo.opentelemetry.io/otel/sdk/resource\ngo.opentelemetry.io/otel/sdk/trace\ngo.opentelemetry.io/otel/sdk/trace/internal/env\ngo.opentelemetry.io/otel/sdk/trace/internal/observ\ngo.opentelemetry.io/otel/sdk/trace/tracetest\n# go.opentelemetry.io/otel/sdk/metric v1.40.0\n```\n\n```bash\n~/kubernetes$ go mod why -m go.opentelemetry.io/otel/sdk\n# go.opentelemetry.io/otel/sdk\nk8s.io/kubernetes/cmd/kubelet/app\ngo.opentelemetry.io/otel/sdk/resource\n```\n\n```bash\n~/kubernetes$ grep -R \"go.opentelemetry.io/otel/sdk/resource\" -n .\ngrep: ./.git/index: binary file matches\n./cmd/kubelet/app/server.go:52: otelsdkresource \"go.opentelemetry.io/otel/sdk/resource\"\n./staging/src/k8s.io/apiserver/pkg/server/options/tracing.go:29:        \"go.opentelemetry.io/otel/sdk/resource\"\n./staging/src/k8s.io/component-base/tracing/utils.go:26:        \"go.opentelemetry.io/otel/sdk/resource\"\n./vendor/go.etcd.io/etcd/server/v3/embed/config_tracing.go:24:  \"go.opentelemetry.io/otel/sdk/resource\"\n./vendor/go.opentelemetry.io/otel/sdk/internal/x/README.md:23:[resource detectors]: https://pkg.go.dev/go.opentelemetry.io/otel/sdk/resource#Detector\n./vendor/go.opentelemetry.io/otel/sdk/resource/config.go:4:package resource // import \"go.opentelemetry.io/otel/sdk/resource\"\n./vendor/go.opentelemetry.io/otel/sdk/resource/os_unsupported.go:6:package resource // import \"go.opentelemetry.io/otel/sdk/resource\"\n./vendor/go.opentelemetry.io/otel/sdk/resource/os_windows.go:4:package resource // import \"go.opentelemetry.io/otel/sdk/resource\"\n./vendor/go.opentelemetry.io/otel/sdk/resource/env.go:4:package resource // import \"go.opentelemetry.io/otel/sdk/resource\"\n./vendor/go.opentelemetry.io/otel/sdk/resource/host_id_bsd.go:6:package resource // import \"go.opentelemetry.io/otel/sdk/resource\"\n./vendor/go.opentelemetry.io/otel/sdk/resource/README.md:3:[![PkgGoDev](https://pkg.go.dev/badge/go.opentelemetry.io/otel/sdk/resource)](ht